_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Hi, I found six different contacts for Vasco. Which one would you like to email about the 'night at the Opera' event? ", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.5, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "ambiguity", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 602, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 2950.69, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 2950.69, "prof_tok_in": 337912, "prof_tok_out": 21496, "prof_llm_calls": 18}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T12:59:50.192601", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_gjw61a", "task_desc": "Schedule a Property Tour event at the most expensive 4 bedroom property in my saved list for this Saturday from 4pm - 5pm. Add the participants of the the most recently updated Messages conversation 'Catching up with friends' as attendees (besides me). Book me a premium cab from Stora Södergatan 25, Lund to the property location (including the zip code) one hour before the property tour starts. Send each of the attendees separate Messages messages with the time and place of the tour. If a new fu", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Schedule a Property Tour event at the most expensive 4 bedroom property in my saved list for this Saturday from 4pm - 5pm. Add the participants of the\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests and start by gathering the necessary information. Let me begin with several independent lookups.\nLet me get the full save\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-tasks and start gathering information. Let me begin with several independent lookups.\nI found saved apartments but the list was truncated, and I need to identify the specific conversation. Let me search for 4-bedroom saved apartments and find the conversation titled 'Catching up with friends'.\nI need to pass integers instead of strings. Let me retry.\nThe tool expects integers. Let me try passing the values without quotes.\nThe tool harness is converting my integer arguments to strings. Let me work around this by listing all saved apartments (to filter manually) and reading the candidate conversations from the search. First, let me get the full saved apartments list and read the search-result conversations.\nThe saved list is truncated in display. Let me try `search_apartments` with only `saved_only` (boolean) to get the full saved list, and read the candidate conversations from the earlier search.\nThe saved list is truncated and the `search_apartments` int/bool parameters fail type checks through this harness. Let me re-fetch the full saved list and read more candidate conversations to identify the one titled \"Catching up with friends\".\nNone of these are titled \"Catching up with friends\" yet. Let me read the remaining candidate conversations and also try to get the full apartment catalog (the saved list is truncated).\nThe saved and full apartment lists are being truncated in display, and the `search_apartments` int/bool filters are being rejected by the harness type-checker. Let me test whether lowercase boolean/int values work, and also test a zip-code search (smaller result sets avoid truncation).\nThe `number_of_bedrooms` int filter is rejected by the harness, but zip_code searches work and return full (untruncated) results. Let me enumerate saved apartments by searching each known saved zip code. Known saved zips so far: 252 23, 753 31, 553 22, 223 61, 754 50, 211 18.\nI now have a more complete saved list via zip searches, but the saved list was truncated (showing at least 5 entries, cut off mid-5th). I've found 9 saved apartments so far, but there may be more in un-searched zip codes. Since `list_saved_apartments` truncates and the int/bool filters fail, let me enumerate ALL apartments by property type (search returns full, untruncated results) to discover every zip code and saved status.\nThe results truncate at ~5 entries, but zip-code searches return complete (small) results. I've discovered many zip codes. Let me search all known zip codes to find every saved apartment and its bedroom count. I'll batch them.\nI'm building a complete picture. The saved list was truncated, so let me get a clean, untruncated list of ALL saved apartments by filtering with `saved_only=true` per property type (string filters work). This will let me find every saved 4-bedroom property.\nThe harness rejects string booleans/ints, so I must rely on zip-code and location searches. I've found 12 saved apartments so far, including one 4-bedroom: **Lund Luxury Living** (4br, 2200, saved). But the property-type searches truncated, so there may be more apartments in undiscovered zip codes. Let me search by city location to discover all zip codes and ensure I find every saved 4-bedroom property.\nThe location searches also truncate at ~5 entries, and I've discovered new zip codes. Critically, the `222 22` zip search truncated and revealed a **4-bedroom \"Lund Luxury Condo\"** (id `e29b75242b67cb75b7376e27223844bb`) whose saved status/price I don't yet know. Let me get its details and search all remaining discovered zip codes to ensure I find every saved 4-bedroom property.\nI now have a comprehensive view of the catalog. Let me compile the saved apartments and their bedroom counts:\n\n**Saved apartments found (11 total):**\n- Malmö Marina (2br, 1500), Lund Living (1br, 900), Malmö Modern (2br, 1300), **Lund Luxury Living (4br, 2200)**, Stockholm Haven (2br, 1800), Uppsala Upscale (2br, 1400), Uppsala Oasis (2br, 1200), Helsingborg Haven (3br, 1600), Jönköping Jewel (3br, 12000), Lund Centrum (3br, 2500), Göteborgs Hamn (2br, 1800)\n\nThe **only saved 4-bedroom property is Lund Luxury Living** (Klostergatan 15, Lund, 222 22, price 2200). The other 4br properties (Lund Luxury Condo, Lund Luxe) are NOT saved. So Lund Luxury Living is the target property.\n\nNow let me get the current time and find the \"Catching up with friends\" conversation.\nThe search returned 11 conversations matching the query. I need to find the one titled exactly \"Catching up with friends\" and determine which is most recently updated. Let me read these conversations to identify the correct one.\nThe search matched conversations by content (many mention \"catching up\"), but I need the conversation whose **title** is exactly \"Catching up with friends\". The `read_conversation` output doesn't show titles. Let me list recent conversations to see titles and identify the correct one.\nThe tool requires integer types. Let me try passing the values as plain numbers.\nThe tool expects integer types. Let me try passing the values as unquoted numbers.\nThe list tool rejects string-typed offset/limit. Since they have defaults, let me try calling it with no arguments.\nThe search matched 11 conversations (mostly on content like \"catching up\"). The first result, `1a4f47ce`, is the one whose content doesn't contain the phrase — it's the title match \"Catching up with friends\". Its participants are `+862162345678`, `+46734567890` (Astrid = the user), and `+46731234567`. So the attendees (besides me) are `+862162345678` and `+46731234567`.\n\nLet me confirm the apartment details/ID and get the attendees' names.\nThe saved list is truncated. I need the apartment ID for \"Lund Luxury Living\" (the only saved 4-bedroom). Let me search for it to get its exact ID and confirm details.\nI have the apartment ID: `a82c4cd615254a539deba855a1438f3e` (Lund Luxury Living, 4br, 2200, zip 222 22). Let me verify it's the only/most expensive saved 4-bedroom by searching saved apartments with 4 bedrooms.\nThe `search_apartments` tool rejects the bedroom count as a string. Let me get the full apartment catalog to reliably identify all 4-bedroom properties and cross-check which are saved.\nThe saved list and full catalog outputs are truncated in display. I need to confirm whether any other saved apartment has 4 bedrooms (and is more expensive). Let me retrieve all saved apartments via search with `saved_only`.\nThe `search_apartments` tool rejects int/bool parameters through this interface. I need to confirm whether any *other* saved apartment has 4 bedrooms and a higher price than Lund Luxury Living (2200). Let me try filtering by price (string param) to find expensive apartments, and re-pull the saved list.\nThe saved list display is truncated (it cut off mid-JSON at the 6th entry), and I haven't yet confirmed there's no *other* saved 4-bedroom apartment more expensive than Lund Luxury Living (2200). The numeric/bool filters on `search_apartments` are rejected by this interface, so I'll enumerate the catalog by splitting on a string attribute (`furnished_status`) to find all 4-bedroom apartments and check their saved status.\nI now have a clear picture of the catalog. Let me confirm my analysis:\n\n**Saved apartments** (from the saved list + cross-referencing the catalog):\n- Helsingborg Haven (3br, 1600)\n- Uppsala Studentboende (1br, 1000)\n- Jönköping Jewel (3br, 12000)\n- Lund Botaniska (2br, 2000)\n- Uppsala Oasis (2br, 1200)\n- Malmö Marina (2br, 1500, saved)\n- Lund Living (1br, 900, saved)\n- Malmö Modern (2br, 1300, saved)\n- Uppsala Upscale (2br, 1400, saved)\n- **Lund Luxury Living (4br, 2200, zip 222 22, saved)** ← the only saved 4-bedroom\n\nNo other saved apartment has 4 bedrooms, so **Lund Luxury Living** is definitively the most expensive saved 4-bedroom.\n\n**Attendees** (from \"Catching up with friends\" conversation `1a4f47ce`, excluding me = Astrid `+46734567890`):\n- Jianhua Wong `+862162345678`\n- Åsa Lindqvist `+46731234567`\n\n**This Saturday", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-8e4fcf55-b253-4826-a081-834aa43ca375", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-df17e0e3-7061-4137-8c72-3460f5a7f280"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Property Tour", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 17:00:00