{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:09:29.808562", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_4r8xq0", "task_desc": "I just ended things with my ex, the marketing manager I work with who also lives in Stockholm, and I want to cut all ties. Delete his contact, remove him from any Messages and Chats conversations we are both in, and move all emails sent to or received from him to the trash. Unsave the property located at the address we currently share, since I won't be living there anymore.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I just ended things with my ex, the marketing manager I work with who also lives in Stockholm, and I want to cut all ties. Delete his contact, remove \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by identifying the ex. He's described as a marketing manager who works with me and lives in Stockholm. Let me search both my contacts and internal co\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by understanding who the ex is. Let me gather information about the current user and search through both contact lists.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nLet me try passing the offset as a plain number.\nLet me try without the offset parameter.\nLet me search for the ex. He's a marketing manager who lives in Stockholm. Let me search both contact lists.\nThe search didn't find the ex directly. Let me look at all contacts by scrolling through them. I'll try passing offset as a number.\nThe offset parameter has a type mismatch. Let me try searching internal contacts for \"manager\" and also look at the saved apartment to identify the shared address.\nThe offset parameter is being rejected as a string. Let me try calling without the offset parameter.\nThe integer parameters are being rejected. Let me try passing them as bare numbers.\nThe integer parameters are being rejected by the framework. Let me work around this using search tools (which accept strings) to find the ex. Let me search messages and chats, and also get the full saved apartments list.\nThe search for \"a\" only returned 2 contacts, suggesting the contacts list may be small or search is limited. Let me enumerate contacts more thoroughly and look at conversations. The ex is a marketing manager in Stockholm who works with Astrid. Let me search messages/chats for \"marketing\" and enumerate contacts by different letters.\nThe ex is a marketing manager in Stockholm who works with Astrid (the user). Let me enumerate the internal contacts more thoroughly by searching common letters, and also examine conversations mentioning \"marketing\".\nThe internal contacts don't include a marketing manager in Stockholm. The ex might be in the regular Contacts. Let me enumerate the regular Contacts by searching various letters, and also examine the \"marketing\" conversations to identify the ex.\nThe contacts search returns a limited set. Let me try `get_contacts` with no offset parameter, and also search for more letters to ensure I find all contacts. Let me also examine the \"marketing\" conversations to identify the ex.\nThe contacts and internal contacts appear to share the same data, and the ex (a marketing manager in Stockholm) isn't obviously in the contact list. Let me identify the ex through the \"marketing\" conversations. Let me read several of them.\nThese are group conversations. The ex is a marketing manager in Stockholm who works with Astrid. Let me identify the participants by looking up the phone numbers, especially the one who mentioned \"our marketing team\" (+46202123456).\nAxel Lindqvist mentioned \"our marketing team\" — he's likely the marketing manager. Let me verify by searching contacts for him and checking the saved apartment (shared address). Let me also look at more conversations to confirm the ex's identity.\nI found the ex: **Axel Lindqvist** (contact_id `eabcdec881124416952bcfebbc179285`), a Marketing Manager in Stockholm whose address is \"Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm, Sweden\" — the same as Astrid's (the user's) address, confirming they share it.\n\nNow let me find the saved apartment at that shared address, and identify conversations with Axel in both Messages and Chats.\nI found the saved apartment at the shared address: **\"Stockholm Serenity\"** (apartment_id `db61fa40d1714954a5b9aee3d20941ec`) at Östermalmsgatan 12, Stockholm, 114 39 — matching Astrid's address.\n\nAxel (+46202123456) is in at least one group conversation (`d9e8aed8d70c46e3a22eea360f8328f2` \"Catch-up and Plans\") with Astrid. The second conversation (1-on-1) got truncated. Let me get the full list, find Axel in Chats, and unsave the apartment.\nThe offset needs to be an int. Let me retry, and search Chats for Axel-related conversations.\nThe offset parameter has a type issue when passed as a string. Let me try passing it as a number, and also check Chats conversations by listing recent ones.\nThe tool expects integer types. Let me pass them as numbers rather than strings.\nThe tool requires integer types. Let me try passing the values as bare numbers (without quotes).\nLet me try without the limit parameter.\nThe apartment is unsaved. Now I need to:\n1. Find the 1-on-1 Messages conversation with Axel (its ID was truncated)\n2. Explore Chats for Axel\n3. Find emails to/from Axel\n\nLet me gather these in parallel.\nNow I have key findings:\n- **Messages conversations with Axel (+46202123456):** group `d9e8aed8d70c46e3a22eea360f8328f2` (\"Catch-up and Plans\") and 1-on-1 `bd5fd1ae6f9947dda2e6631c4cde1773`.\n- **Emails:** Axel's address is `axel.lindqvist@gaia2mail.com`. I need all emails to/from him (not other Lindqvists).\n- **Chats:** uses internal UUIDs; I couldn't find Axel by name. Let me check internal contacts and search Chats more thoroughly.\n\nLet me gather these.\nI've confirmed the key facts. Let me verify the user's identity, check the SENT folder for emails to Axel, and confirm whether Axel appears in any Chats conversations.\nThe Chats search returns many conversations because \"Astrid\"/\"marketing\" appear in message content broadly. I need to determine Axel's Chats user ID. The internal contact_id for Axel is `eabcdec881124416952bcfebbc179285` (32 hex chars). Chats uses dashed UUIDs — let me test if the dashed form maps to a Chats user, and confirm the mapping with the current user (Astrid).\nChats uses a different ID scheme than internal contacts, and \"Lindqvist\" lookup only returned Astrid. Let me verify whether Axel exists in Chats at all.\nAxel has no Chats account (no user ID found), so there are no Chats conversations to remove him from. Now let me confirm the Messages conversations and read the 1-on-1 conversation to verify Axel's participation before removing him.\nBoth Messages conversations include Axel (+46202123456). Now I'll execute all the actions. Axel has no Chats account, so there are no Chats conversations to handle. Let me perform the deletions/removals in parallel:\n\n- Delete Axel's personal contact\n- Remove Axel from both Messages conversations\n- Move both emails (INBOX from Axel, SENT to Axel) to TRASH\nAll actions succeeded. Let me do a final verification of the state — confirm the shared apartment is no longer saved and the emails are in TRASH.\nAll verifications pass: Axel's contact is deleted, both emails are in TRASH, and the saved-apartments list no longer contains the shared Östermalmsgatan 12 apartment. Let me do one final confirmation that the shared apartment is unsaved.\nThe `saved_only` parameter requires a boolean type. The saved-apartments list I retrieved earlier already confirmed Östermalmsgatan 12 is no longer in favorites. Let me do a final direct check by searching all apartments at that location to confirm its saved status.\nAll sub-tasks are complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n**1. Identified your ex:** Axel Lindqvist — Marketing Manager, lives in Stockholm, internal work contact (the only contact matching all three criteria).\n\n**2. Deleted his contact** — removed from your personal contacts (confirmed: search now returns nothing).\n\n**3. Removed him from Messages conversations** — he was a participant in two conversations (the 1-on-1 with you, and a group chat with Åsa). I removed him from both.\n\n**4. Chats conversations** — Axel has no Chats account (no user exists for him), so there were no Chats conversations to clean up.\n\n**5. Moved all emails to/from him to TRASH** — the email he sent you (INBOX) and the one you sent him (SENT) are both now in TRASH.\n\n**6. Unsaved the shared property** — the apartment at Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm (\"Stockholm Serenity\") is now `saved: false`, confirming it's removed from your favorites.\n\nAll ties with Axel have been cut.\nI've delivered the final summary to the user. All parts of the task are complete and verified:\n\n1. **Contact deleted** — Axel Lindqvist removed from personal contacts.\n2. **Messages conversations** — removed him from both shared conversations (1-on-1 and group with Åsa).\n3. **Chats conversations** —", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2a831ac0-6c73-4ab7-abb4-dca91d2ce09c", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-bd5021a2-d4ab-458a-b76f-a36fc820164a"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Contacts", "function": "delete_contact", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "contact_id", "value": "eabcdec881124416952bcfebbc179285", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-97ccce4c-cbe1-4399-aba2-8b4988566350", "dependencies": ["Eve