{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:15:07.593463", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_4o5b3h", "task_desc": "Send a Messages message to Axel in my one-on-one conversation with him asking if he still wants to meet for coffee as I haven't received a calendar invite from him yet, and invite him to join me on this Friday at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop located at Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm. Set up the event in my calendar for an hour on that day and name it \"Coffee Break with Axel\". Book a default cab to pick me up 30 minutes ahead of our coffee break from Home to the Coffee Shop. Let me know when y", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Send a Messages message to Axel in my one-on-one conversation with him asking if he still wants to meet for coffee as I haven't received a calendar in\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: the current date/time, Axel's contact info for Messages, and my calendar availability for Friday.\nI have what I \nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by gathering the key information I need: the current date/time, Axel's contact details, and my existing conversation with him.\nCurrent date is Tuesday, 2024-10-15. So \"this Friday\" is 2024-10-18. Let me find my one-on-one conversation with Axel (phone +46202123456) and check my current user details.\nThe current user is Astrid (+46734567890). The first conversation is a group (3 people). The second one (bd5fd1ae6f9947dda2e6631c4cde1773) appears to be the one-on-one with Axel (+46202123456) and Astrid. Let me read it to confirm.\nThe tool is rejecting string-typed integer arguments. Let me try calling with just the conversation_id.\nThis is the one-on-one conversation between Axel (+46202123456) and me (Astrid). Now I'll complete the 3 tasks. They're independent, so I'll do them together:\n\n1. Send the message to Axel\n2. Create the calendar event (Friday 2024-10-18, 14:00–15:00)\n3. Book the default cab (pickup 13:30, 30 min before, Home → Coffee Shop)\nAll three tasks are complete. Let me report back to you and then monitor for any follow-up messages (e.g., Axel's reply about availability, or event invites from others).\nNew messages arrived. One is from Axel (the critical one), and two are in other conversations. Let me read all three to determine how to handle them.\nKey findings:\n- **Axel** (our one-on-one): He's NOT available Friday, but is available **Monday or Tuesday at 2:00pm**. This triggers the reschedule clause.\n- **Beshoy** (c70dd0c5...): Invites me to coffee next Wednesday — an event invite from someone else → **ignore** per instructions.\n- **Nomsa** (ca0fc7c4...): Invites me to an anniversary gathering Friday — an event invite from someone else → **ignore** per instructions.\n\nI need to reschedule to the earliest day we're both available. Axel offered Monday (2024-10-21) or Tuesday (2024-10-22) at 2pm. Let me verify my own availability on Monday before committing.\nMy availability analysis:\n- **Monday 2024-10-21 at 2pm**: FREE (only Content Creation 10–12 and Yoga 18–19) ✓\n- **Tuesday 2024-10-22 at 2pm**: CONFLICT (Brand Partnership Meeting 14:00–16:00) ✗\n\nSo the earliest day we're both available is **Monday, 2024-10-21 at 2:00pm**. I'll reschedule: delete the Friday event, cancel the Friday cab, create the Monday event, book the Monday cab, and reply to Axel confirming.\nAll reschedule steps are complete. Let me report back to you.\nThe task is fully complete. Here's a summary of everything accomplished:\n\n**Initial 3 tasks (done):**\n1. ✅ Sent a Messages message to Axel in our one-on-one conversation asking if he still wants to meet for coffee (noting I hadn't received his calendar invite) and inviting him to Friday at 2:00pm at the Coffee Shop, Kungsholmsgatan 10, 112 27 Stockholm.\n2. ✅ Created the \"Coffee Break with Axel\" calendar event for Friday 2024-10-18, 14:00–15:00.\n3. ✅ Booked a Default cab for pickup at 13:30 (30 min before) from Home to the Coffee Shop.\n\n**Follow-up handling (done):**\n- Axel replied he's unavailable Friday but free **Monday or Tuesday at 2pm**. I checked my calendar: Tuesday had a conflict (Brand Partnership Meeting 14:00–16:00), so **Monday 2024-10-21** was the earliest day we're both available.\n- Deleted the Friday event, cancelled the Friday cab, created the Monday event (14:00–15:00), rebooked the Monday cab (pickup 13:30), and replied to Axel confirming Monday.\n- Ignored the event-invite messages from Beshoy (coffee next Wednesday) and Nomsa (anniversary gathering Friday), leaving them for you to reply to later.\n\nEverything requested has been completed.\nNo new follow-up message arrived during the wait window. Everything from the task remains complete:\n\n- ✅ Message sent to Axel (one-on-one) about coffee\n- ✅ Calendar event \"Coffee Break with Axel\" set for **Monday, 2024-10-21, 14:00–15:00** (rescheduled from Friday since Axel was unavailable and Tuesday had a conflict)\n- ✅ Default cab rebooked for pickup at 13:30 from Home to the Coffee Shop\n- ✅ Replied to Axel confirming the new Monday date\n- ✅ Ignored the event-invite messages from Beshoy and Nomsa (left for you to reply to later)\n\nThe task is fully handled. If a new message comes in later, I'll be ready to act on it.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a2da3f6f-4d4e-4100-9db7-c9398d589afc", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-20c3836c-4d47-445c-b1a3-94851d8e8a80"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46202123456", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Axel, still up for coffee? Haven't received a cale