{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:15:23.940594", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_3ixhl6", "task_desc": "Cancel all scheduled events tagged as work at the Home Office starting from tomorrow through October 23rd, and order the same amount of the soft velour HANSA Snuggles The Bear Plush as the number of canceled events as this particular size and color has a sentimental value for us. If there is anything unclear, ping me so I can help.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Cancel all scheduled events tagged as work at the Home Office starting from tomorrow through October 23rd, and order the same amount of the soft velou\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by finding the work-tagged events and events at the Home Office. Let me gather this information.\nThe tag search was case-sensitive. The events have t\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by finding the work-tagged events and events at the Home Office. Let me gather this information.\nThe tag search was case-sensitive. The events have tag \"Work\" (capital W). Let me get all Work-tagged events and the events in the date range (tomorrow Oct 16 through Oct 23).\nThe limit needs to be an integer. Let me retry the date range query.\nLet me try without the limit parameter to use defaults.\nThe result is paginated (default 10 events). I need to get all events in the range. Let me paginate. The limit/offset need integer types.\nThe offset/limit parameters need integer types. Let me try passing them as numbers without quotes.\nThe offset/limit parameters are being rejected (the framework passes them as strings but the function requires integers). I'll work around this by querying smaller date windows so each returns ≤10 events. Let me split Oct 16–23 into 2-day windows.\nThe Oct 16–17 window returned a truncated result (more than 10 events). Let me split into single days to capture all events.\nI now have all events in the Oct 16–23 range. Let me identify the Work-tagged events at the Home Office:\n\n**Work + Home Office events to cancel (8 total):**\n1. Oct 16 — Content Creation Session (7491df4dfb5d4586b3d43c0f4f9e81d5)\n2. Oct 16 — Social Media Management (15a8031c0f1e4e6c867b93b08a5d365b)\n3. Oct 17 — Content Creation Session (2c50e300723342fd890a082b5b19cbba)\n4. Oct 17 — Social Media Management (06551b52bea4471a87591728dfb818ab)\n5. Oct 18 — Content Creation Session (1b1df251b5044fab93d395277aff298a)\n6. Oct 20 — Content Creation Session (845a95a84b70414385a357118559ba0a)\n7. Oct 21 — Content Creation Session (8822dd753a8e4728abe46cbd63977d20)\n8. Oct 23 — Social Media Management (da2a225c7b9c4a9fb257699bfe065f13)\n\n(Note: Brand Partnership Meetings are Work but at \"Zoom Meeting\", not Home Office, so excluded.)\n\nLet me delete these 8 events and search for the plush product in parallel.\nAll 8 Work-tagged events at the Home Office (Oct 16–23) have been canceled. \n\nNow, for the plush order: I found the **HANSA Snuggles The Bear Plush**, but there are **three** \"Soft Velour\" variants with different sizes/colors, and the task references \"this particular size and color\" without specifying which:\n\n- Small, Soft Velour, Brown — $140.69\n- Medium, Soft Velour, Brown — $160.99\n- Small, Soft Velour, Gray — $150.99\n\nSince the number of canceled events is **8**, I'd order 8 of whichever variant you mean. This is the one point that's unclear, so I'll ping you to confirm before placing the order.\nI've completed the calendar cancellation and pinged you for clarification on the plush variant. Let me wait for your response.\nNo response yet. Let me check for any unread messages from you.\nI've completed the calendar cancellations and pinged you for the one clarification needed (which Soft Velour size/color variant to order). I'll wait a bit longer for your reply.\nStill no reply. I'll continue waiting for your clarification on the plush variant.\nI've completed everything I can without your input. Here's the status:\n\n**✅ Calendar — Done:** Canceled all 8 Work-tagged events at the Home Office from Oct 16 through Oct 23 (tomorrow through Oct 23):\n- Oct 16: Content Creation Session, Social Media Management\n- Oct 17: Content Creation Session, Social Media Management\n- Oct 18: Content Creation Session\n- Oct 20: Content Creation Session\n- Oct 21: Content Creation Session\n- Oct 23: Social Media Management\n\n(Work-tagged \"Brand Partnership Meeting\" events in that range are at \"Zoom Meeting\", not the Home Office, so I left them intact.)\n\n**⏳ Plush order — Awaiting your clarification:** The HANSA Snuggles The Bear Plush has three \"Soft Velour\" variants, and you referenced \"this particular size and color\" without specifying which. I need you to confirm which one so I can order exactly 8 (matching the 8 canceled events):\n1. Small, Soft Velour, Brown — $140.69\n2. Medium, Soft Velour, Brown — $160.99\n3. Small, Soft Velour, Gray — $150.99\n\nJust let me know the size and color and I'll place the order right away.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ce527ac1-f071-4b77-8dff-024c55aeafc4", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-2f630f35-e68d-4c45-ad6c-85f95dc1bd5d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "15a8031c0f1e4e6c867b93b08a5d365b", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f1ec1e47-753f-47a4-ad07-5594971ae2f9", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-2f630f35-e68d-4c45-ad6c-85f95dc1bd5d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"ac