{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:15:31.486209", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_22_52pwi3", "task_desc": "Tell me only the name of the youngest person I have emailed this month who is not in any of my Messages conversations but is in at least one in Chats. If there is a tie, choose the one based on first name in alphabetical order.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Tell me only the name of the youngest person I have emailed this month who is not in any of my Messages conversations but is in at least one in Chats.\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll work through this step by step. Let me start by gathering the data I need: emails sent this month, my Messages conversations, and my Chats conversations.\nL\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll work through this step by step. Let me start by understanding the time context and gathering the data I need.\nThe current time is 2024-10-15, so \"this month\" is October 2024. Let me list my sent emails.\nThe parameters need to be integers. Let me retry.\nThe tool expects integer types. Let me try passing the values as plain numbers.\nLet me try with just the folder name and no offset/limit.\nThe list returned some emails. Let me get the full list of sent emails. The offset/limit parameters are causing type issues, but the call without them worked. Let me try to paginate to see all sent emails.\nThe offset/limit parameters are being rejected. Let me try `get_email_by_index` to enumerate sent emails instead.\nThe integer parameters are being rejected by the framework. The `list_emails` call with only `folder_name` worked, so let me use that and see the full default response.\nThe `list_emails` with offset/limit fails due to a type coercion issue, but the call with only `folder_name` works (returning a default page). Let me use `search_emails` (which only takes string params) to enumerate sent emails more thoroughly. Let me search with common terms.\nThe search returns 2 emails for both queries. Let me search with different terms to ensure I capture all sent emails this month.\nThe search consistently returns the same 2 emails. Let me verify whether there are more sent emails by searching for terms that would NOT appear in these two wine emails (to test if search covers all emails or has a fixed limit).\nThe search consistently returns the same 2 emails, and \"invoice\"/\"zzzzz\" return nothing. Let me do a few more broad searches to confirm there are only 2 sent emails this month (and check the timestamps are within October 2024).\nAll searches consistently return the same 2 sent emails, both from October 2024 (timestamp ~2024-10-12). The two recipients are:\n1. **augustin.moreno-sanchez@unm.edu** — Professor Moreno-Sánchez\n2. **mehmetozdemir65@gaia2mail.com** — Mr. Özdemir\n\nNow I need to find these people's ages and check their presence in Messages vs Chats. Let me search contacts for both.\nI found both contacts:\n- **Augustín Moreno-Sánchez**, age 61, phone +15051234567\n- **Mehmet Özdemir**, age 65, phone +902125558236\n\nNow I need to check their presence in Messages (phone-based) and Chats (internal ID-based). Let me check Messages conversations by participant for both phone numbers, and Chats conversations using their contact IDs.\nInteresting. Neither contact shows up in Chats by their contact_id, and Mehmet IS in Messages. But the Chats tool uses *internal* user IDs that may differ from the contact_id. Let me look up the correct Chats user IDs by name and search Chats directly.\nKey findings:\n- **Augustín Moreno-Sánchez**: Chats internal ID `b9b3a04d-...`, NOT in Messages (empty), Chats search for \"Moreno\" returned a conversation. Age 61.\n- **Mehmet Özdemir**: NO Chats user ID (empty lookup), NOT in Chats (empty search), but IS in Messages. Age 65.\n\nSo Mehmet is disqualified (he's in Messages, not in Chats). Augustín appears to qualify. Let me confirm Augustín is actually a participant in a Chats conversation.\nI now have all the information needed. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Sent emails this month (October 2024)** — only 2 recipients found:\n1. **Augustín Moreno-Sánchez** (age 61) — email to augustin.moreno-sanchez@unm.edu\n2. **Mehmet Özdemir** (age 65) — email to mehmetozdemir65@gaia2mail.com\n\n**Checking the conditions:**\n\n| Person | Emailed this month | In Messages? | In Chats? | Qualifies? |\n|--------|-------------------|--------------|-----------|------------|\n| Augustín Moreno-Sánchez | ✅ | ❌ (no conversations) | ✅ (in \"Augustín Moreno-Sánchez\" chat) | ✅ |\n| Mehmet Özdemir | ✅ | ✅ (in \"Wine and Music\" group) | ❌ (no Chats ID/conversations) | ❌ |\n\nOnly **Augustín Moreno-Sánchez** satisfies all three conditions (emailed this month, NOT in any Messages conversation, but in at least one Chats conversation). There is no tie.\nAugustín Moreno-Sánchez", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-11c51de6-cc8d-4fdc-920a-40f82f1cf219", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9eefb27a-e169-47e6-938e-ebc95157d849"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Augustín Moreno-Sánchez", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "search", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 602, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 2917.05, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 2917.05, "prof_tok_in": 344005, "prof_tok_out": 12109, "prof_llm_calls": 18}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:17:26.676713", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_fk7puz", "task_desc": "Send an email to Joana Silva saying something urgent came up and I need to meet her today at 1 PM for 15 minutes. Add that to my calendar and name it “Talk with Joana”. Please tell me when you’ve scheduled the event and sent the email. If she can’t make it, reschedule the event for earliest time that she suggests, as long as I don’t have any other meetings at the same time, and reply to let her know.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Send an email to Joana Silva saying something urgent came up and I need to meet her today at 1 PM for 15 minutes. Add that to my calendar and name it \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding Joana Silva's contact details, checking today's calendar, and confirming the current time.\nI found Joana\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding Joana Silva's contact details, checking today's calendar, and confirming the current time.\nI found Joana Silva's email (joana.silva@gaia2mail.com). Today's calendar shows the 1 PM–1:15 PM slot is free (only Photoshoot 9–12, Networking 18–20, Self-Care 20–21). Let me send the email and add the calendar event.\nThe calendar event was created. The email failed because recipients must be a list. Let me retry.\nThe email was sent and I see Joana has replied. Let me read her reply to check if she can make it at 1 PM or suggests another time.\nThat's an older email. Let me check the inbox for the most recent email from Joana (her reply to my urgent request).\nThe tool expects integer types. Let me pass them as integers.\nLet me try listing emails without the offset/limit parameters, or search for the reply content.\nJoana replied: **\"Sorry, I can't make it. I can do 1:45 PM or 6 PM today. What do you prefer?\"**\n\nLet me check her suggestions against my calendar:\n- **1:45 PM** (1:45–2:00 PM): Free ✓\n- **6 PM** (6:00–6:15 PM): Conflicts with Networking Event (18:00–20:00) ✗\n\nThe earliest time she suggests that doesn't conflict is **1:45 PM**. I'll reschedule the event and reply to let her know.\nAll actions are complete. Here's the summary:\nThe task is fully complete. I've:\n\n1. ✅ Sent the email to Joana Silva about the urgent 1 PM meeting\n2. ✅ Added the \"Talk with Joana\" calendar event\n3. ✅ Read Joana's reply (she couldn't make 1 PM, suggested 1:45 PM or 6 PM)\n4. ✅ Checked the calendar — 6 PM conflicted with the Networking Event, so rescheduled to the earliest available option (1:45 PM)\n5. ✅ Replied to Joana confirming 1:45 PM\n\nI'll wait to see if you have any follow-up changes.\nNo further notifications arrived. The task is fully complete:\n\n- 📧 **Email sent** to Joana Silva about the urgent meeting\n- 📅 **\"Talk with Joana\"** calendar event created, then rescheduled to **1:45–2:00 PM today** (since 6 PM conflicted with your Networking Event)\n- 💬 **Reply sent** to Joana confirming 1:45 PM\n\nEverything is done. Let me know if you need any adjustments.\nNo new follow-up message arrived. The task remains fully complete:\n\n- 📧 **Email sent** to Joana Silva (joana.silva@gaia2mail.com) about the urgent meeting\n- 📅 **\"Talk with Joana\"** calendar event created, then rescheduled to **1:45–2:00 PM today** (since 6 PM conflicted with your Networking Event)\n- 💬 **Reply sent** to Joana confirming 1:45 PM\n\nEverything requested has been handled. Let me know if you need any further changes.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2984866f-3766-4daf-a6ea-c774b9e06fc7", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-58c19a37-e8d1-4258-8667-bd0fd5f52c56"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"joana.silva@gaia2mail.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Urgent Meeting Request", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Something urgent came up and I need to meet you today at 1 PM for 15 minutes.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-fde9c444-5bf1-4720-87ff-3776b10c6bb2", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-58c19a37-e8d1-4258-8667-bd0fd5f52c56"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Talk with Joana", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 13:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 13:15:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5fde7c61-d288-4a81-84f2-7e115eb77d33", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-fde9c444-5bf1-4720-87ff-3776b10c6bb2", "OracleEvent-AGENT-2984866f-3766-4daf-a6ea-c774b9e06fc7"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "The event has been scheduled and the email has been sent.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975843.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-efe3d5e7-1d5f-4774-82f6-6ac4ac9f67fb", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "{{OracleEvent-AGENT-fde9c444-5bf1-4720-87ff-3776b10c6bb2}}", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975843.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-39a66ae5-1e78-41cb-ae2e-30f5756fce81", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Talk with Joana", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 13:45:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975843.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-390743fb-131a-4b2e-b5c9-aee4476adf7a", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-cacebcb0-7ca1-4b15-b8b2-4e91ae9b7692}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "I have rescheduled the meeting for today at 1:45 PM", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.8333333333333334, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 514, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.2, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 2827.41, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 2827.41, "prof_tok_in": 241946, "prof_tok_out": 3467, "prof_llm_calls": 14}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:17:35.495224", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_2on5mg", "task_desc": "I have a networking event later today with two attendees. Can you book me a Default cab from the Malmo airport at 230 32 Malmö-Sturup to Norra Vallgatan 60, 211 22 Malmö at 5:30pm today? Also, check with both attendees of my networking event to see if they can still make it and if they want to get a taxi from the airport to the venue via sending separate emails. Let me know when you've scheduled the cab and sent the emails. If both attendees can make it, cancel the existing cab, and create the s", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I have a networking event later today with two attendees. Can you book me a Default cab from the Malmo airport at 230 32 Malmö-Sturup to Norra Vallgat\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by finding the networking event to identify the attendees, and simultaneously book the Default cab.\nI found the networking event with attendees **Ast\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by finding the networking event and its attendees, and simultaneously book the Default cab since that's needed regardless of the attendees' responses.\nI found today's networking event (event_id `541223c32f0b40edb923a728928ace2c`) with two attendees: **Astrid Mikkelsen** and **Beshoy Gadallah**. The Default cab is booked (ride_id `4e3d1297833d3aa85facd3dd11a81ea4`).\n\nNow I need to find the attendees' email addresses and the current user's details to send the emails.\nI have both attendees' emails and the user's details. The Default cab is booked. Now let me send separate emails to both attendees asking if they can still make it and if they want a taxi from the airport to the venue.\nThe recipients parameter needs to be a list. Let me retry with list format.\nBoth emails are sent. Let me inform the user that the cab is booked and the emails are sent, then wait for the attendees' responses.\nNow I'll wait for the attendees' responses.\nNo new notifications from the wait, but earlier I saw notifications about emails received from both attendees. Let me check the inbox for their replies.\nBoth attendees confirmed they can make it:\n- **Astrid Mikkelsen**: \"Sure thing! I am still attending, count me in for the taxi, too!\"\n- **Beshoy Gadallah**: \"Yes, I can still make it and I'll grab a taxi with you guys as planned.\"\n\nSince both can attend, I need to cancel the existing Default cab and book a Premium one. Let me cancel the current ride.\nThe Default cab is cancelled. Now let me book the same journey with Premium service.\nThe Premium cab is booked (ride_id `79245e0d4f85d5715658687d08c9c032`). Now I'll email both attendees separately, telling them I'll see them later and including the new cab details.\nAll steps are complete. Let me summarize the final outcome for the user.\nThe task is fully complete. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n**Initial actions:**\n1. ✅ Booked a Default cab from Malmo airport (230 32 Malmö-Sturup) to Norra Vallgatan 60, 211 22 Malmö at 5:30pm today.\n2. ✅ Sent separate emails to both networking event attendees (Astrid Mikkelsen and Beshoy Gadallah) asking if they could still make it and whether they wanted to share a taxi from the airport to the venue.\n\n**Attendee responses:** Both confirmed they can make it and want to share the taxi.\n\n**Follow-up actions (both can attend → upgrade to Premium):**\n3. ✅ Cancelled the original Default cab.\n4. ✅ Booked a new **Premium** cab for the same journey (ride_id `79245e0d4f85d5715658687d08c9c032`, ~22 min, ~30.68, pickup 5:30pm).\n5. ✅ Sent separate \"see you later\" emails to both attendees, each including the new Premium cab details.\n\nAll sub-requests have been satisfied.\nNo new follow-up message arrived during the wait. The task has been fully completed:\n\n- ✅ Default cab booked, then cancelled after both attendees confirmed attendance\n- ✅ Premium cab booked for the same journey (ride_id `79245e0d4f85d5715658687d08c9c032`)\n- ✅ Separate initial emails sent to both attendees (Astrid Mikkelsen & Beshoy Gadallah) checking attendance/taxi\n- ✅ Both confirmed they can attend\n- ✅ Separate follow-up emails sent to both attendees with the new Premium cab details\n\nThe task is complete and no further action is required.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f916c9ac-e63e-4919-b932-5e395bb1acc2", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9ba0aa71-9148-4c90-b22b-5dc2073b3536"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"astrid.mikkelsen@gaia2mail.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Confirmation for Networking Event Today", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hi Astrid, \nCan you still make it to the networking event today? Would you like to get a taxi from the Malmo airport to the venue? \nBest, \nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-4fb26438-2533-4c8b-9e83-22b7c0bc70b8", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9ba0aa71-9148-4c90-b22b-5dc2073b3536"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"beshoy.gadallah@coptic-church.dk\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Confirmation for Networking Event Today", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": 