{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:19:01.795215", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_xtv9xb", "task_desc": "I'm excited to say the sports coach in my contacts is now officially my girlfriend, so I need to message everyone else I was seeing. Create a group chat with all my Stockholm contacts 35 or younger (except my girlfriend) on Messages and tell them I'm in a committed relationship now so they shouldn't message anymore. Let me know once the message is sent. Watch for replies for 4 minutes after notifying me - if anyone responds, immediately send a private Messages message to this person saying this ", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I'm excited to say the sports coach in my contacts is now officially my girlfriend, so I need to message everyone else I was seeing. Create a group ch\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by exploring the contacts to find the sports coach (girlfriend) and the Stockholm contacts 35 or younger.\nLet me get the contacts list with proper pa\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by exploring the contacts to find the sports coach (girlfriend) and the Stockholm contacts 35 or younger.\nThe first contact is the user (Astrid). Let me get more contacts to find the sports coach and Stockholm contacts.\nLet me try searching for the sports coach directly.\nLet me search for Stockholm contacts and try different offset values.\nThe offset parameter seems to have a type issue. Let me try the InternalContacts tool and also retry the offset.\nThe offset parameter needs to be an integer. Let me try passing it as a number.\nLet me try passing offset as a numeric value without quotes.\nThe offset parameter is being type-coerced to a string. Let me try a different approach to enumerate contacts via search.\nLet me try calling get_contacts without the offset parameter.\nThe offset parameter has a type conflict. Let me enumerate contacts via search using different letters.\nThe search returns a limited view. Let me search for the sports coach and other contacts more systematically.\nThe search only matches name/phone/email, not city. I need to enumerate all contacts. Let me search systematically across letters to find everyone.\nThe search matches only name/phone/email and returns a limited set. Let me continue enumerating contacts by searching remaining letters to build a complete picture.\nThe search returns a limited, relevance-ranked subset and doesn't filter by city. I need the full contact list. The `get_contacts` offset had a type conflict — let me try different offset values to paginate.\nThe offset must be an integer. Let me retry with proper integer values.\nThe framework is passing offset as a string. Let me try calling without the offset parameter to use the default.\nThe `get_contacts` offset has a type-coercion issue (schema says string but implementation wants int). Let me try the InternalContacts variant and also attempt offset pagination again, since I need the full list to find the sports coach and all Stockholm contacts.\nBoth contact lists return only the first 2 contacts due to a view limit, and the `offset` parameter has a type-coercion bug. Let me try passing offset as a numeric value to paginate.\nThe `offset` parameter is broken (string/int coercion). I'll rely on `search_contacts` with targeted queries. First, let me find the sports coach (girlfriend) and any Stockholm contacts by searching relevant terms.\nThe `offset` parameter is broken (type coercion), and `search_contacts` only matches name/phone/email and returns a limited, partly-defaulted window. I'll gather full details on the contacts I've discovered via `get_contact` (which shows job/city/age), and search for the remaining names. Let me fetch details for all known contact IDs.\nI now have details on 14 contacts. Key findings so far:\n- **Astrid Lundqvist** (0d1b1d...) — `is_user: true` → this is the **current user** (age 23, Stockholm).\n- **Åke Lundqvist** (82899f...) — age 45, Stockholm (too old, excluded).\n- All others are in Shanghai/Beijing/Paris/Porto/Lisbon/UK — not Stockholm.\n\nI haven't found the sports coach (girlfriend) or other Stockholm contacts ≤35 yet. The `offset` pagination is broken, so I must enumerate via search. Let me test whether `search_contacts` is windowed by searching common vowels (which should match nearly all names).\nThe `search_contacts` is also windowed (returns only the first few matches in list order), and `get_contacts` offset is broken. However, search matches phone/email too. Let me try: (1) passing `offset` as a numeric value to bypass the type bug, and (2) searching by Swedish phone code `+46` and email domain to surface Stockholm/Swedish contacts.\nThe `+46` search surfaced a new contact: **Göran Lundström** (age 66). The search is windowed, so I can't fully enumerate via it. The girlfriend (sports coach) isn't appearing, and I need to find the Stockholm contacts ≤35 the user was \"seeing.\" Let me look at the Messages conversations to identify who the user was dating, and get Göran's details.\nGöran is in Gothenburg (age 66) — not relevant. The `offset` type bug affects Messages too. Let me retry passing numeric values (not strings) for offset/limit, and read the conversations that matched \"coach\".\nGöran is in Gothenburg (age 66) — not relevant. The `offset` bug blocks `list_recent_conversations`, but `read_conversation` and `search` work. The \"coach\" search returned 10 conversations — let me read the remaining ones to find the sports coach (girlfriend) and the romantic context, and also search contacts for \"coach\".\nKey findings from the conversations:\n- **Åsa** (`+46731234567`) is in **Stockholm** and is called \"a great coach\" (handball/sports) — this is the **sports coach girlfriend**.\n- **Kasper** (`+4531723456`) is a ski coach but in **Denmark** (not Stockholm).\n- The search for `+46` revealed **Göran** (Gothenburg, age 66) — a 15th contact NOT in the first 14, confirming there are more contacts I can't reach via the broken `offset`.\n\nI must enumerate all contacts. The `offset` type bug blocks pagination. Let me try passing `offset` as a numeric value (not string) to bypass it, and look up Åsa's contact.\nThe \"Åsa\" search returned 4 Åsas, but none have phone `+46731234567` (the coach/girlfriend in messages). The search is windowed, so the girlfriend's contact may be hidden. Let me search her phone directly, get Åsa Lindgren's details, and test whether any non-zero offset works.\nI found the girlfriend: **Åsa Lindqvist** (contact `b87d40b5953d4872af385577aa14dead`, age 31, Stockholm, Sports Coach, phone `+46731234567`) — to be excluded.\n\nCritical issue: `get_contacts` only returns the first 14 (windowed) and `offset` is broken, so I can't paginate. The search is also windowed (the \"Åsa\" search hid Lindqvist). I've found these Stockholm contacts so far, but need to find ALL Stockholm contacts ≤35. Let me run many targeted searches to surface the rest.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-82242a99-c57d-4a86-877d-e6403032432d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-ff25bf8c-4199-44d9-b834-418eb56fc9df"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "create_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_ids", "value": "[\"+46700234567\",\"+46701234537\",\"+46202123456\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "title", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-9131cf4a-666f-457f-b355-22cf