 "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1c620f4c-5315-40bd-885d-a8d18225cfb8", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-4bdfee10-5e99-4f0e-91e3-dd7f11e4e44c"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+46700234567", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "This is seriously goodbye", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-b010ea2e-903e-4db8-955e-0adbb9770c6d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-4bdfee10-5e99-4f0e-91e3-dd7f11e4e44c"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Contacts", "function": "delete_contact", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "contact_id", "value": "436b35306ffb4799bc8ad5f42e3f8e06", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "time", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 646, "wc_served": [1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 1, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3571.7, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3571.7, "prof_tok_in": 819096, "prof_tok_out": 56720, "prof_llm_calls": 40}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:23:06.342454", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_wezjyh", "task_desc": "I went to view all the properties that cost $1000 with my housemate Yujie Liang last week. I liked all of them, so can you please add them to my Saved Apartments list? After that, please send a message on Chats to Yujie in our most recent private conversation, asking her which properties she liked the most and would want to view again on the weekend and which ones she didn't like. Let me know when you have sent the message. If she responds within 4 minutes, immediately remove any properties she ", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I went to view all the properties that cost $1000 with my housemate Yujie Liang last week. I liked all of them, so can you please add them to my Saved\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests and work through them systematically. Let me start by gathering information about the properties and the chat conversatio\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Find all properties that cost $1000 (viewed with Yujie Liang last week)\n2. Add them to Saved Apartments list\n3. Send a Chats message to Yujie in most recent private conversation asking about preferences\n4. Notify user when message sent\n5. Handle Yujie's response within 4 minutes (remove disliked properties)\n6. Send reminders at 4 min and 4.5 min if no response\n7. If multiple liked, remove last alphabetically until one remains\n8. Set up \"Property Viewing\" calendar event Saturday 1-2pm with location and Yujie as attendee\n\nLet me start by gathering information about the properties and the chat conversation.\nLet me retry the apartment search with proper integer types and look at the chat conversations.\nThe search tool needs integer types. Let me list all apartments and find Yujie's user ID, and check the remaining conversations.\nThe search tool has a type issue, so I'll work from the full list. I can see Yujie's user ID is `4380ef87-b288-4ca2-afaa-3f0d7733f530` and the current user (Astrid) is `e7ab09f6-1fdf-420f-a28b-c67d4c34f43e`. The conversation `50bdd4012c3942f7badb35b5fc9819d1` appears to be a private conversation between them. Let me get the full apartment list and verify the private conversations with Yujie.\nI found the private conversation with Yujie: `50bdd4012c3942f7badb35b5fc9819d1` (title \"Yujie Liang\", last updated 1728128100, only 2 participants). The other Yujie conversation is a group chat.\n\nThe apartment list is truncated. I need to find ALL properties costing exactly $1000. Let me try the search with proper integer values (the earlier error was a type issue).\nThe search tool has a type-conversion issue. The apartment list appears truncated (cut off at \"Lund Living\"). Let me retry the search with bare numeric values, and also re-list all apartments to get the complete catalog.\nThe search tool has a type-conversion bug (it receives numeric args as strings). The `list_all_apartments` output is being truncated mid-object at \"Lund Living\", so there are more apartments I can't see. Let me try `search_apartments` with no numeric filters to get the complete catalog.\nThe output is consistently truncated at \"Lund Living\" (a display limit), so there are more apartments I can't see. The numeric price filter is broken (type mismatch on the server). I'll enumerate the full catalog using non-numeric filters. Let me split by property type to avoid truncation.\nThe output truncates at ~5 items, so there are more apartments than I can see. The price filter is broken server-side. I'll enumerate the full catalog by location (smaller result sets won't truncate). Let me search by each known city.\nThe location searches also truncate at ~5 items, so there are more apartments than displayed. I need to verify whether the tool returns complete data for narrow queries. Let me test with a specific zip code and name to understand the result size, and probe for more $1000 properties.\nI now understand the tool: it returns complete results for narrow queries (≤5 items), but truncates when a query matches many. The price filter is broken server-side. I'll enumerate the full catalog by city + property_type to get complete, non-truncated results. Let me start with Stockholm and Göteborg.\nThe city+type queries still truncate at ~5 items, so there are many more apartments. The price filter is broken, so I'll enumerate by price using a different approach: search by each city with a price filter via the `name` field won't work. \n\nLet me reconsider: the truncation happens at ~5 results. I'll enumerate by **city + bedrooms** (smaller buckets) to get complete lists. Let me try Stockholm with 1 bedroom.\nAll numeric filters (price, bedrooms) are broken server-side (type mismatch), and results truncate at ~5 items. I've found one $1000 property so far: **Uppsala Urban** (0d836a21c18a4e029531ac8ffc9fb3fc). I need to find any others. Let me enumerate the remaining city+type combinations and use furnished_status to dig past the truncation.\nKey insight: every `search_apartments` call returns **exactly 5 results then truncates** — there's a 5-item display limit and no pagination, plus the price filter is broken. I've found only one $1000 property so far (Uppsala Urban). \n\nBut the user said they \"went to view all the properties that cost $1000 with Yujie last week\" — the chat conversation with Yujie likely contains the actual list of properties they viewed together. Let me read that private conversation in full.\nThe offset/limit need integer types. Let me retry with integer values.\nThe tool implementation wants int but the schema passes string. Let me try calling without the offset/limit parameters.\nThis conversation is about a Shanghai trip — not property viewing, and the participants aren't Yujie Liang. I need to find the actual Yujie Liang. Let me look up her user ID and find conversations with her.\nYujie Liang = `4380ef87-b288-4ca2-afaa-3f0d7733f530`, and the other participant in that conversation is **Astrid Lundqvist** (`e7ab09f6-1fdf-420f-a28b-c67d4c34f43e`) — so the current user is Astrid. But that conversation is about a Shanghai trip, not properties. There may be a separate (property) conversation. Let me list all conversations involving Yujie and Astrid.\nYujie Liang (`4380ef87...`) and the current user is **Astrid Lundqvist** (`e7ab09f6...`). Their only **private** (2-person) conversation is `50bdd4012c3942f7badb35b5fc9819d1` (the other is a 3-person group). That's the most recent private conversation — I'll send the message there.\n\nNow, the critical issue: I must find ALL $1000 properties, but search truncates at 5 and the price filter is broken. I'll enumerate completely by city + type + furnished_status. Let me start with Stockholm, Göteborg, and Uppsala Apartments.\nI've now enumerated Stockholm, Göteborg, and Uppsala apartments/condos by furnished status. So far only **Uppsala Urban** ($1000) is confirmed. The truncation at 5 is a real obstacle. Let me try the `name` filter (exact match) to probe for any other $1000 properties, and finish Göteborg condos.\nI found another $1000 property hidden by truncation: **Göteborgs Gård** (`3f4f5d1d8e6f49b6bbb98834ad1903c1`, Göteborg, Condo, Unfurnished). Both $1000 properties share a clear signature: **Condo, Unfurnished, Ground floor, 1 bed, 1 bath**. Let me use that signature to find ALL $1000 properties efficiently (and check Apartments too, for safety).\nThe bedroom/bathroom params need int type. Let me drop those and use the signature (Condo, Unfurnished, Ground floor) plus the Apartment variant.\nThe signature search reveals MORE $1000 properties hidden by truncation: **Västerås View** (`a6b069d7531847e4ab2d641e1fa9bb60`) and **Uppsala Studentboende** (`d8f02d5d11c14e5588120a316cbafef4`). The $1000 tier is consistently: Unfurnished, Ground floor, 1 bed, 1 bath. To get complete (non-truncated) lists, I'll search per-city with Unfurnished + Ground floor.\nNow I have per-city Unfurnished+Ground floor lists. The $1000 tier is consistently **1 bed, 1 bath, Unfurnished, Ground floor**. Let me get the complete list by adding bedroom/bathroom filters (as ints) for both property types — this should return a small, complete set.\nThe `number_of_bedrooms`/`bathrooms` params reject string input, so I can't use them. The per-city lists also truncate at ~5. The cleanest complete enumeration is `max_price=1000` per city (the $1000 tier is small per city, so no truncation). Let me run that for all cities I've encountered.\nThe `max_price` param also needs a numeric type, and passing it alone errors — but my very first call passed `min_price`+`max_price` together as \"1000\" and worked. Let me mirror that exact pattern (both min and max = 1000) per city to get clean, complete $1000 lists.\nThe `min_price`/`max_price` filter is inconsistent (worked once, now errors), and searches truncate at ~5 results. The truncation-risk cities (returned exactly 5) are Göteborg, Uppsala, and Lund. Let me split those by prope", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-0b7fe640-0381-4a6e-99f9-e46b5ec6d784", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-56bec660-4259-4d21-922a-380bdaf9d8f5"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "0d836a21c18a4e029531ac8ffc9fb3fc", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5244d90a-4d77-4e48-89f3-8881b077ba69", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-56bec660-4259-4d21-922a-380bdaf9d8f5"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "3f4f5d1d8e6f49b6bbb98834ad1903c1", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-eb65b745-b4ea-4155-8428-cdb0047f6673", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-56bec660-4259-4d21-922a-380bdaf9d8f5"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "a6b069d7531847e4ab2d641e1fa9bb60", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-73ce8626-f1dd-4ba0-b37b-b78a01b14fd7", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-0b7fe640-0381-4a6e-99f9-e46b5ec6d784", "OracleEvent-AGENT-5244d90a-4d77-4e48-89f3-8881b077ba69", "OracleEvent-AGENT-eb65b745-b4ea-4155-8428-cdb0047f6673"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Chats", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "4380ef87-b288-4ca2-afaa-3f0d7733f530", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Yujie, which properties did you like the most and want to view again this weekend? And which ones didn't you like?", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975603.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d2a524e2-a1b3-4aaf-852c-9c5667e28fcb", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-73ce8626-f1dd-4ba0-b37b-b78a01b14fd7"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "f