{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:41:50.841476", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_rxo9gu", "task_desc": "For the next 3 minutes, immediately add 2 of each variant of Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder that gets added to the store and becomes available, and also add two each of ones that are already available as well to the shopping cart (you can do this now as they are already available). Checkout the cart exactly 45 seconds after the last addition of Poke Ball 3-Ring Binderalls to the cart within this 3 minute window. Then tell my Fashion Designer friend that I got him the Pokémon merchandise that he asked f", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: For the next 3 minutes, immediately add 2 of each variant of Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder that gets added to the store and becomes available, and also add \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by searching for the \"Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder\" products to see what variants are available.\nLet me try a broader search.\nI found the product \"Pokemon\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by searching for the \"Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder\" products to see what variants are available.\nLet me try a broader search.\nI found the product \"Pokemon Poke Ball 2\" 3-Ring Binder\" with two variants:\n- Variant 1 (item_id `edb4dff49ae143eba088de8e8178f23e`): $9.98, **available** (Plastic, Red, Zipper)\n- Variant 2 (item_id `ded0ca7472a04ce2aa5a195ffd672430`): $12.99, **not available** (Fabric, Blue, Velcro)\n\nLet me get the current time and add the already-available variant to the cart now.\nThe quantity needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nLet me try passing the quantity as a plain number value.\nThe quantity parameter keeps being interpreted as a string. Let me try adding without specifying quantity (default is 1) and call it twice.\nThat added 1. Let me add another to make it 2.\nI now have 2 of the available variant in the cart. Let me verify the cart state.\nI now have 2 of the available variant in the cart. The other variant is currently unavailable. \n\nNow I need to monitor for the next 3 minutes (until sim time ~1728975786) for any new variants that get added and become available. Let me wait for notifications about new products.\nNo new products yet. Let me continue monitoring.\nWe're near the end of the 3-minute window (started at 1728975606, ends ~1728975786). Let me wait a bit more to cover the full window.\nThe 3-minute window has now passed (started at 1728975606, now at 1728975805 ≈ 199 seconds). No new variants were added during this window. Let me re-check the product to confirm the state of all variants.\nNew variants have been added during the monitoring window! There are now 5 newly-available Metal variants (Copper, Black, Platinum, Rose Gold, Silver) plus the original available Plastic/Red one. The Fabric/Blue one is still unavailable.\n\nI need to add 2 of each newly-available variant to the cart immediately. Let me add them now (2 each = 10 items).\nAll 5 new Metal variants added (2 each). Let me verify the cart state.\nThe cart now contains 2 of each of the 6 available variants (Plastic/Red + 5 Metal variants). \n\nThe last additions just happened. I need to checkout exactly 45 seconds after the last addition. Let me get the current time to track this.\nThe last additions happened at ~1728975836. I need to checkout exactly 45 seconds after, at ~1728975881. Let me wait for that time.\nWe're now past 45 seconds after the last cart addition. Let me proceed to checkout the cart.\nCheckout succeeded. Let me get the order details to find the total cost.\nThe order total is **$249.86**. Now I need to find my Fashion Designer friend on Chats to send them a message. Let me look them up.\nNo match with that exact name. Let me search for the friend differently.\nLet me search the contacts for someone with the job \"Fashion Designer\".\nLet me list all contacts to find the Fashion Designer friend.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nThe contacts tool has a type conflict. Let me try a different approach — list recent Chats conversations to identify the Fashion Designer friend.\nThe offset parameter has a type conflict. Let me try the search function instead, which may not have this issue.\nThe contacts tool has a type conflict. Let me try passing offset as an integer value, and also check the current user details.\nThe contacts tool has a parameter type conflict. Let me try calling it without the offset parameter.\nThe contacts tool works without offset. Let me scroll through more contacts to find the Fashion Designer friend. I'll try passing offset as a number.\nThe offset parameter has a type conflict (schema says string but implementation wants int). Let me try passing it as a numeric value.\nThe offset parameter has a framework type conflict. Let me try passing it as a bare number instead of a string.\nThe contacts pagination has a framework type conflict. Let me find the Fashion Designer friend through the Chats conversations instead. Let me read one of the \"Fashion\" search results to identify the friend.\nThis conversation involves Astrid, Lianying, and Åke. Let me search the chats more specifically for the Fashion Designer friend.\nLet me read some of these \"designer\" conversations to find the Fashion Designer friend.\nThese conversations don't clearly identify a Fashion Designer. Let me search chats more specifically and also try to find the fashion designer friend through other means.\nLet me search the chats for \"Pokémon\" and \"Poke\" to find the conversation where the friend asked for merchandise.\nLet me read the \"Poke\" conversation that might be about the merchandise request.\nLet me search contacts for the people mentioned in conversations who might be the Fashion Designer. Akira was mentioned as helping with design.\nAkira is a Graphic Designer. Let me search for \"fashion\" in contacts to find the Fashion Designer friend.\nLet me search contacts for \"designer\" and \"Pokemon\" to find the right friend.\nLet me focus on the shopping task and also identify the Fashion Designer friend. Let me search for the product and look at fashion-related chats.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1237383c-0080-4a29-adf3-575eb0d2147f", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-ba17f84c-590e-47f1-970b-94bf7bedb719"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "edb4dff49ae143eba088de8e8178f23e", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5cdffa18-2e31-4974-bd1b-ea60a7e3beb8", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-3feb34bc-02cc-47fa-ac83-928e6ed02499"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-3feb34bc-02cc-47fa-ac83-928e6ed02499}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a22355d3-e70d-453c-9713-76b8cf1e6cfe", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-f2530dea-b008-4bea-b69d-61a35f418c42"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-f2530dea-b008-4bea-b69d-61a35f418c42}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-3407c4b8-ad3c-450d-84ed-48153a7fea76", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-a2a8de0c-8d70-4ddd-a7f3-a210f11d2374"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-a2a8de0c-8d70-4ddd-a7f3-a210f11d2374}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-bda8a7aa-46a2-4cb5-8440-62c7013904f6", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-eeac0f43-6435-49bf-aa19-48808ca49d4a"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-eeac0f43-6435-49bf-aa19-48808ca49d4a}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-c63f0535-1397-4d05-9349-1465010185e6", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-45b8d73e-3c78-40ba-b0cd-175cf0f35769"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-45b8d73e-3c78-40ba-b0cd-175cf0f35769}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1182dc2c-fcd4-4561-be6f-d5a15629b57a", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-5cdffa18-2e31-4974-bd1b-ea60a7e3beb8", "OracleEvent-AGENT-1237383c-0080-4a29-adf3-575eb0d2147f", "OracleEvent-AGENT-a22355d3-e70d-453c-9713-76b8cf1e6cfe", "OracleEvent-AGENT-3407c4b8-ad3c-450d-84ed-48153a7fea76", "OracleEvent-AGENT-bda8a7aa-46a2-4cb5-8440-62c7013904f6", "OracleEvent-AGENT-c63f0535-1397-4d05-9349-1465010185e6"], "event_relative_time": 45.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-b99ba0ef-145e-4682-ae6e-1dea6e85290d", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-1182dc2c-fcd4-4561-be6f-d5a15629b57a"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Chats", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "22a2c76b-bb6a-410e-9edb-68bab6ca9df8", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Zhaolong Liang, I got the Pokémon merchandise you asked for! Total cost is $249.86", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5e40655f-7743-4ecd-b350-ddf515f8da44", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-b99ba0ef-145e-4682-ae6e-1dea6e85290d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Total cost of the Pokémon merchandise was $249.86", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.7777777777777778, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "time", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 646, "wc_served": [1.0, 1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.05, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3410.62, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3410.62, "prof_tok_in": 730328, "prof_tok_out": 13848, "prof_llm_calls": 40}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:42:14.158912", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_97ym83", "task_desc": "Please send a message on Chats to Emil Rasmussen letting her know I’ve found a few properties for our next student accommodation and want to check them out today. If she hasn’t replied in 2 minutes after sending the message, save an unsaved furnished one-bedroom property located on the upper floors at the beginning of each 30-second interval, in order of lowest to highest price, until she replies (if there is a tie in price, sort alphabetically). If all properties have been added and she still h", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Please send a message on Chats to Emil Rasmussen letting her know I’ve found a few properties for our next student accommodation and want to check the\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by finding Emil Rasmussen's user ID in Chats, and also look at the available properties to understand what I'm working with.\nFound Emil's user ID. Le\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by finding Emil Rasmussen's user ID in Chats, and also look at the available properties to understand what I'm working with.\nFound Emil's user ID. The apartment search needs integer types. Let me retry.\nThe search function is rejecting the string type for bedrooms. Let me try passing it as a number, and if that fails, I'll search with the other filters and filter bedrooms myself.\nThe tool keeps treating the value as a string. Let me search with the other filters and filter bedrooms manually.\nThe search result was truncated. Let me get the complete list of all apartments to filter properly.\nThe results are being truncated in display. Let me get the complete set of furnished, upper-floor apartments by splitting the search on price, and also check which apartments are already saved.\nThe numeric filters (bedrooms, price) fail because the framework passes strings. I'll filter manually. The results are being truncated in display, so let me split the search by property type to get the complete list of furnished upper-floor apartments.\nThe results keep getting truncated. Let me split by saved status to get complete, smaller result sets for each property type.\nThe boolean/int filters fail due to string serialization. I'll narrow by `lease_term` (a string field) to get complete result sets. Let me split the Apartment results by lease term.\nI now have the complete 6-month Apartment list. The 1-year Apartment list is still truncated. Let me split it further by pet policy to get the complete set.\nThe \"Pets allowed\" 1-year Apartment list is still truncated at 5 entries. Let me check the \"No pets\" policy for 1-year Apartments to capture any remaining entries.\nI have the \"No pets\" 1-year Apartments (2 entries). The \"Pets allowed\" 1-year Apartment list is still truncated at 5 entries. Let me get all \"Pets allowed\" furnished upper-floor apartments (across all types/leases) to capture the remaining ones.\nThe \"Pets allowed\" set is large and still truncated. Let me split it by property type (Condo) and by location (Stockholm) to capture the remaining 1-year Apartments.\nI'm getting more entries but the display truncates at ~5 per call. I need to enumerate ALL furnished upper-floor apartments to find every 1-bedroom unsaved one. Let me search by location (string filter) for each city to get complete, smaller result sets.\nThe location searches also truncate at ~5 entries. I need complete enumeration. Let me split Stockholm and Göteborg by pet policy to get full result sets and find any 1-bedroom units.\nThe location/pet-policy searches still truncate at ~5 entries, making full enumeration tedious. Let me get the complete catalog in one call instead, then filter manually.\nThe catalog display also truncates at ~5 entries. I need to narrow to just 1-bedroom units (the only ones I need). Let me try filtering by `number_of_bedrooms` as a string, combined with the other criteria.\nThe catalog also truncates. I need to enumerate furnished upper-floor apartments per city per lease term to get complete (≤5) result sets. Let me split by city and lease term.\nI now have most cities. I still need complete enumeration for Stockholm and Göteborg (their location searches truncated). Let me split those by lease term to get full result sets and find any 1-bedroom units.\nStockholm and Göteborg 1-year sets still truncate. Let me split those by pet policy to get complete result sets and capture any 1-bedroom units.\nThe \"Pets allowed\" 1-year sets for Stockholm and Göteborg still truncate at 5. Let me split those further by property type to get complete result sets.\nThe \"Pets allowed\" + Apartment sets still truncate at 5. Let me split by price to capture the remaining units.\nThe price args need numeric types. Let me retry with int values.\nThe price filter has a type issue, but I realize I can avoid the truncation problem entirely by filtering directly on `number_of_bedrooms=1`, which will give a small, complete result set. Let me search for all furnished 1-bedroom upper-floor properties.\nThe numeric filters reject string values. Let me try passing them as unquoted numbers.\nNumeric filters are rejected (strings). I'll split the truncated \"Pets allowed\" 1-year Apartment sets by saved status to get complete enumerations.\nThe typed filters (int/bool) are all rejected by the harness, and string-only queries truncate at 5 results. The clean solution is to list the entire catalog and filter client-side. Let me do that.\nThe listing/search outputs are being truncated mid-entry (the 5th item is cut off), meaning result sets larger than ~5 items get cut at a character limit. To get complete data, I need to narrow queries to small result sets. I'll enumerate by zip code (each zip should have few apartments) combined with the furnished + upper-floors filters, covering all known zips plus the other cities.\nI now have complete data for Stockholm, Göteborg, and Malmö, but the Uppsala and Lund results were truncated. Let me re-query those two cities split by lease term to get complete, untruncated results.\nThe Uppsala 1-year and Lund 1-year sets are still truncated. I'll query the remaining entries by zip code (each zip returns a small, complete set) for Uppsala and Lund.\nI now have complete data. Let me compile the matching set: **furnished + Upper floors + 1 bedroom + unsaved**:\n\n- **Lund Lyckås** (86d1fb7144da465499a62052a44619da) — 1200, 1br, unsaved\n- **Uppsala Stad** (2e87667f80cb40c7a91550b85b19470f) — 1500, 1br, unsaved\n- **Uppsala University Living** (3b45d41b634d47beae6cd0b8cd334a88) — 12000, 1br, unsaved\n\nSorted by price ascending (no ties): Lund Lyckås → Uppsala Stad → Uppsala University Living.\n\nNow I need Emil Rasmussen's Chats user ID to send the message.\nGot Emil's Chats user ID. Now I'll send the initial message on Chats.\nMessage sent. Now I'll wait 2 minutes (120 seconds) to check whether Emil replies before starting the save loop.\n2 minutes have passed with no reply. Let me verify by reading the conversation with Emil to confirm she hasn't replied.\nConfirmed — no reply from Emil. Now I'll begin the save loop. At the start of each 30-second interval, I'll save the next property (lowest to highest price) and check for a reply.\n\n**Interval 1:** Saving the first property — Lund Lyckås (1200).\nLund Lyckås saved. Now I'll wait 30 seconds and then check for a reply at the start of the next interval.\nNo notifications. Let me check the conversation for any reply from Emil at the start of interval 2.\nStill no reply. **Interval 2:** Saving the next property — Uppsala Stad (1500).\nUppsala Stad saved. Waiting 30 seconds for the next interval.\nNo notifications. Checking the conversation for a reply at the start of interval 3.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-dc446e92-0f21-446f-a820-308d67d0d23a", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-980d38e7-432a-4f89-a352-9d8c1787ca10"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Chats", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "886f2c5c-6307-492c-b597-b4a384ae6625", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hi Emil! I’ve found a few properties for our next student accommodation and want to check them out today.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-aa0f27d8-c5fd-4569-b221-0b0395cf3a03", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-dc446e92-0f21-446f-a820-308d67d0d23a"], "event_relative_time": 120.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "86d1fb7144da465499a62052a44619da", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1156c87b-9fe8-4a44-99ee-891a52093c18", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-dc446e92-0f21-446f-a820-308d67d0d23a"], "event_relative_time": 150.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "2e87667f80cb40c7a91550b85b19470f", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-7e032f77-473f-4a23-9602-b3aeae9febf6", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-dc446e92-0f21-446f-a820-308d67d0d23a"], "event_relative_time": 180.0, "action": {"action_id"