{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:46:02.774013", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_7fvkoi", "task_desc": "I need you to do a bunch of tasks, I won't have time to do them myself. Let me know if are unsure about anything before proceeding, I don't want you to make a mess. Reply to the email sent by Luís Mourão, saying I would love to collaborate, and that he should send his phone number. Book a Premium cab for 30 minutes before the photoshoot today, from Home to Frejgatan 103B, 113 26 Stockholm. Edit the photoshoot event for today so that it ends at 1 PM. Order the cheapest blue Baby Play Mat for Kids", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: I need you to do a bunch of tasks, I won't have time to do them myself. Let me know if are\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-tasks:\n1. Reply to Luís Mourão's email (collaborate + ask for phone number)\n2. Book a Premium cab 30 min before today's photoshoot\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score +20%", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-tasks:\n1. Reply to Luís Mourão's email (collaborate + ask for phone number)\n2. Book a Premium cab 30 min before today's photoshoot (Home → Frejgatan 103B, 113 26 Stockholm)\n3. Edit today's photoshoot event to end at 1 PM\n4. Order the cheapest blue Baby Play Mat for Kids\n\nLet me gather the needed information first.\nI have all the information I need. Let me analyze:\n\n- **Email**: Luís Mourão's email_id is `4503878a4de4463e81c91d14c4213cfc`\n- **Photoshoot**: starts 09:00, ends 12:00 today. Need to change end to 13:00. (No edit tool exists, so I'll delete and re-add.)\n- **Cab**: 30 min before 09:00 = 08:30, Premium, Home → Frejgatan 103B, 113 26 Stockholm\n- **Baby Play Mat**: Cheapest BLUE available variant is `2746feb842c949489a596e6f6a9b6548` (Blue, Microfiber, Large, $12.99). The $12.99 Pink one is excluded (not blue), and the $16.99 Blue XL is unavailable.\n\nLet me execute the independent actions now.\nEmail replied, cab booked, event deleted. The cart add failed due to a type issue with quantity. Let me retry the cart add and re-create the photoshoot event with the corrected end time.\nThe photoshoot event was re-created. The cart add still fails with the quantity type. Let me try without specifying quantity (default is 1).\nItem added to cart. Now let me checkout the order.\nCart has the correct blue Baby Play Mat. Let me checkout.\nAll tasks are complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n1. **Replied to Luís Mourão's email** — Confirmed I'd love to collaborate and asked him to send his phone number.\n\n2. **Booked a Premium cab** — For 08:30 today (30 minutes before the 09:00 photoshoot), from Home to Frejgatan 103B, 113 26 Stockholm. Status: BOOKED (estimated price ~30.68, ~23 min ride, ~4 min delay).\n\n3. **Edited the photoshoot event** — Changed the end time to 1:00 PM (it now runs 09:00–13:00). Since the calendar has no direct edit function, I recreated the event with the same details (Work tag, Studio location, attendee Kasper Rønnow) and the new end time.\n\n4. **Ordered the cheapest blue Baby Play Mat for Kids** — Added the Blue / Microfiber / Large variant ($12.99, the cheapest available blue option) and checked out. Order ID: `aca6b83d12734f57bdbaab220a2c2588`.\n\nNote: I excluded the $12.99 Pink variant (not blue) and the $16.99 Blue Extra Large variant (out of stock), so the $12.99 Blue Microfiber Large was the correct cheapest blue choice.\nAll sub-tasks have been completed successfully. Let me deliver the final summary to the user.\nAll tasks have been completed and the final summary has been delivered to the user.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1502e1a1-71f0-4630-ad8d-ecf91eab91dc", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-035e78b3-c278-409c-a3c2-d68338a5c3ed"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "4503878a4de4463e81c91d14c4213cfc", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hi Luís, \n\nI'd love to collaborate! Please send me your phone number.\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-fdfa0a38-b97c-4cb7-a8a4-bcdd6701d750", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-035e78b3-c278-409c-a3c2-d68338a5c3ed"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Cabs", "function": "order_ride", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "start_location", "value": "Home", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_location", "value": "Frejgatan 103B, 113 26 Stockholm", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "service_type", "value": "Premium", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "ride_time", "value": "2024-10-15 08:30:00", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-0b93fdb4-9767-4e87-8453-e8d0aa57752c", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-035e78b3-c278-409c-a3c2-d68338a5c3ed"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Photoshoot", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 09:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-15 13:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "Work", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "Photoshoot for upcoming brand campaign.", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Studio", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Kasper Rønnow\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-c47634f1-eb07-4c1c-b142-34e875cd37ae", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-035e78b3-c278-409c-a3c2-d68338a5c3ed"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "2746feb842c949489a596e6f6a9b6548", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "1", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a795ca51-b63c-4c3b-b2b2-d1c8dc589a4f", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-035e78b3-c278-409c-a3c2-d68338a5c3ed"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "d2f892cf34ab4e16be08eb6dbfd01727", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-673fd117-8da8-4e73-b345-bdab3dcc5d8c", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-c47634f1-eb07-4c1c-b142-34e875cd37ae"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.8333333333333334, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "execution", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 502, "wc_served": [0.4, 0.4], "wc_mean": 0.4, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.9, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3415.67, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3415.67, "prof_tok_in": 154304, "prof_tok_out": 3217, "prof_llm_calls": 9}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:46:35.278869", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_0obld3", "task_desc": "In my Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, suggest the dates and times two hours before my next two yoga classes for a 1 hour call between the three of us. Let me know as soon as you’ve done this. Wait exactly 3 minutes from your message to me for responses. If availability is confirmed by both of them in that time, schedule the call at the agreed upon time. If they are both available for both times, tell them in the same Messages conversation that we'll do the earlier one. I", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: In my Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, suggest the dates and times two hours before my next two yoga classes for a 1 hour call\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: my yoga classes from the calendar and the Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne.\nThe yoga clas\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding the Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, and finding my next two yoga classes.\nLet me check the current time and find the yoga classes that are upcoming (after now).\nThe current time is 2024-10-15 07:00:00 UTC. The yoga classes found are all in August (past). Let me search for upcoming yoga classes from now forward.\nThe future events list doesn't show yoga classes yet. Let me search more specifically and get a fuller list of upcoming events.\nThe search results are being truncated. Let me re-run the yoga search to see the complete list of yoga classes, and also check the conversation with Joana and Vigdis.\nThe search results are truncated. Let me get the truncated event to see its date, and read the conversation with Joana and Vigdis.\nThe conversation exists (current user is Astrid, +46734567890). Now I need to find the next two yoga classes after the current time (2024-10-15 07:00:00). The search results are truncated. Let me use the \"Health\" tag to find all health events (yoga classes are tagged Health) and narrow the date range.\nThe results are being truncated in display. Let me narrow the date range to find yoga classes in the coming weeks. I'll query specific weeks to avoid truncation.\nThe results are being truncated. Let me query in narrower date ranges to find the yoga classes without truncation.\nI found the first upcoming yoga class: Monday, 2024-10-21 18:00:00. But the Oct 15-18 query was truncated, so there may be a yoga class hidden there. Let me check Oct 17-18 specifically.\nFound the first yoga class: Thursday, 2024-10-17 18:00:00. Now let me check Oct 18-20 to find the second yoga class (between the 17th and the 21st).\nI now have the next two yoga classes:\n1. **Thursday, 2024-10-17 18:00:00** (Yoga Class)\n2. **Friday, 2024-10-18 18:00:00** (Yoga Class)\n\nTwo hours before each gives the call options:\n- **Thursday, 2024-10-17 16:00–17:00**\n- **Friday, 2024-10-18 16:00–17:00**\n\nLet me suggest these in the group conversation with Joana and Vigdis.\nI've sent the suggestion to the group conversation. Now let me let you know that this is done, as requested.\nI received notifications of new messages. Let me wait the full 3 minutes as instructed, then read the conversation to check their responses.\n3 minutes have passed. Let me read the conversation to check Joana and Vigdis's responses.\nI've reviewed the responses after the 3-minute wait. Let me analyze them:\n\n- **Joana (+351954123456):** \"Both of those times are good for me!\" — confirms availability for both proposed times (Oct 17 and Oct 18, 16:00–17:00). ✓\n- **Vigdis (+4571345678):** \"Give me one second while I check my schedule!\" and \"I'm up for 4-5PM on the 16th!\" — she did **not** confirm either of the two proposed times (Oct 17 or Oct 18); instead she proposed a different time (Wednesday, Oct 16) and was still checking her schedule.\n\nThe scheduling conditions are:\n1. *Both confirm availability → schedule at the agreed time* — NOT met, since Vigdis didn't confirm either proposed time (no mutually agreed time exists; Joana is free 17th/18th, Vigdis wants the 16th).\n2. *Both available for both times → do the earlier one* — NOT met, since Vigdis isn't available for either proposed time.\n\nSince both did not confirm availability for the proposed times and there's no agreed-upon common time, the call cannot be scheduled. Let me report this to you.\nThe task is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n**1. Found the next two yoga classes** (after the current time, 2024-10-15 07:00):\n- Thursday, Oct 17, 18:00–19:00\n- Friday, Oct 18, 18:00–19:00\n\n**2. Suggested two 1-hour call options** (two hours before each class) in the group Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne:\n- Option 1: Thursday, Oct 17, 16:00–17:00\n- Option 2: Friday, Oct 18, 16:00–17:00\n\n**3. Let you know immediately** that the suggestion was sent.\n\n**4. Waited exactly 3 minutes** for responses, then checked the conversation:\n- Joana: available for both times ✓\n- Vigdis: did NOT confirm either proposed time (was still checking, then suggested a different time — Wed Oct 16, 4–5 PM)\n\n**5. Outcome:** Since both did not confirm availability for the proposed times and there was no mutually agreed time, neither scheduling condition was met. Per the instructions (\"If only one or neither of them replies, you're done\" — and by extension, if they don't both confirm a common time), I did not schedule the call or send a confirmation message, and I reported the result to you.\n\nNo calendar event was created, as the conditions for scheduling were not satisfied.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-395097df-23ff-4689-a281-4b85f574d78d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-1002ac8b-cff9-409e-9170-a615155a24bb"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message_to_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "conversation_id", "value": "ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Joana and Vigdis, I was thinking of scheduling a 1-hour call with both of you. Would both of you be available on Oct 16 at 4 PM or Oct 17 at 4 PM? ", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-e18425b4-df03-4b0a-8777-ce4f314d566e", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-395097df-23ff-4689-a281-4b85f574d78d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Message sent to Joana and Vigdis suggesting a 1-hour call on October 16 at 4 PM and October 17 at 4 PM. Waiting for their response.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-81a7cc64-32f8-472d-a4cc-408a781c0d38", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-479d2a41-6896-4780-9f73-3dbc51784e01", "OracleEvent-AGENT-ded9b844-a686-4fe0-8313-baed17e87e8d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "October 16 at 4 PM was chosen as the date and time for the 1-hour call with Joana and Vigdis.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-479d2a41-6896-4780-9f73-3dbc51784e01", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-e53b14eb-4f75-4fed-912f-29b6acb98f7b", "Event-ENV-c2a86c3c-e49e-4beb-8156-fae9d918c57f"], "event_relative_time": 30.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Phone Call with Joana and Vigdis", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 17:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Joana Silva\",\"Vigdis Rønne\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ded9b844-a686-4fe0-8313-baed17e87e8d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-c2a86c3c-e49e-4beb-8156-fae9d918c57f", "Event-ENV-e53b14eb-4f75-4fed-912f-29b6acb98f7b"], "event_relative_time": 30.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message_to_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "conversation_id", "value": "ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Joana and Vigdis, just confirming our 1 hour call for October 16 at 4 PM. Looking forward to catching up then!", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.6, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "time", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 586, "wc_served": [1.4, 1.4], "wc_mean": 1.4, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.05, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3678.98, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3678.98, "prof_tok_in": 405906, "prof_tok_out": 16170, "prof_llm_calls": 19}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:47:43.981726", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_axgfp0", "task_desc": "Add the two-bedroom apartments with a minimum square footage of 800 in the zip code of 753 32 to my saved apartments list and order me a medium cardboard Acoustic Guitar Pinata. Send an email to the youngest contact who lives in my city to ask if they know how to play the guitar and if they are looking for a roommate. Also, I am unable to attend the photoshoot session today, could you reschedule it to the earliest available 3-hour slot between 9 AM and 5 PM starting from tomorrow and then messag", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: Add the two-bedroom apartments with a minimum square footage of 800 in the zip code of 753 32 to my saved apartments list and order me a medium cardbo\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests and start gathering information. Let me make several independent calls in parallel.\nLet me fix the type errors and gather\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> ", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Add 2-bedroom apartments (≥800 sq ft) in zip 753 32 to saved list\n2. Order a medium cardboard Acoustic Guitar Pinata\n3. Email the youngest contact in my city about guitar/roommate\n4. Reschedule today's photoshoot to earliest 3-hour slot (9 AM–5 PM) from tomorrow\n5. Message the attendee (via our prior conversation method) with the new time\n\nLet me gather initial information in parallel.\nLet me retry the apartment search with correct types, search for Stockholm contacts, and check calendar availability from tomorrow.\nThe apartment search tool has a type issue. Let me list all apartments and all contacts directly, and get the full calendar for the reschedule window.\nThe list was truncated. Let me retry with proper integer types for the tools that need them, and re-list apartments.\nThe tools require integer types. Let me try with no optional params (using defaults) and re-list apartments fully.\nThe contacts and calendar results are paginated/truncated. Let me get the full apartment list, paginate contacts, and check Oct 16 events specifically. I'll pass integers where the tools require them.\nThe apartment list is truncated and the search tool has a type bug. Let me try searching apartments with just zip_code and square_footage (filtering bedrooms myself), and look up the calendar attendees' contact details to find Stockholm residents.\nI found Stockholm residents. Now I need to: (1) get the full apartment list to find all 753 32 apartments, and (2) paginate contacts to ensure I find the youngest Stockholm resident. The search/pagination tools need integer types. Let me try passing integers.\nThe integer-parameter tools reject string values. Let me work around this: search apartments by zip_code only (string param), and use search_contacts to find more Stockholm residents.\nI found the 753 32 apartments. The two-bedroom ones with ≥800 sqft so far: Uppsala Universitet (900) and Uppsala University Heights (800). Uppsala Oaks (2 bed) is truncated—I need its sqft. Let me get its details and search more surnames to ensure I find the youngest Stockholm resident (currently Linnea Svensson, 21).\nI now have the 753 32 apartments. The two-bedroom ones with ≥800 sqft are: **Uppsala Universitet** (900), **Uppsala University Heights** (800), and **Uppsala Oaks** (1000).\n\nFor the youngest Stockholm contact, I've found Linnea Svensson (21). Let me verify there's no younger Stockholm resident by searching more names, and get Åsa Lindqvist's age.\nThe search tool only matches names/phone/email, not city. To be thorough about finding the youngest Stockholm resident, let me try enumerating the full contact list via get_contacts with an integer offset.\nThe framework is passing my value as a string. Let me try passing the offset as a bare number (no quotes) to satisfy the int requirement.\nThe `get_contacts` view limit is 2 and pagination is blocked by a type error, so I must rely on `search_contacts`. To confidently find the youngest Stockholm resident, let me do a broad sweep of common Swedish first names.\nGood — I found two Stockholm residents so far (Birgitta Larsson, 66; Brother Mikael Svensson, 51). I need to find younger Stockholm residents. Let me search more Swedish names.\nI found more Stockholm residents. Note Astrid Lundqvist (23) is the current user (is_user: true), so she's excluded. The youngest non-user Stockholm resident so far is Linnea Svensson (21). Let me enumerate all contacts to be thorough about finding the youngest Stockholm resident.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nThe offset must be passed as an integer. Let me retry without quotes.\nLet me try calling without the offset parameter.\nThe default call works but I need to paginate. The offset parameter is being treated as a string. Let me try passing it as a raw number.\nThe `offset` parameter requires an integer type which the harness is passing as a string, so pagination is blocked. However, my `search_contacts` for \"Stockholm\" returned all 5 Stockholm residents (the search clearly includes city/address fields). Among them, excluding the current user (Astrid, 23), the youngest is **Linnea Svensson (21)**.\n\nLet me now proceed with the actionable sub-tasks in parallel: save the two apartments, find the piñata product, and confirm Linnea's contact details.\nThe apartment IDs and contact IDs aren't what I assumed. Let me re-run the searches to get the exact IDs, and note the medium cardboard piñata variant is `14bd9507e3914098933178cdb4e24c30`.\nThe contacts search returned empty this time (inconsistent). Let me retry it, and fix the bedrooms parameter to be an integer.\nThe contacts search is now flaky (returning empty). Let me search by the specific name to confirm Linnea exists, and retry the apartment search with an integer bedrooms value.\nLinnea Svensson (21, Stockholm) is confirmed as the youngest non-user Stockholm resident. The apartment search keeps rejecting the string \"2\" for bedrooms. Let me try passing it as a raw integer.\nThe harness keeps passing bedrooms as a string. Let me search with just zip_code and square_footage, then filter bedrooms myself.\nThe harness is stringifying all numeric parameters. Let me try the search with only the zip_code string filter, then I'll filter bedrooms and square footage from the results myself.\nI now have the apartments in zip 753 32. The last entry was truncated. Let me get its details to check square footage, and also confirm the full list.\nI now have all 5 apartments in zip 753 32. The two-bedroom ones with ≥800 sqft are:\n- **Uppsala Universitet** (2br, 900 sqft) — `7d4dbc092e214487b48b05e59aa8026c`\n- **Uppsala University Heights** (2br, 800 sqft) — `c4bdb29680ad4a6ab2f185bb0858574d`\n- **Uppsala Oaks** (2br, 1000 sqft) — `698ba26263b14bdfbafbe16af46aca99`\n\nLet me save all three and add the medium cardboard piñata (item `14bd9507e3914098933178cdb4e24c30`) to the cart.\nThe three apartments are saved. The cart quantity needs to be an integer; let me add without specifying quantity (defaults to 1).\nThe piñata is in the cart. Now let me handle the calendar and messaging. Let me find the photoshoot event and check the calendar for tomorrow's availability.\nThe current sim time is **2024-10-15 07:05:51 UTC** (Tuesday), confirming today is 2024-10-15. The photoshoot search returned events only in August 2024 (all in the past). Let me verify there's no photoshoot actually scheduled for today and get the complete photoshoot list.\nFound today's photoshoot: **event `d2f892cf34ab4e16be08eb6dbfd01727`**, \"Photoshoot\", 2024-10-15 09:00–12:00 (3 hours), attendee **Kasper Rønnow**.\n\nNow I need to find the earliest available 3-hour slot between 9 AM and 5 PM starting tomorrow (2024-10-16). Let me check tomorrow's calendar for conflicts.\nTomorrow (Wed 2024-10-16) has no available 3-hour gap between 9 AM–5 PM — the only free windows are 11:00–12:00 and 16:00–17:00 (each just 1 hour). I need to check the next day, Thursday 2024-10-17.\nThursday also has no 3-hour gap (busy 10:00–16:00). Let me check Friday 2024-10-18.\nFriday 2024-10-18 has a free 12:00–15:00 window (the earliest 3-hour gap, since 9–12 is blocked by a 10–12 session). That's the earliest available 3-hour slot between 9 AM–5 PM starting from tomorrow.\n\nNow let me reschedule: delete the old photoshoot and create it on Friday 12:00–15:00. I'll also look up the attendee Kasper Rønnow in both messaging systems to find our conversation history.\nThe photoshoot is rescheduled to Friday 2024-10-18 12:00–15:00. Now I need to find which messaging system has conversation history with Kasper Rønnow. The Chats system found him (id `5f06df26-d63b-4ac1-84d9-8b81e60ae733`), but Messages returned empty. Let me check recent conversations in both systems.\nThe offset/limit need to be integers. Let me call without those arguments to use defaults.\nLet me find conversations with Kasper Rønnow in the Chats system (where he has an id).\nI found the conversation history with Kasper Rønnow i", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-e7be4ece-ebe1-4f59-afb1-07e7f8b9dcab", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-e639d895-8d07-419e-9fba-53d84c261d06"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "c4bdb29680ad4a6ab2f185bb0858574d", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-57713b98-1345-41b7-9409-25d834a2c78f", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-e639d895-8d07-419e-9fba-53d84c261d06"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "698ba26263b14bdfbafbe16af46aca99", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f0e10bef-fb20-4e80-9528-2c3942f3ee05", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-e639d895-8d07-419e-9fba-53d84c261d06"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "7d4dbc092e214487b48b05e59aa8026c", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-4cc65f48-3749-4b6e-a9b2-1400f28d52a4", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-e639d895-8d07-419e-9fba-53d84c261d06"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "14bd9507e3914098933178cdb4e24c30", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "1", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-6cfa2f9a-b906-400f-bdcd-f332d350c844", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-e639d895-8d07-419e-9fba-53d84c261d06"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"linnea.svensson@byggab.se\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Guitar and Roommate Inquiry", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Linnea,\n\nDo you know how to play the guitar? Are you looking for a roommate?\n\nBest,\nAstrid Lundqvist", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-6b8f7074-f192-42ed-8079-1d6a8362c3fe", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-e639d895-8d07-419e-9fba-53d84c261d06"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "d2f892cf34ab4e16be08eb6dbfd01727", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-c8881b19-dd8a-4c56-afac-6d90d0cde95b", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-e639d895-8d07-419e-9fba-53d84c261d06"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Photoshoot", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 12:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 15:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "Work", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "Photoshoot for upcoming brand campaign", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "Studio", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Kasper Rønnow\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-09c03978-7d02-4006-a59b-3158b852af2f", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-4cc65f48-3749-4b6e-a9b2-1400f28d52a4"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975602.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-35890e9b-2fa0-4753-a2ca-bafd8ab034ba", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-6b8f7074-f192-42ed-8079-1d6a8362c3fe", "OracleEvent-AGENT-c8881b19-dd8a-4c56-afac-6d90d0cde95b"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Chats", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "5f06df26-d63b-4ac1-84d9-8b81e60ae733", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hi Kasper, the photoshoot has been rescheduled to Friday, 18 October 2024, 12:00 pm - 3:00 pm at the Studio. See you then!", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.7777777777777778, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "execution", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 646, "wc_served": [0.6, 0.6], "wc_mean": 0.6, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3697.9, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3697.9, "prof_tok_in": 775232, "prof_tok_out": 36659, "prof_llm_calls": 40}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:47:55.790326", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_b647lw", "task_desc": "Cancel all my events for tomorrow that I have with any attendee who emailed me at least once in 2024, and reschedule them for the next day. If you find any events conflicting with the new schedulings, tell me what they are and ask me how to proceed with those.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Cancel all my events for tomorrow that I have with any attendee who emailed me at least on\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: tomorrow's calendar events and the emails I received in 2024 (to identify which attendees emailed me).\nTomorrow'\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score +40%", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: tomorrow's calendar events and the emails I received in 2024 (to identify which attendees emailed me).\nTomorrow (Wednesday, 2024-10-16) has 5 events. Two have attendees:\n- **Brand Partnership Meeting** (09:00–11:00) with Åke Svensson\n- **Yoga Class** (18:00–19:00) with Åsa Lindgren\n\nThe other three have no attendees, so they're not affected. Now I need to check whether these attendees emailed me in 2024. Let me fix the email listing and search for emails from these attendees.\nÅke Svensson emailed me in 2024 (July 2024). The search for Åsa Lindgren returned nothing, but let me verify more thoroughly with broader searches and also list the inbox to confirm.\nBoth attendees emailed me in 2024:\n- **Åke Svensson** (ake.svensson@dif.se) — July 2024\n- **Åsa Lindgren** (asa.lindgren@gaia2mail.com) — October 2024\n\nSo both events with attendees qualify. Before rescheduling, let me check what's already on the next day (2024-10-17) to detect conflicts.\nBoth attendees emailed me in 2024, so both events with attendees qualify for cancellation and rescheduling:\n- **Brand Partnership Meeting** (Wed 09:00–11:00) with Åke Svensson\n- **Yoga Class** (Wed 18:00–19:00) with Åsa Lindgren\n\nNow I see that Thursday 2024-10-17 already has events. Let me analyze the conflicts if I reschedule to the same times on Thursday:\n\n- **Brand Partnership Meeting** → Thu 09:00–11:00 would **overlap** with the existing *Content Creation Session* (Thu 10:00–12:00).\n- **Yoga Class** → Thu 18:00–19:00 would **directly conflict** with the existing *Yoga Class* already on Thursday at 18:00–19:00 (same attendee Åsa Lindgren).\n\nPer the task, I'll cancel the qualifying Wednesday events first, then report the conflicts and ask how to proceed. Let me cancel the two events.\nBoth qualifying events have been cancelled. Now I'll report the conflicts that would arise from rescheduling them to the same times on Thursday and ask how to proceed.\nI've completed the cancellation and reported the conflicts. Now I'll wait for the user's response on how to handle the rescheduling.\nNo response yet. Let me continue waiting for the user's instructions on how to handle the rescheduling.\nStill no response. I'll continue waiting for the user's decision.\nI've completed the actionable part of the task and am awaiting the user's decision on the conflicting reschedulings. Let me wait a bit longer for a response.\nI've completed the cancellation of the qualifying events and reported the conflicts to the user, asking how to proceed. The user has not yet responded with instructions for the rescheduling. I'll wait once more for their decision.\nI've completed the autonomous portion of the task:\n\n1. **Identified** tomorrow's (Wed, Oct 16) events with attendees who emailed me in 2024 — both Åke Svensson (July 2024) and Åsa Lindgren (October 2024) qualified.\n2. **Cancelled** both qualifying events (Brand Partnership Meeting and Yoga Class).\n3. **Reported** the conflicts that would arise from rescheduling them to the same Thursday slots and asked the user how to proceed.\n\nI've waited for a follow-up response but none has arrived. The rescheduling is blocked pending the user's decision on how to handle the two conflicts (Brand Partnership Meeting overlapping the Thursday Content Creation Session, and Yoga Class clashing with the existing Thursday Yoga Class). I'll stop here and await the user's instructions.\nNo new message arrived from the user. I've already completed the actionable portion of the task and reported the conflicts, awaiting the user's decision on how to handle the rescheduling. Since no follow-up request came in, I'll stop here.\n\n**Summary of what was done:**\n- ✅ Cancelled the two Wednesday, Oct 16 events with attendees who emailed in 2024:\n  - *Brand Partnership Meeting* (09:00–11:00) with Åke Svensson (emailed July 2024)\n  - *Yoga Class* (18:00–19:00) with Åsa Lindgren (emailed October 2024)\n- ✅ Left the three attendee-less Wednesday events untouched\n- ✅ Identified and reported the conflicts that would occur if rescheduled to the same Thursday slots:\n  - Brand Partnership Meeting → Thu 09:00–11:00 overlaps the existing *Content Creation Session* (Thu 10:00–12:00)\n  - Yoga Class → Thu 18:00–19:00 clashes with the existing *Yoga Class* (Thu 18:00–19:00, also with Åsa Lindgren)\n- ⏳ Rescheduling is pending your decision on how to handle those two conflicts.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-8a8db522-f8d4-4206-a509-cf42b2f5cd4d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9226bff0-900a-4952-b1c4-bda398d4bd40"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "81141f54d8904d15b58faaff860d0d65", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5a1c51fa-9ec1-42ee-ad42-adffabfc4cb6", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9226bff0-900a-4952-b1c4-bda398d4bd40"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "d161b55ebc704647bc8d949977009093", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-89af3afe-deaa-4313-aead-31c81e950242", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9226bff0-900a-4952-b1c4-bda398d4bd40"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "There are scheduling conflicts. The Brand Partnership Meeting conflicts with the Content Creation Session on October 17, 10:00 AM - 12:00 PM. The Yoga Class conflicts with another Yoga Class on October 17, 06:00 PM - 07:00 PM. Please clarify how to proceed.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "ambiguity", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 534, "wc_served": [1.0, 1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.2, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3581.32, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3581.32, "prof_tok_in": 256222, "prof_tok_out": 7572, "prof_llm_calls": 14}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T13:48:22.607192", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_lwmt8g", "task_desc": "I want you to send some messages to my uncle, Åke Lindström, in Chats. Send him a new message every 40 seconds from now until he responds, asking him if I can come over at 6 PM this Saturday for an hour. Do this a total of 3 times if he doesn't respond and let me know when you have sent 3 messages, then wait a maximum of 1 minute (he's usually a pretty slow responder) after the third message for a response. As soon as he responds, if it's a yes, schedule “Annoying Uncle Åke” in my calendar, the ", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: I want you to send some messages to my uncle, Åke Lindström, in Chats. Send him a new mess\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by understanding the current time, finding my uncle's Chats user ID, and locating his address in contacts.\nI have everything I need:\n- Current time: \nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I want you to send some messages to my uncle, Åke Lindström, in Chats. Send him a new mess\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by understanding the current time and finding my uncle's contact in Chats.\nI found my uncle's Chats user ID. Now let me get his contact details to fi\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll start by understanding the current time, finding my uncle's Chats user ID, and locating his address in contacts.\nI have everything I need:\n- Current time: 2024-10-15 07:00:00 UTC\n- Uncle's Chats user ID: `b7ac8a90-f559-4440-a1ab-b54678021172`\n- Uncle's address: Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm, Sweden\n\nThis Saturday is 2024-10-19, so 6 PM = 2024-10-19 18:00:00 (for an hour, 18:00–19:00).\n\nLet me send the first message now.\nFirst message sent. Now I'll wait 40 seconds before the second message.\nA new message arrived in the conversation with Åke. Let me check if he responded.\nÅke has responded with **\"No please. I value my peace.\"** — that's a clear NO.\n\nPer your instructions, since he said no, I'll do everything anyway and send him a message that he doesn't have a choice. Let me proceed with all the actions: schedule the calendar event, book the Premium cab (30 min before = 2024-10-19 17:30), send him the \"no choice\" message, and find the Zebra Foal toy.\nAll actions are done except ordering the wooden Zebra Foal toy. The wooden variant is item_id `7eb3d17b7e3845a8a052177b1341311b` (Material: Wood, 12.99). Let me add it to the cart and check out.\nEverything is complete. Let me send you a summary message.\nAll tasks have been completed successfully. Here's what happened:\n\n**Messages to Uncle Åke (Chats):**\n- Sent message #1 at 07:00:00 asking if you can come over at 6 PM this Saturday for an hour.\n- Åke responded almost immediately with **\"No please. I value my peace.\"** — a clear NO.\n\nSince he said no, I followed your instructions to do everything anyway:\n- 📅 **Calendar:** Scheduled \"Annoying Uncle Åke\" on Sat 2024-10-19, 18:00–19:00, at his address (Östermalmsgatan 12, 114 39 Stockholm, Sweden), with Åke Lindström as attendee.\n- 🚕 **Cab:** Booked a Premium cab from Home to his address, picking you up at 17:30 (30 min before the event). Status: BOOKED.\n- 💬 **Message to Åke:** Sent \"You don't have a choice, Åke. Expect me at 6 PM this Saturday for an hour. See you then!\"\n- 🦓 **Shopping:** Ordered the wooden SCHLEICH Zebra Foal toy (Order confirmed).\n\nEverything you asked for is done.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-bd26f312-bda3-4038-a6cd-3c28c2f6a687", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-