{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:10:54.914637", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_hwe7io", "task_desc": "Send an email with the subject \"Egypt\" to Viggo Mikkelsen and attach the picture with the filename containing Egypt. Tell him I'm taking off November 30, 2024 - December 7, 2024, for our trip to Egypt. Cancel everything on my schedule during that time period and then schedule \"Trip to Egypt\" with Viggo Mikkelsen from 11/30/2024 at 7 am - 12/7/2024 at 7 pm. Order one of the Funforge Kingsport Festival the Card Game, the English version for 1-2 players for the trip. Send a Messages message to Åke ", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Send an email with the subject \"Egypt\" to Viggo Mikkelsen and attach the picture with the \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Send email to Viggo Mikkelsen (subject \"Egypt\", attach Egypt picture, mention trip dates)\n2. Cancel all schedule even\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score -85%", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Send email to Viggo Mikkelsen (subject \"Egypt\", attach Egypt picture, mention trip dates)\n2. Cancel all schedule events during 11/30/2024 - 12/7/2024\n3. Schedule \"Trip to Egypt\" with Viggo Mikkelsen 11/30 7am - 12/7 7pm\n4. Order Funforge Kingsport Festival Card Game (English, 1-2 players)\n5. Send Messages message to Åke about cat-sitting\n\nLet me gather the needed information first.\nLet me find the Egypt picture and locate Åke's user ID.\nLet me look deeper into the Pictures folders and find Åke.\nLet me explore the Travels folder and try to find Åke's contact info.\nI found the Egypt picture at `/Pictures/Personal/Travels/Egypt_2021.jpg`. There are three contacts named Åke, so I need to determine which one. Let me check existing message conversations to identify the right Åke.\nThe tool expects integers. Let me retry with integer values.\nThe conversation listing tool has a type issue. Let me try to identify the right Åke by checking existing conversations via participant lookup, and also try exact user-id lookups.\nThe Messages listing tools have a type bug with offset/limit. Let me try without those optional parameters.\nNone of the Åkes have prior conversations. There are three Åke contacts, so I need to determine which one. Let me get the third Åke's details.\nThere are three Åke contacts (Lundqvist, Lindström, Svensson) with no prior conversations to disambiguate. I'll handle the unambiguous parts first, then check with you about which Åke. Let me gather the needed info.\nI now have all the info I need for the unambiguous parts:\n- **Viggo Mikkelsen**: vmikkelsen@teatret.dk\n- **Egypt picture**: `/Pictures/Personal/Travels/Egypt_2021.jpg`\n- **Trip events to cancel** (Nov 30 – Dec 7): 3 events on Nov 30\n- **Game**: Funforge Kingsport Festival, English, 1-2 players → item `1bcf6000c2574e1b9b2b9392742a1b5c`\n\nLet me execute the email, calendar cancellations, trip event, and game order.\nCalendar events cancelled and trip event created. Let me fix the email (needs list) and cart (needs int).\nEmail sent. The cart `quantity` keeps failing as a string — let me try without it (default is 1).\nGame added to cart. Let me check out the order.\nThe order is placed. Now, for the Messages message to Åke — there are **three** contacts named Åke in the address book, and none have prior conversations to disambiguate:\n\n- **Åke Lundqvist** (+46701234567) — Stockholm, Retired teacher\n- **Åke Lindström** (+46702123456) — Gothenburg, Software engineer\n- **Åke Svensson** (+46700123456) — Stockholm, Scout manager\n\nSince the task says to check with you if unsure, I'll ask which Åke to message before sending.\nI've sent the clarification question to you. Let me wait for your response to determine which Åke to message.\nNo response yet. Let me continue waiting for your reply.\nI've been waiting for your response about which Åke to message, but no reply has come through yet. Let me wait a bit longer.\nI've completed all the unambiguous parts of the task and am waiting for your answer on which Åke to message. Let me do one more wait in case your reply comes through.\nI've waited a total of 20 minutes for your response but haven't received a reply. Since the only remaining action (the Åke message) is blocked on your clarification, I'll provide a final status summary. Everything else is complete.\nI've completed all the unambiguous parts of the task and am blocked only on the one item that requires your clarification.\n\n**Completed:**\n- ✅ Sent the \"Egypt\" email to Viggo Mikkelsen (vmikkelsen@teatret.dk) with the Egypt picture attached, mentioning the Nov 30 – Dec 7, 2024 trip.\n- ✅ Cancelled all 3 scheduled events during Nov 30 – Dec 7, 2024 (Content Creation, Social Media Analytics, Relaxation Time).\n- ✅ Added the \"Trip to Egypt\" calendar event with Viggo Mikkelsen (Nov 30 7:00 AM – Dec 7 7:00 PM).\n- ✅ Ordered the Funforge Kingsport Festival card game (English, 1-2 players) for the trip.\n\n**Pending your input:**\n- ⏳ The Messages message to Åke about house/cat-sitting — there are three contacts named Åke (Lundqvist, Lindström, Svensson), so I asked you which one to message. Once you reply, I'll send it right away.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-04a2dcc0-a99d-463d-b1e0-00126626b4ab", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-02b62099-a29d-49e1-ac70-ee40c196a0ca"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "delete_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "event_id", "value": "a7355cc7556d47e08