{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:22:40.821472", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_22_2oh10h", "task_desc": "Add Matthew Beaumont as a new contact in Dallas, Texas with the email mbeaumont@gaia2mail.com and the phone number +12145567891. He is 27 and a chef. Tell me the name of the most expensive apartment in Dallas and save it if it hasn't been saved already. If there's a tie, send the first result in alphabetical order. Send an email with the subject \"Dallas Apartment Recommendation\" to Matthew Beaumont asking if that apartment would be a good place to live when I move. Schedule an event for my fligh", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Add Matthew Beaumont as a new contact in Dallas, Texas with the email mbeaumont@gaia2mail.\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Add Matthew Beaumont as a contact (Dallas, TX; email; phone; age 27; chef)\n2. Find the most expensive Dallas apartmen\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score -10%", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Add Matthew Beaumont as a contact (Dallas, TX; email; phone; age 27; chef)\n2. Find the most expensive Dallas apartment (tie → first alphabetical), tell the name, save if not saved\n3. Send email to Matthew with subject \"Dallas Apartment Recommendation\"\n4. Schedule flight event Dec 1 at 6 AM for 5 hours\n5. Cancel all events on Nov 30 (day before flight)\n\nLet me start with the independent actions.\nThe contact add failed (age must be int). Let me retry with int age, and get the full apartment list to confirm the most expensive.\nThe contact add fails because age is being passed as a string. Let me add without age first, then edit to add it. Also, the Dallas apartment search was truncated, so let me re-run it to see all Dallas apartments.\nContact added (ID: 04af3af7bea91a5ebe08dc20b83f2186). Now I need to add age 27 via edit. The Dallas search output is truncated, so let me confirm the most expensive by filtering with a high min_price, and edit the contact's age.\nAge updated. The min_price needs to be an int. Let me retry to confirm the most expensive Dallas apartment.\nThe contact is now complete. The `min_price` filter failed because I passed it as a string — I need to pass it as a bare number (like I did with age in the edit). Let me retry to confirm the most expensive Dallas apartment.\nThe `min_price` keeps being serialized as a string. Let me get the full apartment catalog by listing with an offset to see all Dallas apartments and confirm the most expensive.\nThe contact is complete. The `min_price` filter keeps failing due to a type serialization issue, and the Dallas search output is truncated (cut off mid-entry at \"Lakewood Apartments\"). I need to see ALL Dallas apartments to find the most expensive. Let me search by each known Dallas zip code to get the complete, untruncated list.\nI now have most Dallas apartments, but the 75204 search was truncated (cut off at \"Uptown Dallas Apartments\" 2200), so there may be more. The `min_price` filter can't be passed as a number through this interface. Let me enumerate Dallas apartments via name-based searches to ensure I capture everything (especially any 6th 75204 apartment) and confirm the most expensive.\nI now have a comprehensive list, but the `location=Dallas` search was truncated and I discovered additional apartments (e.g., Lakeside Apartments in 75218) only via name searches. To be certain about the most expensive, I must check all Dallas zip codes. Let me sweep the remaining Dallas zip codes in batches.\nAll other Dallas zip codes are empty. I've now confirmed the complete Dallas inventory across zip codes 75201, 75202, 75204, 75214, and 75218. The most expensive is **Uptown Lofts** ($2,500/mo, 75201), which is already saved.\n\nNow let me: (1) ensure Uptown Lofts is saved (idempotent), (2) schedule the Dec 1 flight, and (3) find events on Nov 30 (the day before) to cancel. These are independent.\nUptown Lofts is saved, the flight is scheduled (event a6f807f2c8c09795b8351b2eef49916a), and I found 4 events on Nov 30 (the day before the flight) to cancel. Let me cancel all of them.\nAll 4 Nov 30 events are canceled. Now let me send the email to Matthew Beaumont about the apartment recommendation.\nThe recipients must be a list. Let me retry.\nAll actions are complete. Let me verify the contact was successfully added before finalizing.\nAll sub-requests are complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n**1. Added Matthew Beaumont as a contact** ✅\n- Name: Matthew Beaumont\n- Location: Dallas, Texas (USA)\n- Email: mbeaumont@gaia2mail.com\n- Phone: +12145567891\n- Age: 27, Job: Chef\n\n**2. Most expensive Dallas apartment** ✅\nAfter checking all Dallas zip codes (75201, 75202, 75204, 75214, 75218), the most expensive is **Uptown Lofts** — a 2-bed, 2-bath furnished penthouse at 789 Uptown Dr, Dallas (75201) for **$2,500/month**. (No tie at the top; the next highest is Dallas Downtown Lofts at $2,400.)\n\n**3. Saved the apartment** ✅\nUptown Lofts was already in your favorites, so it remains saved.\n\n**4. Sent the email** ✅\nSubject: \"Dallas Apartment Recommendation\" sent to mbeaumont@gaia2mail.com, asking whether Uptown Lofts would be a good place to live when you move.\n\n**5. Scheduled the flight** ✅\n\"Flight to Dallas\" on December 1, 2024, 6:00 AM–11:00 AM (5 hours).\n\n**6. Canceled events the day before the flight (Nov 30)** ✅\nCanceled all 4 scheduled events on Saturday, Nov 30:\n- Wine List Update Meeting (10:00–11:30 AM)\n- Staff Training Session (2:00–3:30 PM)\n- Yoga Class (6:00–7:00 PM)\n- Dinner with Friends (8:00–10:00 PM)\n\nEverything is done.\nAll sub-requests have been completed and verified. Let me deliver the final summary to the user.\nThe task is fully complete. I've delivered the final summary to the user covering all six sub-requests:\n\n1. ✅ Added Matthew Beaumont as a contact (Dallas, TX; email; phone; age 27; chef)\n2. ✅ Identified the most expensive Dallas apartment: **Uptown Lofts** ($2,500/mo)\n3. ✅ Saved Uptown Lofts (already in favorites)\n4. ✅ Sent the \"Dallas Apartment Recommendation\" email to Matthew\n5. ✅ Scheduled the Dec 1 flight (6 AM–11 AM, 5 hours)\n6. ✅ Canceled all 4 events on Nov 30 (the day before the flight)\nNo new follow-up message arrived during the wait. The task is fully complete — all six sub-requests have been handled and verified:\n\n1. ✅ Added Matthew Beaumont as a contact (Dallas, TX; mbeaumont@gaia2mail.com; +12145567891; age 27; chef)\n2. ✅ Most expensive Dallas apartment: **Uptown Lofts** ($2,500/mo)\n3. ✅ Saved Uptown Lofts (already in favorites)\n4. ✅ Sent the \"Dallas Apartment Recommendation\" email to Matthew\n5. ✅ Scheduled the Dec 1 flight (6 AM–11 AM, 5 hours)\n6. ✅ Canceled all 4 events on Nov 30 (the day before the flight)\n\nNothing further is required.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-dc61c37b-672a-4428-bebb-5a6722ef5ed4", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-92b5f93c-ab22-4dbf-a379-2ed8ba99e6fd"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Contacts", "function": "add_new_contact", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "first_name", "value": "Matthew", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "last_name", "value": "Beaumont", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "gender", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "age", "value": "27", "value_type": "Optional[int]"}, {"name": "nationality", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "city_living", "value": "Dallas", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "country", "value": "United States", "valu