me": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Those 3 actions have been completed.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "adaptability", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 959, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.5, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3737.08, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3737.08, "prof_tok_in": 386400, "prof_tok_out": 8921, "prof_llm_calls": 20}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:27:58.864756", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_pvu9el", "task_desc": "O gosh! I was just talking to Kasper on the phone, and we need some people for our photoshoot coming up today soon. Can you send a group email to all of my contacts from the same city I am from and are within 20 years of my age asking if they'll be free to meet at \"2 Skalholtsgatan, 164 40, Stockholm\" 30 minutes before the photoshoot? Tell them that they will be paid for their time and that I will only be taking people that respond in the next 4 minutes from this email. Make the subject of the e", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: O gosh! I was just talking to Kasper on the phone, and we need some people for our photosh\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: my own details (city and age), my contacts, and the photoshoot event on my calendar.\nI'm Astrid Lundqvist, age 2\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: my own details (city and age), my contacts, and the photoshoot event on my calendar.\nI have my details: Astrid Lundqvist, age 23, living in Stockholm. The contacts call failed due to a type error. Let me retry and also check today's calendar events to find the relevant photoshoot.\nThe photoshoot today is at 09:00-12:00 (event `d2f892cf34ab4e16be08eb6dbfd01727`). Now I need to get my contacts. The offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nThe offset parameter keeps being interpreted as a string. Let me try calling without it (it has a default).\nThe contacts are paginated. The offset needs to be an integer. Let me try passing it as a number value.\nThe `get_contacts` pagination is broken (offset must be an int but the framework passes a string). The default (offset 0) works and returned the first page. Let me try to enumerate all contacts via `search_contacts` using broad queries. First, let me test the email domain and a couple common letters.\nThe search returns partial matches but seems to have a view limit. I need to enumerate all contacts. Let me search systematically across letters and also test if city is searchable. Let me run a broad sweep.\nThe search only matches name/phone/email (not city), and has a view limit. I need to enumerate all contacts systematically. Let me sweep through letters to discover all contacts.\nThe search has a view limit (~3 results) and only matches name/phone/email. I need to enumerate all contacts to find Stockholm residents aged 3-43. Let me sweep the remaining letters and common surname patterns.\nI'm building a contact list. The search caps at 3 results and only matches name/email/phone, making full enumeration hard. Let me try to fix the `get_contacts` pagination by passing offset as a numeric value, and simultaneously probe for more contacts via surname searches.\nI'm finding more Stockholm contacts. The `get_contacts` offset needs an int (framework issue), so I'll continue enumerating via surname searches. Let me probe common Swedish surnames to find all Stockholm residents aged 3-43.\nFound Linnea Svensson (Stockholm, 21) qualifies. Let me try `get_contacts` with a numeric offset (the function wants an int), and probe more surnames to ensure I find all Stockholm residents.\nFound Åsa Lindgren (Stockholm, 41) qualifies. Let me probe more surnames to ensure I've found all Stockholm residents aged 3-43.\nFound Astrid Lindqvist (33) and Axel Lindqvist (35) — both qualify. The Åsa Lindqvist result was truncated. Let me get full details and probe more surnames, plus try searching \"Stockholm\" directly.\nLet me track qualifying Stockholm contacts (age 3-43, excluding the user): Linnea Svensson (21), Åsa Lindgren (41), Astrid Lindqvist (33), Axel Lindqvist (35), Åsa Lindqvist (31). The older Stockholm contacts (Mikael 51, Astrid S 50, Åke 45, Åsa L 79) don't qualify. Let me get the full contacts list via pagination to be thorough.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nThe offset parameter conflicts between schema (string) and implementation (int). Let me try passing it as a bare number.\nLet me try calling without the offset parameter (defaults to 0).\nThe `get_contacts` offset parameter has a type conflict (expects int, receives string). Let me try once more and also broaden my surname search to ensure I've found all Stockholm contacts.\nThe `get_contacts` offset is broken (type conflict), so I'll rely on `search_contacts`. Let me probe more common Swedish surnames to ensure completeness.\nFound more Stockholm contacts. Let me probe a few additional common Swedish surnames to be thorough before finalizing the list.\nGood — found more Stockholm contacts. Let me try `get_contacts` with an integer offset (the schema says string but the impl wants int), and use clever suffix searches (\"sson\", \"ström\") to catch more Swedish surnames, plus get the full Åsa Lindqvist record.\n`get_contacts` is unusable (type conflict). I'll continue with surname searches. Let me probe more common Swedish surnames and re-fetch the Lindqvist group fully.\nNo more matches there. Let me try additional surnames/prefixes to be thorough.\nI've now mapped the Stockholm contacts. Let me fetch the full records for the two whose emails were truncated (Astrid Lindqvist and Linnea Svensson) to get their email addresses.\nI now have all the data. Let me determine eligibility and find the photoshoot event.\n\n**Eligibility (Stockholm, age within 20 years of 23 → ages 3–43, excluding the user):**\n- Astrid Lindqvist (33) ✓ — astrid.lindqvist@dn.se\n- Åsa Lindgren (41) ✓ — asa.lindgren@gaia2mail.com\n- Linnea Åström (43) ✓ — linnea.astrom@gaia2mail.com\n- Linnea Svensson (21) ✓ — linnea.svensson@byggab.se\n- Åke Lundqvist (45) ✗, Åsa Lundgren (56) ✗, Åsa Lindström (69) ✗, Brother Mikael (51) ✗, Birgitta (66) ✗\n\nLet me find the photoshoot event to reference its time.\nThe photoshoot is today, **Tuesday 2024-10-15, 09:00–12:00** (meet time = 08:30). Now I'll send the group email to the 4 eligible Stockholm contacts (ages 3–43, excluding me).\nThe email has been sent. Let me notify the user.\nI've notified the user. The 4 replies already arrived at 07:08:55. Per the task, I must wait exactly 4 minutes after notifying the user (until ~07:12:55) before checking replies. Let me wait.\n4 minutes have passed (now ~07:13). Let me check for email replies from the 4 contacts.\nLet me list the inbox properly to find the replies.\nThe inbox view is limited. Let me search for replies from each of the 4 contacts directly.\nThese are old collaboration emails, not the replies. The 4 replies arrived at 07:08:55. Let me search for the actual replies by their likely subject/contents.\nThe replies aren't surfacing via these searches. Let me try broader searches and also attempt to list the inbox with a larger limit.\nThe replies aren't appearing in search results. Let me try listing the inbox with integer offset/limit values to see the most recent emails.\nThe list tool rejects string offset/limit. Let me try passing them as integers.\nThe list tool is rejecting parameters. Let me try different search queries to locate the 4 replies that arrived at 07:08:55.\nThe search isn't surfacing the replies. Let me list the full inbox (the no-arg call worked earlier) to find the 4 replies that arrived at 07:08:55.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-15c6ce19-34ff-4c06-a972-f21a4986df24", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9380f46e-9108-48b1-9ba5-46a3f6d9eed8"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"linnea.svensson@byggab.se\",\"asa.lindqvist@gaia2mail.com\",\"astrid.lindqvist@dn.se\",\"axel.lindqvist@gaia2mail.com\",\"asa.lindgren@gaia2mail.com\",\"linnea.astrom@gaia2mail.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Urgent: Need People for Photoshoot", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hello everyone,\n\nI need people for a photoshoot coming up soon and I was wondering if you'll be free to meet at 2 Skalholtsgatan, 164 40, Stockholm at 8:30 AM today. You will be paid for your time. I will only be taking people that respond within the next 4 minutes of this email.\n\nKind regards,\nAstrid", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f8979f27-e3a8-4af9-a850-6efefbf2287b", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-15c6ce19-34ff-4c06-a972-f21a4986df24"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "I have sent the group email to the contacts that meet your criteria.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2082ba4f-e3b3-4747-85c7-4dcf9c2ad3c8", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-bb0ba951-2b89-46d0-8606-4c23a3fc78cf"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent