{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:30:05.487853", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_2on5mg", "task_desc": "I have a networking event later today with two attendees. Can you book me a Default cab from the Malmo airport at 230 32 Malmö-Sturup to Norra Vallgatan 60, 211 22 Malmö at 5:30pm today? Also, check with both attendees of my networking event to see if they can still make it and if they want to get a taxi from the airport to the venue via sending separate emails. Let me know when you've scheduled the cab and sent the emails. If both attendees can make it, cancel the existing cab, and create the s", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: I have a networking event later today with two attendees. Can you book me a Default cab fr\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by finding the networking event and its attendees, and simultaneously book the Default cab since that's needed regardless of the attendees' responses\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\n[Prior attempt — store version v1]\nTask: I have a networking event later today with two attendees. Can you book me a Default cab fr\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by finding the networking event to identify the attendees, and simultaneously book the Default cab.\nI found the networking event with attendees **Ast\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score +70%", "response": "I'll start by finding the networking event and its attendees, and simultaneously book the Default cab since that's needed regardless of the attendees' responses.\nI found the networking event with attendees **Astrid Mikkelsen** and **Beshoy Gadallah**, and I've booked the Default cab (ride_id: 4e3d1297833d3aa85facd3dd11a81ea4).\n\nNow I need to find the contact details for both attendees so I can email them. Let me search for both contacts.\nI found both attendees. There are also notifications of new emails from both attendees. Let me get the current user's details (to sign the emails) and check the inbox for those new emails.\nThe current user is **Astrid Lundqvist** (astrid.lundqvist@gaia2mail.com). Let me retry listing emails with proper integer types.\nLet me try searching for the emails from the attendees instead.\nI found both attendees' contact details and the current user is **Astrid Lundqvist**. I also see there are already responses in the inbox, but per the task I need to first send separate emails to both attendees asking if they can still make it and if they want a taxi from the airport to the venue.\n\nLet me send those two separate emails now.\nThe recipients parameter needs to be a list. Let me retry with list format.\nBoth emails have been sent. The Default cab is booked (ride_id: 4e3d1297833d3aa85facd3dd11a81ea4). I noticed there are already responses in the inbox from both attendees. Let me notify the user of the checkpoint and then check the responses.\nI've notified the user and the cab is booked with emails sent. Now I need to check the attendees' responses to decide the next steps. I already saw responses in the inbox, but let me wait for any notifications and confirm the latest responses.\nNo new notifications. I already have both attendees' responses from the inbox:\n\n- **Astrid Mikkelsen**: \"Sure thing! I am still attending, count me in for the taxi, too!\"\n- **Beshoy Gadallah**: \"Yes, I can still make it and I'll grab a taxi with you guys as planned.\"\n\nBoth attendees **can make it** and want the taxi. Per the task, I need to:\n1. Cancel the existing Default cab\n2. Create the same journey with Premium cab type\n3. Email both attendees separately with the new cab details\n\nLet me cancel the existing Default cab first.\nThe Default cab is cancelled. Now let me book the same journey with Premium cab type.\nThe Premium cab is booked (ride_id: 79245e0d4f85d5715658687d08c9c032). Now let me email both attendees separately with the new cab details.\nAll steps are complete. Both attendees confirmed they can make it, so I cancelled the Default cab and booked a Premium cab, then emailed both with the new details. Let me send the final summary.\nThe task is fully complete. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n1. **Default cab booked** from Malmö-Sturup airport to Norra Vallgatan 60, 211 22 Malmö at 5:30pm today.\n\n2. **Check-in emails sent** separately to both networking event attendees (Astrid Mikkelsen and Beshoy Gadallah) asking if they could still attend and if they wanted a taxi from the airport to the venue.\n\n3. **Both attendees confirmed** they can make it and want the taxi.\n\n4. **Cab upgraded to Premium** — cancelled the Default cab and rebooked the same journey as a Premium cab (Ride ID: 79245e0d4f85d5715658687d08c9c032).\n\n5. **Follow-up emails sent** separately to both attendees confirming I'll see them later, including the new Premium cab details.\n\nAll sub-requests in the task have been completed.\nNo new message arrived during the wait period. The task has been fully completed:\n\n- ✅ Default cab booked (then cancelled since both attendees confirmed)\n- ✅ Separate check-in emails sent to both attendees\n- ✅ Both attendees confirmed they can attend and want the taxi\n- ✅ Default cab cancelled and rebooked as Premium (Ride ID: 79245e0d4f85d5715658687d08c9c032)\n- ✅ Separate follow-up emails sent to both attendees with the new Premium cab details\n\nThere are no further actions required. The task is complete.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-f916c9ac-e63e-4919-b932-5e395bb1acc2", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9ba0aa71-9148-4c90-b22b-5dc2073b3536"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"a