d Ma, Luísa Sousa, and Lianying Wang. Let me send the emails to each.\nThe recipients need to be a list. Let me retry.\nAll three emails have been sent. Now I'll notify the user as required, then wait 2 minutes (simulated) before checking for responses.\nEmails sent and user notified. Now I'll wait exactly 2 minutes (as instructed) before checking for responses.\n2 minutes have passed. Now let me check the responses from the three friends.\nLet me try calling without the offset/limit parameters since they have defaults.\nI have the responses:\n- **Khalid Ma**: \"Absolutely! Count me in!\" → CAN attend\n- **Luísa Sousa**: \"Sorry Astrid, I won't be able to make it...\" → CANNOT attend\n- **Lianying Wang**: \"Yes! I'd love to catch up.\" → CAN attend\n\nThat's 2 or more who can attend, so I'll proceed. This Friday is 2024-10-18. Let me add the calendar event, book the cab (30 min prior = 21:30), and send replies to Khalid and Lianying.\nCalendar event and cab booked. Now let me send email replies to Khalid and Lianying (the two who can attend), with the address and excitement. Luísa said she can't come, so no email to her.\nAll sub-tasks are complete:\n\n1. ✅ Sent dinner invitation emails to the 3 friends who are participants in \"A Conversation Across Cultures\" (Khalid Ma, Luísa Sousa, Lianying Wang — excluding Astrid, the current user).\n2. ✅ Notified the user when sent and to whom.\n3. ✅ Waited exactly 2 minutes after the notification.\n4. ✅ Checked responses: Khalid (yes), Lianying (yes), Luísa (no) → 2 or more can attend.\n5. ✅ Added a 2-hour \"Dinner with Friends\" calendar event for Friday 2024-10-18 22:00–00:00 at Uppsala Castle.\n6. ✅ Booked a Premium cab from home (Östermalmsgatan 12, Stockholm) to Uppsala Castle, 753 30 Uppsala, at 21:30 (30 min prior).\n7. ✅ Sent email replies to Khalid and Lianying with the address and excitement; no email sent to Luísa (she declined).\n\nThe task is fully done. Stopping.\nNo new follow-up message arrived. The task is fu