{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:32:41.048237", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_jg8s6c", "task_desc": "Move the social media management on my calendar from Oct 16th to Oct 18th, keeping all the other details the same, and order me the Ravensburger German Tourists puzzle made from recycled paper, I have something planned for that meeting. After buying it, please delete my contact from the United States. Be careful not to delete the wrong contact, let me know if something is not clear.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Move the social media management on my calendar from Oct 16th to Oct 18th, keeping all the\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Move the \"social media management\" calendar event from Oct 16 to Oct 18 (keeping other details the same)\n2. Order the\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score -35%", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Move the \"social media management\" calendar event from Oct 16 to Oct 18 (keeping other details the same)\n2. Order the \"Ravensburger German Tourists puzzle made from recycled paper\"\n3. After buying it, delete my contact from the United States (carefully, to avoid the wrong contact)\n4. Let you know if anything is unclear\n\nLet me start by gathering information in parallel.\nI found several \"Social Media Management\" events but they're all in August. The task references Oct 16th, so let me query that specific date range. The puzzle search returned nothing, so let me try a broader search. And I need to see all contacts to find the one from the United States.\nI found the \"Social Media Management\" event on Oct 16th (event_id: 15a8031c0f1e4e6c867b93b08a5d365b, 14:00–16:00). The puzzle search for \"Ravensburger\" didn't show \"German Tourists\" yet, and the contacts offset needs to be an integer. Let me proceed with the calendar move and continue searching.\nThe calendar event was deleted. Now I'll re-add it on Oct 18th with the same details. I also found the puzzle — \"Ravensburger 17004 German Tourists - 3000 Piece Puzzle\" with a Recycled Paper variant (item_id faacc5243a374151bf972ccfc1f84bd5, available). Let me add the calendar event and continue listing contacts (offset must be an integer).\nThe calendar event was successfully moved to Oct 18th. The contacts offset keeps erroring — it seems to require an integer type. Let me try passing it as a number.\nThe offset parameter keeps being rejected. Let me try calling without the offset argument to get the default page, and also try the search function to find US contacts.\nThe default `get_contacts` returns only 2 contacts (there's a view limit), and the offset is being rejected as a string. Let me try passing offset as a numeric value instead.\nThe offset is being rejected because it's passed as a string but the implementation requires an integer. Let me try passing it as a numeric value directly.\nThe offset parameter is being rejected due to a type mismatch in the framework. Let me try passing it as a bare numeric value, and also try searching contacts by other means.\nThe offset parameter has a type bug in the framework (it requires an int but receives a string). Let me try a different approach to find US contacts — searching by the US phone country code \"+1\", and also try the search with other queries.\nI found the puzzle and the calendar move is done. Now, regarding the contacts: searching for US phone numbers (+1) returned **two** contacts from the United States:\n- **Astrid Kjær** (contact_id: 3e3a53d243b2462ab1d29e1d33397591) — Amherst, MA, United States\n- **Vasco Oliveira** (contact_id: 714a6f1325bf4df598a96fef298ac5e1) — Punxsutawney, PA, United States\n\nThis is ambiguous (the task says \"my contact from the United States\" — singular, but there are two). Per your instruction to be careful and flag unclear things, I'll hold off on deleting until I clarify. But first, let me complete the puzzle order (the prerequisite). Let me add the Recycled Paper variant to the cart and check out.\nSame type issue with quantity. Let me pass it as a numeric value.\nThe quantity parameter has the same type issue. Let me try without specifying quantity (default is 1).\nThe puzzle was added to the cart. Let me verify the cart contents and then check out.\nThe cart has the correct item: Ravensburger German Tourists 3000-piece puzzle, Recycled Paper variant, $39.95. Let me check out.\nThe puzzle order is complete (order ID: 4008acbcde6d48b08424d5d1b3769ee6). \n\nNow, regarding the contact deletion: the task says \"delete my contact from the United States\" (singular), but my search for US phone numbers (+1) returned **two** contacts in the United States. Before deleting anything, I want to be thorough and make sure I've found all US contacts. Let me run a few more searches to confirm the full set.\nI've completed the first two parts of the task. However, the third part — deleting \"my contact from the United States\" — is ambiguous, and per your instruction to be careful and flag unclear things, I need to clarify before deleting anything.\n\nHere's my status:\n- ✅ **Calendar:** Moved \"Social Media Management\" from Oct 16 (14:00–16:00) to **Oct 18 (14:00–16:00)**, keeping all other details identical (tag: Work, location: Home Office, description: \"Manage social media accounts and respond to comments\").\n- ✅ **Puzzle order:** Ordered the **Ravensburger German Tourists 3000-piece puzzle (Recycled Paper variant)** — order ID `4008acbcde6d48b08424d5d1b3769ee6`, $39.95.\n- ⚠️ **Contact deletion:** I found **two** contacts in the United States, not one:\n  1. **Astrid Kjær** (id `3e3a53d243b2462ab1d29e1d33397591`) — Amherst, MA, United States\n  2. **Vasco Oliveira** (id `714a6f1325bf4df598a96fef298ac5e1`) — Punxsutawney, PA, United States\n\nSince you said \"delete **my contact** from the United States\" (singular) but there are two US-based contacts, I don't want to delete the wrong one. Let me confirm with you.\nI've sent the clarification request. Now I'll wait for the user's response before deleting any contact.\nNo response was received within the wait window. I've completed the two unambiguous parts of the task and flagged the ambiguous contact-deletion step as instructed. Since deleting the wrong contact would be a mistake, I will not proceed with the deletion until you clarify which US contact to remove.\n\nHere's the final status:\n\n- ✅ **Calendar:** \"Social Media Management\" moved from Oct 16 → **Oct 18 (14:00–16:00)**, all other details unchanged.\n- ✅ **Puzzle:** Ravensburger German Tourists 3000-piece puzzle (Recycled Paper) ordered — Order ID `4008acbcde6d48b08424d5d1b3769ee6`, $39.95.\n- ⏳ **Contact deletion (pending your input):** Two US-based contacts exist — **Astrid Kjær** (`3e3a53d243b2462ab1d29e1d33397591`, Amherst MA) and **Vasco Oliveira** (`714a6f1325bf4df598a96fef298ac5e1`, Punxsutawney PA). Please tell me which to delete (or both), and I'll take care of it right away.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-def9ca5d-e917-4086-8a2a-4d7aaf339e2c", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-1d48775f-7fce-4fbf-8316-3eaf97143e0d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Social Media Management", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-18 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "Work", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "valu