ge_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "There are two contacts from the United States. Which one would you like to delete?", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.8, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "ambiguity", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 590, "wc_served": [1.0, 1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.1, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3425.86, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3425.86, "prof_tok_in": 367356, "prof_tok_out": 12164, "prof_llm_calls": 19}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:32:51.717244", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_mq2acb", "task_desc": "What is the age of the person who attended the most \"dinner with friends\" events (excluding myself) in the months of August, September and October 2024? If there is a tie, choose the one who sent me an email most recently.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: What is the age of the person who attended the most \"dinner with friends\" events (excludin\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by understanding the task. I need to:\n1. Find \"dinner with friends\" events in Aug, Sep, Oct 2024\n2. Identify attendees (excluding myself)\n3. Count ev\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll start by analyzing this task. I need to:\n1. Find \"dinner with friends\" events in Aug, Sep, Oct 2024\n2. Identify attendees (excluding myself)\n3. Count events per person\n4. Find the person who attended the most (tie-break by most recent email)\n5. Get that person's age\n\nLet me begin by searching for these events.\nThe search returned some events but was truncated. Let me get the full list of events in the date range with proper integer limit.\nThe parameters need to be integers. Let me retry.\nLet me try without the optional integer parameters.\nThe default limit returned only 10 events. I need to paginate. The integer parameters failed when passed as strings. Let me try passing them as actual numbers.\nThe integer parameters are being rejected. Let me use search instead to capture all dinner events. Let me search with different terms.\nThe search results are truncated in display. I need to see all dinner events. Let me try paginating the calendar with integer parameters written as numbers, and also get events by tag.\nThe `get_calendar_events_from_to` with offset/limit fails on type. Let me try passing them as bare numbers (no quotes) and also get the \"Personal\" tag events.\nThe offset/limit parameters have a type mismatch. The search and tag queries work but results get truncated in display. Let me try more specific searches to capture all dinner events. I'll search the exact title and also by individual months.\nThe search results are being truncated in display. I need to capture all dinner events. Let me try searching by the specific description variants to get smaller, complete result sets.\nThe search results are being truncated in display. I need a complete list of dinner events. Let me search by specific attendees to find all their dinner events, which will help me capture the September/October ones I haven't seen yet.\nThe search results are being truncated in display. I'll use date-filtered searches per month to get complete, smaller result sets. Let me search \"Dinner with Friends\" within each month's range.\nThe search tool truncates display. Let me try `get_calendar_events_from_to` with integer offset/limit values (the earlier failure was due to string type). I'll write them as numbers.\nThe pagination parameters have a type bug, and search truncates display. Let me work around this by reading specific events and using targeted searches. First, let me identify \"myself\" and read the truncated 08-26 event, plus search for more dinner events via distinctive description fragments.\nI now know \"myself\" is Astrid Lundqvist (age 23). I've found dinner events in Aug and Sep. I still need to find any October \"Dinner with Friends\" events, which were truncated in the broad search. Let me search by individual attendees to discover all their dinner events, especially October ones.\nI've found dinner events in August (7) and September (1), but I need to confirm October events. The search results are truncated, so let me try `get_calendar_events_from_to` with just the date range (using defaults) to get a complete list, and also search for October-specific dinner events.\nThe `get_calendar_events_from_to` works without offset/limit (default limit 10), but display truncates. Let me try passing offset/limit as integer literals (no quotes) to paginate through all events.\nThe pagination has a type bug I can't work around. Let me confirm there are no October dinner events by searching for generic attendees (\"Friend 1\"/\"Friend 2\") and doing a broad \"Dinner\" search to catch any I might have missed.\nI've now confirmed the complete set of \"Dinner with Friends\" events in Aug–Sep–Oct 2024. Let me tally the attendees (excluding myself, Astrid Lundqvist):\n\n**August:**\n- Aug 5: Astrid Lundqvist, Ebba Lindström, Linnea Åström\n- Aug 8: Åke Svensson, Astrid Kjær\n- Aug 11: Åke Svensson, Astrid Kjær\n- Aug 15: Astrid Lundqvist, Akira Lundström, Linnea Åström\n- Aug 18: Astrid Lundqvist, Akira Lundström, Linnea Åström\n- Aug 19: Åsa Lindström, Kirstine Rasmussen\n- Aug 26: Astrid Lundqvist, Friend 1, Friend 2\n\n**September:**\n- Sep 10: Astrid Lundqvist, Åsa Lindström, Emil Rasmussen\n\n**October:** None found.\n\nCounts (excluding myself): Linnea Åström = **3** (most), Åke Svensson = 2, Astrid Kjær = 2, Akira Lundström = 2, Åsa Lindström = 2, others = 1. No tie. The winner is **Linnea Åström**. Let me get her age.\nI have all the information needed. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**\"Dinner with Friends\" events (Aug–Sep–Oct 2024), attendees excluding myself (Astrid Lundqvist):**\n- Aug 5: Ebba Lindström, Linnea Åström\n- Aug 8: Åke Svensson, Astrid Kjær\n- Aug 11: Åke Svensson, Astrid Kjær\n- Aug 15: Akira Lundström, Linnea Åström\n- Aug 18: Akira Lundström, Linnea Åström\n- Aug 19: Åsa Lindström, Kirstine Rasmussen\n- Aug 26: Friend 1, Friend 2\n- Sep 10: Åsa Lindström, Emil Rasmussen\n- October: none\n\n**Counts:** Linnea Åström = **3** (the most), Åke Svensson = 2, Astrid Kjær = 2, Akira Lundström = 2, Åsa Lindström = 2, others = 1. No tie, so the tiebreaker isn't needed.\n\nThe winner is **Linnea Åström**, whose age is **43**.\nThe task is complete. \n\n**Answer: Linnea Åström is 43 years old.**\n\nShe attended the most \"Dinner with Friends\" events (3) in August–September–October 2024 (Aug 5, Aug 15, Aug 18), excluding yourself (Astrid Lundqvist). No tie occurred, so the email tiebreaker wasn't required, and there were no such events in October.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-eef8f0e6-2a6d-4a1f-ad02-131c4c1dc6a6", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-68c8eee4-a8bc-4a0e-a9fd-a8ab77ee06a4"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "43", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "search", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 642, "wc_served": [1.0, 1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3614.67, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3614.67, "prof_tok_in": 466412, "prof_tok_out": 25624, "prof_llm_calls": 21}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:33:09.530386", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_ti5ym5", "task_desc": "Please add Remus Lupin as a new contact. His phone number is +46734567732 and his email is remuslupin.moony@gaia2mail.com. Add 'Malmö' as his city, 'Sweden' as his country, and 'SEO Specialist' as his Job. My realtor is about to list my property called 'Malmö Beach Bungalow' for rent. As soon as the listing goes up, please do the following:\nSend all the property details to Remus in an email and request him to write a summary of the property's features fully optimized for search engines. Also, CC", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Please add Remus Lupin as a new contact. His phone number is +46734567732 and his email is\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this complex task into sub-requests and work through them systematically. Let me start with the independent actions I can do immediately, plus check \nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score -5%", "response": "I'll break this complex task into sub-requests and work through them systematically. Let me start with the independent actions I can do immediately, plus check the state of things I'll need.\n\nLet me begin by:\n1. Adding Remus Lupin as a contact\n2. Searching for the property listing\n3. Finding the \"Influencer Gathering\" calendar event\n4. Finding the construction company owner and executive assistant contacts\nRemus Lupin added successfully. The \"Influencer Gathering\" event was found (attendees: Astrid Lindqvist, Axel Lindqvist). The property listing isn't up yet, and my contact searches for \"construction\" and \"executive assistant\" returned empty. Let me look at all contacts to find the construction company owner and executive assistant, since the search terms may not match exactly.\nThe contacts list is paginated. Let me get more contacts to find the construction company owner and executive assistant. I'll try scrolling with an offset.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me try passing it as a number value.\nThe offset parameter has a type mismatch. Let me try passing it as a numeric value without quotes.\nThe offset parameter has a type mismatch in this interface. Let me re-call `get_contacts` with no offset to see the full first page, and also try searching contacts by other likely terms.\nThe `get_contacts` pagination is blocked by a type error, and `search_contacts` only matches name/phone/email (not job). I need to enumerate contacts to find the construction company owner and executive assistant. Let me search using common letters to enumerate the full contact list.\nThe search only matches name/phone/email, not job, and `get_contacts` pagination is broken. I need to enumerate all contacts to find the construction company owner and executive assistant. Let me search with many letters to enumerate the full contact list.\nThe search returns a capped subset, making full enumeration hard. Let me search for the \"Influencer Gathering\" attendees (Lindqvist) to get their contact info for the CC, and check the property listing status. I'll also try the InternalContacts app which may have working pagination.\nThe \"Influencer Gathering\" attendees are **Astrid Lindqvist** (Music Journalist, astrid.lindqvist@dn.se) and **Axel Lindqvist** (Marketing Manager, axel.lindqvist@gaia2mail.com) — these are my CC contacts. The property \"Malmö Beach Bungalow\" is not yet listed (the RentAFlat catalog shows other Malmö properties but not this one).\n\nI still need to find the construction company owner and executive assistant contacts. Since search is capped and `get_contacts` pagination is broken, let me enumerate contacts via single-letter searches.\nI've found the Influencer Gathering attendees (Astrid & Axel Lindqvist) for the CC. The contact search is capped at ~3 results, making full enumeration hard, and `get_contacts` pagination is broken. I still need to find the construction company owner and executive assistant. Let me explore the Messages and Calendar apps, which may reference these contacts by name.\nThe Calendar query for Sept 1–Oct 15 didn't surface \"Influencer Gathering\" yet. Let me search for that event specifically, and retry Messages with an integer offset (the backend wants int, not str).\nConfirmed: \"Influencer Gathering\" (Sept 24) attendees are **Astrid Lindqvist** and **Axel Lindqvist** — my CC contacts. \n\nThe Messages tool needs an integer offset. Let me retry with a numeric value, and search for the construction company owner and executive assistant by job keywords.\nThe Messages tool rejects the offset (framework stringifies it). Let me try without offset, and test whether contact search covers job/description fields (searching known job terms). This will tell me how to locate the construction owner and executive assistant.\nKey finding: contact search only matches first name, last name, phone, and email (not job/description) — that's why \"CEO\"/\"Architect\"/\"Influencer\" returned empty. The search is also capped at 3 results, so I can't fully enumerate via search. \n\nThe `InternalContacts` app returned a paginated list. Let me enumerate it fully to find the construction company owner and executive assistant, and also try the Messages search.\nInteresting — `InternalContacts__get_contacts(offset=\"0\")` worked once but non-zero offsets fail with a type error. Let me re-test offset \"0\" and try the main `Contacts` app to see if it has working pagination or a larger default set.\nThe contact pagination is flaky and search only covers name/phone/email. Let me try `InternalContacts__get_contacts` with no offset argument (as the first call worked), and probe the Messages app via search and no-arg listing.\nThe `InternalContacts` list returns only 2 per call and offset pagination is broken (type error). I need another way to find the construction company owner and executive assistant. \n\nFirst, let me locate the property \"Malmö Beach Bungalow\" in RentAFlat (needed for bedrooms, address, and details across multiple steps), and probe contact enumeration.\nFound the property: **Malmö Beach Bungalow**, 5 bedrooms, address **Beleshoegsvaegen 50B, Malmö, Sweden**. So I need 5 wall decals.\n\nThe contact list is capped at 2 per call and offset pagination is broken. Let me try the main `Contacts` app's `get_contacts` (no offset) to see if it returns more, and search for the construction owner / executive assistant by likely names.\nFound the property: **Malmö Beach Bungalow** — 5 bedrooms, address **Beleshoegsvaegen 50B, Malmö, Sweden**. Remus Lupin is already added (contact_id `04af3af7bea91a5ebe08dc20b83f2186`).\n\nThe contact list is capped at 2/page and offset pagination is broken, and search only matches name/phone/email. I'll enumerate contacts by searching letters that do **not** appear in the first-3 default results (Søren, Astrid Jensen, Åke), which will surface the other contacts including the construction owner and executive assistant.\nI'm building the contact list. So far I've found 21 contacts but still need the \"construction company owner\" and \"executive assistant\". The search matches name/phone/email substrings and returns up to 3. Let me search the remaining letters to surface all contacts.\nI've found 21 contacts but 4 have truncated job descriptions (Aurélie Dupont, Khurram Saeed, Jianyu Liang, Jianzhi Liang). The construction owner / executive assistant are likely among these. Let me get their full details.\nI've found 21 contacts but the construction company owner and executive assistant aren't among them, and the search is capped at 3 results (biased toward default contacts). Let me test whether `get_contacts` offset actually works with different values, and get Aurélie Dupont's full details.\nThe offset must be an integer. Let me enumerate all contacts properly with integer offsets.\nThe offset parameter requires an integer type that the harness isn't passing correctly. Let me instead search for the remaining contacts by name to get their full details (jobs). I'll search the names I haven't fully identified.\nThe search returns only a capped subset and doesn't cover all contacts reliably. The construction company owner and executive assistant are likely among the contacts with truncated job descriptions (Liang Chen, Zhang Wei, Wei Chen, Chen Zhang, Zhang Chen, Liang Wei, Chen Liang, Wei Liang). I need their contact_ids. Let me search for these specific full names.\nThe search is capped at 3 results and `get_contacts` offset is broken (type error). The construction owner and executive assistant must be among the contacts whose jobs I haven't fully seen — possibly Mateo Rossi, Elena Petrova, Ridho Santoso, or the truncated Liang/Chen/Wei contacts. Let me check InternalContacts (a separate contact store) and get details for the remaining named contacts.\nImportant discovery: there are two contact stores. `InternalContacts` contains the actual user (Astrid Lundqvist, is_user:true, a Social Media Influencer) plus others like Jianhua Wang. The `Contacts` app has 21 generic cont", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d93d30c2-6782-494b-94ca-58afb982d08d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-7c445f75-e66b-4695-9066-a718f8a78139"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Contacts", "function": "add_new_contact", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "first_name", "value": "Remus", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "last_name", "value": "Lupin", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "gender", "value": "Male", "value_type"