{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:41:34.433093", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_22_52pwi3", "task_desc": "Tell me only the name of the youngest person I have emailed this month who is not in any of my Messages conversations but is in at least one in Chats. If there is a tie, choose the one based on first name in alphabetical order.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Tell me only the name of the youngest person I have emailed this month who is not in any o\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll work through this step by step. Let me start by understanding the time context and gathering the data I need.\nThe current time is 2024-10-15, so \"this mont\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll work through this step by step. Let me start by gathering the data I need: emails sent this month, Messages conversations, and Chats conversations.\nThe parameters need to be integers. Let me retry.\nLet me try without the offset/limit parameters.\nThe default calls returned truncated results. Let me get the full picture. The email list seems to show only 2 sent emails but content was cut off. Let me verify the full sent email list and get details. Let me also try searching emails to ensure I capture all sent emails this month.\nThe SENT folder shows 2 emails. Let me confirm there aren't more and get the second email's details. Let me also check the contacts to understand the people involved.\nThe SENT folder has 2 emails this month (October 2024). Let me get the second email's details and check the timestamps. I also need to see all conversations in Messages and Chats. Let me try passing integer parameters properly.\nThe integer parameters keep failing. Let me work with the default calls and gather contacts. The SENT folder has 2 emails this month to: augustin.moreno-sanchez@unm.edu and mehmetozdemir65@gaia2mail.com. Let me find these people in contacts and get current user details.\nI've identified the two people I emailed this month (October 2024):\n1. **Augustín Moreno-Sánchez** (age 61) — augustin.moreno-sanchez@unm.edu\n2. **Mehmet Özdemir** (age 65) — mehmetozdemir65@gaia2mail.com\n\nNow I need to determine who is in Messages vs Chats. Let me map the conversation participants. The Messages conversation has participant +15037654321, and the Chats conversation has two internal UUIDs. Let me identify them.\nThe Messages conversation is with Nalani Jensen, and the Chats conversation is with Çağla Öztürk. But I need to check ALL conversations, not just the most recent. Let me look up the user IDs for the two emailed people (Augustín and Mehmet) in both Messages and Chats, and list their conversations.\nKey findings:\n- **Augustín Moreno-Sánchez**: NOT found in Messages, but found in Chats (id `b9b3a04d-d7f3-4245-95b0-c26bf434342d`)\n- **Mehmet Özdemir**: found in Messages (id `+902125558236`), NOT found in Chats\n\nThis suggests Augustín qualifies (not in Messages, in Chats) and Mehmet does not. But let me verify thoroughly by checking actual conversations for each person in both systems.\nI now have a clear picture. Let me verify the second sent email's timestamp to confirm it's this month, and double-check there are no other sent emails. Let me also confirm Augustín's Chats conversation is real (already confirmed above).\nI found a discrepancy — the search returned a **third** sent email to `luisapimentel74@gaia2mail.com` that wasn't in the SENT folder list. Let me investigate this carefully, as it may be in a different folder or the SENT list was incomplete.\nI found a discrepancy: the search returned a sent email to Luísa Pimentel that wasn't in the SENT folder list. The `list_emails` may have a default limit truncating results. Let me get the complete SENT list with a higher limit and verify the Luísa sent email.\nThe search results are limited per query, making it hard to be sure I've found ALL sent emails. The `list_emails` default truncates to 2. Let me search comprehensively using the sender's email and distinctive terms to find every sent email this month.\nThe search tool consistently returns only 2 results per query, and `list_emails` default truncates to 2. I need the complete SENT list. The integer-parameter error suggests the tool wants actual ints. Let me try passing integers directly.\nThe search tool caps results at 2 per query, and `list_emails` pagination fails on the int-type error. I've discovered additional sent emails to Pimentel addresses. Let me try `list_emails` with integer values once more, and in parallel surface the other sent emails via unique search terms and find the Pimentel contacts' ages.\nI've now found the complete picture of sent emails. The search returns only the 2 most recent matches per query, but by peeling back layers I've identified the 5 most recent sent emails:\n- **Oct 12**: Augustín Moreno-Sánchez (unm.edu)\n- **Oct 11**: Mehmet Özdemir (gaia2mail)\n- **Oct 2**: Luísa Pimentel (luisapimentel74@gaia2mail.com)\n- Sep 24: Nádia Silva (nadiasilva@gaia2mail.com) — NOT October\n- Sep 5: Luís Pimentel (lpimentel@author.com) — NOT October\n\nSo the **October** email recipients are: Augustín (61), Mehmet (65), Luísa (74). The 4th most recent is Sep 24, confirming exactly 3 October recipients.\n\nNow I must verify the Messages/Chats condition for each. Let me check Luísa in both systems, and get the full list of Messages and Chats conversations to be thorough.\nI've now confirmed the key facts:\n- **Augustín Moreno-Sánchez**: NOT in Messages (lookup empty), IS in Chats (conversation confirmed) → **qualifies**\n- **Mehmet Özdemir**: IS in Messages (conversation exists), NOT in Chats → does not qualify\n- **Luísa Pimentel**: IS in Messages (id `+351968123456`), NOT in Chats (lookup returned only \"Luís Pimentel\" and \"Luísa Pereira de Sousa\", not her) → does not qualify\n\nThe October email recipients are Augustín (61), Mehmet (65), Luísa (74). But the search tool only returns 2 results per query, so I must verify I haven't missed a 4th October email (which could be to a younger qualifier). Let me run distinctive searches to enumerate all sent emails and close any gaps.\nI'm discovering there are MANY more sent emails than the top 3. The search returns only the 2 most recent matches per query, so I'm peeling them back layer by layer. I've now found recipients: Augustín (Oct 12), Mehmet (Oct 11), Luísa (Oct 2), Nádia (Sep 24), Luís Pimentel (Sep 5), plus **Deniz Öztürk**, **Citlali**, and **Luís Faria** whose timestamps I need. Let me get their exact timestamps via distinctive searches.\nI'm finding many more sent emails than expected. The search returns only the 2 most recent matches, so I'm peeling them back. Let me track the October emails found so far:\n- Oct 12: Augustín Moreno-Sánchez (qualifies: NOT in Messages, IS in Chats)\n- Oct 11: Mehmet Özdemir (IS in Messages → no)\n- Oct 11: Mehmet Öztürk (need to check)\n- Oct 5: Deniz Öztürk (need to check)\n- Oct 2: Luísa Pimentel (IS in Messages → no)\n- Evelyn Nakamura (timestamp unknown)\n\nI must find ALL October emails and check each. Let me get Evelyn's timestamp and the candidate details, plus search for any other October recipients.\nThis is a large email set. The search returns only the 2 most recent matches, so I must enumerate systematically. Let me get the full contacts list (the universe of people) and the remaining timestamps for Ryder Nakamura and Evelyn Nakamura.\nThe contacts `get_contacts` also fails on the int-type error. Let me enumerate contacts via search and get the remaining timestamps/ages. I've found 6 October emails so far (Augustín, Mehmet Özdemir, Mehmet Öztürk, Deniz Öztürk, Luísa, Kaia). Let me find any others and get candidate details.\nI've found 6 October emails so far: Augustín (Oct 12), Mehmet Özdemir (Oct 11), Mehmet Öztürk (Oct 11), Deniz Öztürk (Oct 5), Kaia (Oct 6), Luísa (Oct 2). I still need timestamps for Aurélia Silva Castro and Xóchitl Hernández, and the full contacts list. Let me also get the contacts properly with an integer offset.\nMore October emails keep appearing (Luís Pereira Oct 9, Luísa Oliveira unknown). I need to be systematic. Let me get the full contacts list (to map emails→ages) and find remaining timestamps. The `get_contacts` failed on offset type — let me try without it.\nThe contacts list is paginated (only 4 shown). But more importantly, I should get the COMPLETE sent-email list directly rather than relying on search (which only returns 2 matches). Let me list all SENT emails.\nThe `list_emails`/`get_contacts` have small default view limits and the int offset param fails, so I'll rely on `search_emails` (returns 2 most recent matches). I've now identified 7 October sent emails. Let me get the ages of the remaining October candidates and confirm ", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-11c51de6-cc8d-4fdc-920a-40f82f1cf219", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-9eefb27a-e169-47e6-938e-ebc95157d849"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Augustín Moreno-Sánchez", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "search", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 602, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_prov