nt-USER-d5c54aaf-a8d3-4e83-8873-b39f01814e75"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "delete_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "696b7978e34c4d4cab203becefad1b83", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "execution", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 654, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 4131.67, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 4131.67, "prof_tok_in": 282232, "prof_tok_out": 31557, "prof_llm_calls": 15}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:49:42.358807", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_1juxxq", "task_desc": "Search for a condo under $3000 with 4 bedrooms that's on the ground floor and also a square footage larger than 1500 and save it to my favorites list. Share the amenity details of this saved property with Astrid via email. Be sure that you send the email to the correct Astrid, the one who will attend at least 5 hours of events in total next month. Also, remove all properties I have saved in Uppsala. In case of any issues, ask me with possible answers.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Search for a condo under $3000 with 4 bedrooms that's on the ground floor and also a squar\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Search for a condo under $3000, 4 bedrooms, ground floor, >1500 sqft, and save it to favorites.\n2. Identify the corre\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score +5%", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Search for a condo under $3000, 4 bedrooms, ground floor, >1500 sqft, and save it to favorites.\n2. Identify the correct Astrid (who will attend ≥5 hours of events next month).\n3. Email that Astrid the amenity details of the saved property.\n4. Remove all saved properties in Uppsala.\n\nLet me start by searching for the condo and investigating the Astrid candidates in parallel.\nThe search failed due to type error (max_price needs to be numeric). Let me fix that and get the full list of November events to compute hours per Astrid.\nThe parameters need numeric types, not strings. Let me retry with proper numeric values.\nThe numeric parameters are being passed as strings and rejected. Let me work around this: I'll list all apartments and filter manually, and use search to find events for each Astrid. From the November events I can see two Astrids so far: \"Astrid Lundqvist\" and \"Astrid Svensson\".\nThe search_events returns all-time events, not just November. I need November-specific events. Let me retry the date-range query without the problematic offset/limit params (using defaults), and also get the full apartment list.\nThe apartment list display got truncated. Let me try the search tool with only the string-based filters (property_type and floor_level) to get a manageable, non-truncated list, and also get the rest of the November events.\nThe search with string filters works. I now have ground-floor condos but the list is truncated. I need to see all of them to find one with 4 bedrooms and >1500 sqft. Let me get all condos, and split November into two halves to capture all events (the default limit truncates the display).\nThe display truncates results. I need to narrow searches so I can see all matches. Let me search condos with 4 bedrooms specifically, and break November into weekly windows to capture all events.\nThe display truncates long results, and numeric filters are being rejected as strings. Let me try passing the numeric filters as bare numbers (not quoted) to see if the type validation passes.\nThe numeric filters are unusable (framework sends strings). The display truncates large result sets. Let me enumerate all condos by city location to see every condo, including ones beyond the truncation limit.\nI now have a clearer picture. The 4-bedroom condos I've found are all Penthouse (Stockholm Waterfront, Stockholm Söder, Stockholm Sanctuary, Lund Luxury Living). I need to check the remaining Stockholm condos (truncated) and other cities for any 4-bedroom GROUND FLOOR condo. Let me check the rest of Stockholm and other cities.\nI now have comprehensive ground-floor condo data. Key finding: the only 4-bedroom **ground-floor** condo is \"Lund Stadsparken\" (1300 sqft — fails the >1500 requirement). All 4-bedroom condos with >1500 sqft are Penthouses. Let me verify completeness by enumerating Stockholm condos by floor level (ground floor was empty) and confirm I haven't missed any 4-bedroom condos.\nI now have nearly all Stockholm condos. The truncated \"Stockholm City Center\" needs checking, and I want to ensure I haven't missed any 4-bedroom condos. Let me get its details and verify the complete set.\nI now have the complete condo picture. Critically, **no condo satisfies all four criteria** (under $3000, 4BR, ground floor, >1500 sqft). The only 4-bedroom ground-floor condo is \"Lund Stadsparken\" (1300 sqft — fails the >1500 requirement), and all 4BR condos with >1500 sqft are Penthouses.\n\nBefore I ask you about this, let me gather the remaining info I need: the saved apartments (for Uppsala removal) and the complete November event data to correctly identify \"Astrid.\" Let me get the saved list and search for all Astrid events.\nThe saved list is truncated. I need the complete saved list (to find all Uppsala ones) and the complete November Astrid events. Let me use date-filtered event search and per-city saved searches.\nThe framework converts all args to strings, so bool/date filters fail. I'll work around: get all November events directly (to identify Astrid by November attendance) and enumerate Uppsala properties by type to find all saved ones. Let me batch these.\nThe `limit` arg must be a true int (framework sends strings), so I'll omit it. For Uppsala, only Apartment and Condo types exist (others empty). I've found saved Uppsala properties: Uppsala Studentboende, Uppsala Oasis, Uppsala Upscale. Let me confirm Uppsala Oasis and Uppsala City Living details, and get November events.\nI have November events but the list is truncated. I need the complete November set to compute each Astrid's total hours. Let me page through with offset.\nThe `offset`/`limit` args must be true ints (framework sends strings → error), and the full-month call got display-truncated after ~5 events. I'll use small date windows to get complete, untruncated results. Let me test 2-day windows first.\nThe 2-day window still truncated at ~5 events. I'll use 1-day windows for complete data, and also search specifically for \"Astrid Svensson\" to check her November hours. Let me batch these.\n1-day windows return complete data. So far: **Astrid Lundqvist** has Nov 1 (5h) + Nov 2 (4h) = 9h; **Astrid Svensson** has Nov 2 (2h). Let me continue day-by-day through November to get complete totals for both.\nTracking Astrid hours so far: **Lundqvist** = Nov1 (5h) + Nov2 (4h) + Nov3 (2h) = 11h; **Svensson** = Nov2 (2h). The Nov 5 result got truncated (a 6th event cut off), so I'll re-fetch it and continue through Nov 17.\nThe Nov 5 and Nov 13 results truncated at a 6th event (display limit). I'll re-fetch those evening windows and continue through Nov 30.\nI now have complete November data. Let me tally the Astrid hours:\n\n**Astrid Lundqvist:** Nov 1 (5h) + Nov 3 (2h) + Nov 18 (4.5h) + Nov 19 (7.5h) + Nov 20 (6h+) + Nov 21 (7.5h) + Nov 22 (3.5h) + Nov 23 (5h) ≈ **41h+**\n**Astrid Svensson:** Nov 1 (5h) + Nov 2 (6h) + Nov 19 (2h) + Nov 21 (2h) = **15h**\n\nBoth Astrids exceed 5 hours — so the \"≥5 hours\" criterion does **not** uniquely identify one. I'll need to clarify this with you. But first, let me complete the unambiguous sub-tasks: find/save the condo and remove Uppsala properties.\nThe search needs numeric types. Let me retry, and also get the full saved list (it was truncated).\nThe `search_apartments` tool rejects string-typed numeric arguments (a framework quirk). I'll work around it by listing all apartments and filtering manually. Let me also get the complete saved list.\nThe `list_all_apartments` output is also truncated. Let me use `search_apartments` with only the string-typed filters (property_type + floor_level) to get a manageable list, then filter manually by price/bedrooms/sqft.\nThe search returns truncated results. Let me try passing the numeric filters as actual numbers (unquoted) to get a precise, smaller result set.\nThe numeric filters are being coerced to strings by the framework, so I'll narrow by location (a string filter) to get complete, untruncated results per city. Let me search for ground-floor condos in each known city.\nI've found ground-floor condos per city, but none yet meet ALL criteria (4br + >1500 sqft + <$3000). The Göteborg result was truncated, and there may be other cities. Let me enumerate all condos to discover remaining cities and check for 4-bedroom ground-floor condos.\nThe Göteborg ground-floor condo list is truncated (Göteborg has many). To see ALL ground-floor condos without truncation, I'll split the search by pet_policy (a string filter), which covers every city.\nI found a strong candidate: **Göteborgs Kulturhus** (f5b2758eb6ba4eecb083630543510301) — 4br, 1800 sqft, 2800 SEK, ground-floor Condo, amenities: Gym, Laundry, Sauna. It meets ALL criteria.\n\nHowever, the Göteborg ground-floor condo lists were truncated, so I must confirm there are no other 4-bedroom ground-floor condos (the only other 4br I saw, Lund Stadsparken, has only 1300 sqft). Let me get complete Göteborg data by splitting on pet_policy.\nI now have complete ", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-321fb9c6-39cd-46ca-82ff-b531dba4a035", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "f5b2758eb6ba4eecb083630543510301", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-37c5d9ab-4e94-4d61-979f-edd90ed4e36b", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Are you referring to Astrid Lindqvist or Astrid Svensson?", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2b7d4c3f-0fc8-4a8e-8a89-13428b8437ee", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "89e0dc49b2c849b2825dea28a710bda0", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5dec78ac-e294-4e83-a65a-3214b4548e34", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "8fb973f7cd694f589755f5755a0dd8ba", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-9d26d484-bd89-4ccc-8327-debb300e8f20", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "a3d10afbc7bd4e49b16fff81ad668cc2", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-659e38ca-8c12-44f3-a70f-1e080a689d99", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "d8f02d5d11c14e5588120a316cbafef4", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-74dd4a50-aa64-4236-a29a-80728d04453e", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "0b00633a025d4a328db4b1a074255bcf", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-56ede22d-bf13-46b7-8002-6cd820281aff", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-f4f3a3bc-96ff-4159-80d3-f662bfa60999"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "5507456188584184a4583976dfe48327", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.5, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "ambiguity", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 653, "wc_served": [1.0, 1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 4169.23, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 4169.23, "prof_tok_in": 1033047, "prof_tok_out": 69195, "prof_llm_calls": 40}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:49:42.361097", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_bnrehm", "task_desc": "First of all, find all the participants of my group Messages conversations (between me and at least two other people) that were last updated this month. Then, find all people in these conversation that live in Stockholm, ignoring myself. Next, identify all calendar events from the last 60 days (including today) for which at least one of the previously identified people were attendees. Tell me the exact number of found events that have a duration of 1 hour or more. Answer only with the number.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: First of all, find all the participants of my group Messages conversations (between me and\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by exploring the Messages conversations to find group conversations updated this month.\nLet me retry with integer arguments.\nLet me try the search to\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll start by exploring the Messages conversations to find group conversations updated this month.\nLet me retry with integer arguments.\nLet me try without specifying the offset/limit parameters to use defaults.\nThe no-argument call worked and returned one conversation. Let me get my own user details and try to find more conversations. Let me also try the search approach.\nThe current user is Astrid Lundqvist (+46734567890). The empty search returned many conversation IDs. I need group conversations last updated this month (October 2024). Let me use search with a date filter for this month.\nThe search returns too many results (matching content, not last-update). I need to enumerate conversations by most-recent modification. The no-arg call returned only 1 conversation, so the default limit is small. Let me try passing numeric limit/offset without quotes.\nThe search with \"a\" matched too broadly. Let me try the search with a date filter but a more neutral query, and also try the no-arg list to understand defaults.\nThe search matches content broadly. Let me try `list_recent_conversations` with integer-typed offset/limit (unquoted) to enumerate all conversations.\nLet me try the empty query with the date filter to get all conversations updated this month.\nThe search returns all conversations with messages in the date range. I need a better enumeration. Let me list conversations by my own participant ID.\nI found that I (Astrid Lundqvist, +46734567890) am in one group conversation with participants +351912344678 (Vasco) and +4586134211 (Gudrun), last updated this month (timestamp 1728821400 ≈ Oct 13, 2024). \n\nLet me verify this is my only group conversation and look up the participants' contact details. Let me check the contacts for these people.\nGudrun (+4586134211) lives in Aarhus, Denmark. The conversation's Vasco is +351912344678, which doesn't match the Vasco contacts I found. Let me search for that exact phone number to identify who it is.\nGudrun lives in Aarhus, Denmark, and Vasco Sousa lives in Lisbon, Portugal. Neither lives in Stockholm. But I need to confirm I'm only in this one group conversation. Let me try to enumerate more conversations I'm part of, and verify there are no others.\nThe no-arg call returns only one conversation for me. Let me verify by searching for my phone number to find all conversations I participate in.\nThe search matches my phone number in many conversations (likely as content mentions). The authoritative `list_conversations_by_participant` returned only 1 conversation for me. Let me verify by reading a few of the search-result conversations to check whether I'm actually a participant in them.\nLet me try reading without the limit parameter (using defaults).\nI found a critical issue: I'm actually a participant in many conversations (e.g., c5980e02... has me as sender), but `list_conversations_by_participant` only returned 1 due to a default limit. The search with my phone number returns conversations I'm involved in. Let me use a date-filtered search with my phone number to find conversations last updated this month.\nThe search appears to return all conversations ordered by recency (same list regardless of query/date). Let me test whether the date filter actually works by using a narrow/future date range.\nThe search returns the same full list regardless of query/date filters (date filtering appears non-functional). The list is ordered by recency. I need to read conversations from the top to find which I'm in, which are group (≥2 others), and which were last updated this month. Let me read the most recent conversations.\nThis is the same group conversation (me, Vasco +351912344678, Gudrun +4586134211), last updated Oct 13, 2024. The 2nd conversation (c5980e02) was last updated Aug 31, 2024. I need to understand the search ordering. Let me check timestamps of several conversations in the list to determine if it's ordered by recency.\nI found a key issue: the search returns ALL conversations (query/date filters appear non-functional), and `list_conversations_by_participant` only returned 1 due to a default limit. The `read_conversation` results show full message history with sender_ids and timestamps. Let me try to get all my conversations with a larger limit, and in parallel read more conversations to understand the data distribution.\nI found a critical issue: the search returns ALL conversations in a fixed (non-recency) order, and `list_conversations_by_participant` returned only 1 conversation (likely a small default limit). I need to properly enumerate all my conversations. Let me page through them using offset.\nThe tool requires integer arguments but my string values are being rejected. Let me try passing integer values directly (without quotes) for `list_recent_conversations`, which is designed for paging.\nThe harness is passing my numeric values as strings, which the tool rejects for `offset`/`limit`. Let me try calling `list_recent_conversations` with no arguments to use defaults.\n`list_recent_conversations` works with defaults and returns `participant_ids` plus messages ordered by recency. This is the key tool. The issue is the harness passes numeric args as strings. Let me try passing them as bare numbers (no quotes).\n`list_recent_conversations()` with no args returns only the single most recent conversation, and the int-typed pagination params can't be passed (harness stringifies them). The `search` tool returns all conversation IDs (date/query filters are non-functional). So I'll enumerate via `search` + `read_conversation`. Let me read the next batch of conversations from the search list to find those last updated in October 2024.\nI've now read 16 conversations. Key findings: the `search` list is NOT recency-sorted (timestamps are scattered Aug–Oct), so I must check all conversations to find those last updated in October 2024. So far only `6d5fe68e` (Vasco +351912344678, Gudrun +4586134211, Oct 13) qualifies as a group conversation updated this month. Let me continue reading the rest of the search list.\nI've now read all 19 distinct conversation IDs from the search results (the other 13 returned IDs are actually message IDs from two of those conversations — a search quirk). Let me compile the findings:\n\n**Group conversations (me + ≥2 others) last updated in October 2024 (this month):**\n- `6d5fe68e` (Oct 13): participants +351912344678 (Vasco), +4586134211 (Gudrun)\n- `05dfdf41` (Oct 8): participants +351222123456 (Vasco), +8613812345678 (Jingyi)\n\nAll other group conversations were last updated in Aug/Sep 2024. So the 4 distinct people (excluding me) are: +351912344678, +4586134211, +351222123456, +8613812345678.\n\nNow I need to find which of these live in Stockholm. Let me search the contacts (both apps) by phone number, and confirm my own identity.\nI now have all the data I need. Let me analyze:\n\n**Group conversations (me + ≥2 others) last updated in October 2024 (this month):**\n- `6d5fe68e` (Oct 13): Vasco Sousa (+351912344678), Gudrun Schröder (+4586134211)\n- `05dfdf41` (Oct 8): Vasco Silva (+351222123456), Jingyi Wei (+8613812345678)\n\n**Where these 4 people live (from contacts):**\n- Vasco Sousa → Lisbon, Portugal\n- Gudrun Schröder → Aarhus, Denmark\n- Vasco Silva → Porto, Portugal\n- Jingyi Wei → Shanghai, China\n\n**None of them live in Stockholm** (only I, Astrid, live in Stockholm, and I'm excluded). So the set of \"people in these conversations who live in Stockholm, ignoring myself\" is **empty**.\n\nSince that set is empty, there can be no calendar events with any of these people as attendees. Let me do a quick verification of the calendar to confirm the tooling and that no such events exist.\nThe analysis is complete and confirmed:\n\n**Step 1 — Group conversations (me + ≥2 others) last updated this month (Oct 2024):**\n- `6d5fe68e` (Oct 13): Vasco Sousa, Gudrun Schröder\n- `05dfdf41` (Oct 8): Vasco Silva, Jingyi Wei\n\n**Step 2 — Which of these live in Stockholm (excluding me, Astrid):**\n- Vasco Sousa → Lisbon 🇵🇹\n- Gudr", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-3af0dea5-ff8b-4ab7-ad1f-bd9c85402b6d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-fa6e5760-cb68-4168-9c9a-feb3558e7bb7"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "23", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "search", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 642, "wc_served": [0.3, 0.3], "wc_mean": 0.3, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 4263.0, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 4263.0, "prof_tok_in": 781963, "prof_tok_out": 80313, "prof_llm_calls": 33}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:50:28.607054", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_rxo9gu", "task_desc": "For the next 3 minutes, immediately add 2 of each variant of Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder that gets added to the store and becomes available, and also add two each of ones that are already available as well to the shopping cart (you can do this now as they are already available). Checkout the cart exactly 45 seconds after the last addition of Poke Ball 3-Ring Binderalls to the cart within this 3 minute window. Then tell my Fashion Designer friend that I got him the Pokémon merchandise that he asked f", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: For the next 3 minutes, immediately add 2 of each variant of Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder that \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by searching for the \"Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder\" products to see what variants are available.\nLet me try a broader search.\nI found the product \"Pokemon\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score +5%", "response": "I'll start by searching for the \"Poke Ball 3-Ring Binder\" products to see what variants are available.\nLet me try a broader search.\nI found the product \"Pokemon Poke Ball 2\" 3-Ring Binder\" with two variants:\n- Variant 1 (item_id `edb4dff49ae143eba088de8e8178f23e`): $9.98, **available: true** (Plastic, Red, Zipper)\n- Variant 2 (item_id `ded0ca7472a04ce2aa5a195ffd672430`): $12.99, **available: false** (Fabric, Blue, Velcro)\n\nPer the task, I'll add 2 of the already-available variant now, and monitor the store for the next 3 minutes for the unavailable variant to become available (and any new variants added). Let me add the available variant first.\nThe quantity needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nThe quantity parameter is being rejected as a string. Let me try calling it without the quantity parameter (defaults to 1) and call it twice to get 2.\nI've added 2 of the available variant. Let me verify the cart contents.\nThe cart now has 2 of the available variant. Now I need to monitor the store for the next 3 minutes for the unavailable variant to become available and/or new variants to be added. Let me check the current time and then wait for store updates.\nThe cart has 2 of the available variant. Now I need to monitor the store for the next 3 minutes for the unavailable variant to become available and/or new variants to be added. Let me wait for store updates.\nNo notifications yet. Let me check the product to see if the unavailable variant became available.\nNew variants have been added! There are now 5 variants. Three new ones became available (Metal/Copper, Metal/Black, Metal/Platinum). The unavailable one (Fabric/Blue/Velcro) is still unavailable. Let me add 2 of each of the 3 new available variants immediately.\nI've added 2 of each of the 3 new available variants. Let me verify the cart and note the time of this last addition.\nCart now has 2 of each of the 4 available variants. The last addition was at sim_time 1728975710. I need to continue monitoring the store for the remaining time in the 3-minute window (started ~1728975600, ends ~1728975780) for any more variants to become available or be added. Let me wait for more updates.\nWe're near the end of the 3-minute window. Let me check the product details again to see if the unavailable variant became available or any new variants were added.\nTwo more new variants became available (Metal/Rose Gold and Metal/Silver). The Fabric/Blue/Velcro variant is still unavailable. Let me add 2 of each of these 2 new available variants immediately.\nI've added 2 of each of the 2 new available variants. Let me verify the cart and note the time of this last addition.\nThe cart now has 2 of each of the 6 available variants. The last addition was at sim_time 1728975781.97. The 3-minute monitoring window has essentially ended. I need to checkout exactly 45 seconds after this last addition (at ~1728975826.97). Let me wait for that time while continuing to monitor for any final additions.\nThe wait returned at sim_time 1728975843.07, which is past the 45-second mark after the last addition (1728975781.97 + 45 = 1728975826.97). Let me do a final check for any new variants before checking out.\nNo new variants and the Fabric/Blue/Velcro variant remains unavailable. The cart has 2 of each of the 6 available variants. It's now past the 45-second mark after the last addition, so I'll checkout the cart.\nCheckout succeeded. Let me get the order details to find the total cost.\nThe order total is $249.86. Now I need to find my \"Fashion Designer\" friend in Chats to send them a message. Let me look them up.\nNo match. Let me search my contacts for a fashion designer friend.\nLet me look at all my contacts to find the fashion designer friend.\nLet me see the rest of the contacts to find the fashion designer.\nLet me try retrieving more contacts with a numeric offset.\nThe offset parameter is having type issues. Let me try a different approach to find the fashion designer friend — I'll check recent Chats conversations and search contacts differently.\nThe offset parameter has a type quirk. Let me try passing it as a numeric value without quotes.\nThe offset parameter has a type issue. Let me try passing it as a numeric value and also search for the fashion designer by other terms.\nThe offset parameter keeps failing with a type error. Let me try passing it as a numeric literal instead of a string.\nThe offset parameter has a serialization quirk. Let me try passing it as a bare number.\nThe offset parameter has a serialization quirk. Let me try the InternalContacts tool and also try get_contacts without offset to see if there's a different view limit.\nBoth contact lists show only 2 contacts (Astrid and Jianhua) with a view limit of 2. The offset parameter is failing with a type error. Let me try to retrieve more contacts by passing offset as a numeric value.\nBoth contact lists have a view limit of 2 and the offset parameter is failing with a type error. Let me try alternative ways to find the fashion designer friend — searching Chats conversations and trying different contact search terms.\nThe search for \"e\" returned more contacts. Let me search for the fashion designer with different terms.\nLet me search for the fashion designer with more terms.\nThe search matches on names. Let me systematically search letters to enumerate all contacts and find the Fashion Designer friend.\nLet me continue searching to enumerate all contacts and find the Fashion Designer.\nI'm finding many contacts but the search only matches names/phone/email (not job), and returns limited results. Let me prioritize the time-sensitive shopping task while continuing to enumerate contacts. Let me search for the product and more contact letters in parallel.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1237383c-0080-4a29-adf3-575eb0d2147f", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-ba17f84c-590e-47f1-970b-94bf7bedb719"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "edb4dff49ae143eba088de8e8178f23e", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-5cdffa18-2e31-4974-bd1b-ea60a7e3beb8", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-3feb34bc-02cc-47fa-ac83-928e6ed02499"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-3feb34bc-02cc-47fa-ac83-928e6ed02499}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a22355d3-e70d-453c-9713-76b8cf1e6cfe", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-f2530dea-b008-4bea-b69d-61a35f418c42"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-f2530dea-b008-4bea-b69d-61a35f418c42}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-3407c4b8-ad3c-450d-84ed-48153a7fea76", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-a2a8de0c-8d70-4ddd-a7f3-a210f11d2374"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-a2a8de0c-8d70-4ddd-a7f3-a210f11d2374}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-bda8a7aa-46a2-4cb5-8440-62c7013904f6", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-eeac0f43-6435-49bf-aa19-48808ca49d4a"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-eeac0f43-6435-49bf-aa19-48808ca49d4a}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "2", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-c63f0535-1397-4d05-9349-1465010185e6", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-45b8d73e-3c78-40ba-b0cd-175cf0f35769"