{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:52:20.165340", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_bdn1w8", "task_desc": "Send an email to amscan-corporate@amscan.com and ask for a sponsorship deal in return for reviewing their products. Purchase the black version of \"Amscan Glamourous Party Wig Costume, White\" and the adult version of \"Amscan Super Hero Mask, Party Accessory, White\". Wait exactly 1 minute after the purchase is made and the email is sent, then let me know these tasks were complete. \n\nIf they reply and agree within 4 minutes from messaging me, immediately reply to them via email that I can begin rev", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Send an email to amscan-corporate@amscan.com and ask for a sponsorship deal in return for \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Send email to amscan-corporate@amscan.com requesting sponsorship deal\n2. Purchase black version of \"Amscan Glamourous\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score +10%", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Send email to amscan-corporate@amscan.com requesting sponsorship deal for product reviews\n2. Purchase black version of \"Amscan Glamourous Party Wig Costume, White\"\n3. Purchase adult version of \"Amscan Super Hero Mask, Party Accessory, White\"\n4. Wait exactly 1 minute after purchase + email, then notify user of completion\n5. If Amscan replies agreeing within 4 minutes, reply via email with review dates\n6. Create calendar review events (wig Oct 19, mask Oct 26, first 1-hr slot at/after 1PM)\n7. Message social media strategist about securing the deal\n8. Ignore emails from other companies agreeing to reviews\n\nLet me start by searching for the products and finding the social media strategist contact.\nI found the products. The black Glamorous wig variant is `bd3f62dd88da4a279405ac5cde66cec1` and the adult mask variant is `52b554fb447442f986b97d5e3ac52a22`. The social media strategist search returned nothing, so let me search differently.\nThe current user is Astrid (Social Media Influencer). I need to find a \"social media strategist\" contact. Let me get more contacts.\nThe offset parameter has a type conflict. Let me search contacts with different queries to find the social media strategist.\nA new email arrived from SCHLEICH (a non-Amscan company) — I'll note to ignore it per instructions. I still need to find the social media strategist. Let me try listing more contacts with different offset handling.\nThe contacts search only matches name/phone/email, not job title. Let me check InternalContacts and try to find the social media strategist there.\nThe contacts list seems paginated but offset has a type conflict. Let me try different approaches to find more contacts.\nThe contacts pagination has a type bug. Let me check the Messages app to find the social media strategist, and re-confirm contacts.\nThe contacts list only shows 2 people and pagination is buggy. Let me try listing conversations without the problematic limit param, and search messages for the strategist.\nThe contacts list only shows 2 people (Astrid and Jianhua), and pagination is buggy. The \"social media strategist\" is likely a message contact. Let me identify the message participants and look for the strategist. Let me also read a conversation that matched \"social media\".\nThe read_conversation also has a type conflict. Let me try without the limit param, and search messages for the strategist role.\nLet me read the conversation that matched \"strategy\" to identify the social media strategist.\nThis conversation is between Astrid and +46202123456, who discusses \"marketing strategy\" and \"social media campaigns.\" Let me identify this person.\nAxel is a \"Marketing Manager,\" not a \"social media strategist.\" The contacts list seems incomplete due to a pagination bug. Let me try to retrieve more contacts by passing offset as an integer, and search for other candidates.\nThe contacts pagination has a type bug. Let me try passing offset as a raw integer (the tool wants int, not string).\nThe contacts pagination is buggy and only shows 2 contacts. The \"social media strategist\" is likely a message contact. Let me search messages more specifically and look at conversation participants.\nThe contacts pagination has a type bug. Let me try passing offset as a raw integer value, and also check the InternalContacts app which may have a separate contact set.\nBoth contact apps show only 2 contacts with a broken pagination. Let me try passing offset as a numeric value, and identify the remaining message participants to find the social media strategist.\nThe contacts pagination is broken (it rejects string offsets). Let me try passing offset as a numeric value instead of a string.\nThe contacts pagination is unusable (it rejects string offsets). The \"social media strategist\" must be identifiable another way. Let me search messages more specifically to find who is described as a social media strategist.\nThe contacts pagination is broken, and message search for \"strategist\" returns nothing. The social media strategist is likely a contact I can find via messages. Let me list recent conversations to identify participants and find who is described as a social media strategist.\nThe offset/limit parameters need to be integers. Let me try passing them as numeric values.\nThe tool framework converts integers to strings, breaking pagination. Let me use search_contacts to find the message participants' contact details and identify the social media strategist.\nThe contacts app is limited to 2 entries due to a pagination bug, and none is a \"social media strategist.\" The strategist is likely a message contact. Let me enumerate all of the user's conversations to find them.\nLet me list conversations by participant to enumerate all message contacts.\nThe contacts app is limited to 2 entries (pagination bug), and the only social-media-related person is Astrid Lundqvist (Social Media Influencer) in InternalContacts. Let me enumerate InternalContacts fully and start the core actions (email + product searches) in parallel.\nI found the products. Now I need to fix the email recipients format (must be a list) and find the social media strategist. Let me re-send the email and search InternalContacts for the strategist.\nThe email was sent (ID: 91e75d8f2dc8144f48068891918988c3). Now let me find the social media strategist by searching the regular Contacts app and trying other job-title keywords.\nFound Yuting Liang, a \"Marketing Strategist\" in InternalContacts. Let me verify there isn't a more specific \"social media strategist\" by searching for \"social\" in both contact apps.\nYuting Liang (Marketing Strategist, InternalContacts) is the best match for \"social media strategist.\" Now let me add the two products to the cart (black wig + adult mask) and get Yuting's user_id for Messages.\nThe quantity parameter needs to be an integer. Let me add the items to cart with integer quantities.\nThe framework keeps converting quantity to a string. Since the default quantity is 1, let me omit the parameter entirely.\nBoth items are in the cart. Let me verify the cart contents and then check out.\nThe cart shows quantity 2 for each item — the earlier errored calls apparently still added items. I only need 1 of each, so let me remove 1 of each.\nCart now has exactly 1 of each (black wig + adult mask). Let me check out to complete the purchase.\nThe purchase is complete (order `bea8de9720fe4eb7bca80aa5ba63a7d7`) and the email was sent earlier. Now I'll wait exactly 1 minute (as instructed) before notifying you of completion.\nThe 1-minute wait is complete. Both core tasks are done:\n- ✅ Email sent to amscan-corporate@amscan.com requesting a sponsorship deal in return for product reviews\n- ✅ Purchased the black \"Amscan Glamourous Party Wig Costume, White\" and the adult \"Amscan Super Hero Mask, Party Accessory, White\" (order `bea8de9720fe4eb7bca80aa5ba63a7d7`)\n\nNow I'll let you know these are complete and then monitor for Amscan's reply for the next 4 minutes.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-23270bab-c03c-4cc6-893f-32cc6166b913", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-a3c56d0e-1160-43ab-9f1f-4ba97f2efb4f"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "bd3f62dd88da4a279405ac5cde66cec1", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "1", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-b5ee6469-32b4-4303-9d42-249a990a7fe3", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-a3c56d0e-1160-43ab-9f1f-4ba97f2efb4f"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "add_to_cart", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "item_id", "value": "52b554fb447442f986b97d5e3ac52a22", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "quantity", "value": "1", "value_type": "int"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a77a2587-0c00-4452-8ce3-fa02db8db5df", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-a3c56d0e-1160-43ab-9f1f-4ba97f2efb4f"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"amscan-corporate@amscan.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Sponsorship Deal", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "I'd like a sponsorship deal in return for reviewing your products, please.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-6a4dc5b5-e55d-4d1a-8d67-3390650a52eb", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-23270bab-c03c-4cc6-893f-32cc6166b913", "OracleEvent-AGENT-b5ee6469-32b4-4303-9d42-249a990a7fe3"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Shopping", "function": "checkout", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "discount_code", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-a851cc4d-8018-4360-b4be-bff5cf2531fd", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-a77a2587-0c00-4452-8ce3-fa02db8db5df", "OracleEvent-AGENT-6a4dc5b5-e55d-4d1a-8d67-3390650a52eb"], "event_relative_time": 60.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "The requested actions are complete.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-3eee812c-8c2a-4d95-a07a-d760b6ac7077", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-2fd1a39c-dd76-405e-803c-6ac4560b7dea"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "reply_to_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "{{Event-ENV-2fd1a39c-dd76-405e-803c-6ac4560b7dea}}", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "I can begin reviewing \"Amscan Glamourous Party Wig Costume, White\" and \"Amscan Super Hero Mask, Party Accessory, White\" on the 19th and 26th of this month, respectively.", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-8ef438a7-2ded-45e5-8e50-33861722fde2", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-2fd1a39c-dd76-405e-803c-6ac4560b7dea"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Reviewing Mask", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-26 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-26 15:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-1c064321-f510-41ac-86ac-bc20bfc75bec", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-2fd1a39c-dd76-405e-803c-6ac4560b7dea"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_id", "value": "+351912345378", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "I got the Amscan deal!", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-51fb02f3-f861-4acc-8b3e-309b22d00884", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-2fd1a39c-dd76-405e-803c-6ac4560b7dea"], "event_relative_time": 2.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Reviewing Wig", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 13:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-19 14:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.4444444444444444, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "time", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 570, "wc_served": [1.0, 1.0], "wc_mean": 1.0, "wc_active": 0, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 4194.85, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 4194.85, "prof_tok_in": 773887, "prof_tok_out": 38545, "prof_llm_calls": 40}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:52:21.819734", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_0obld3", "task_desc": "In my Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, suggest the dates and times two hours before my next two yoga classes for a 1 hour call between the three of us. Let me know as soon as you’ve done this. Wait exactly 3 minutes from your message to me for responses. If availability is confirmed by both of them in that time, schedule the call at the agreed upon time. If they are both available for both times, tell them in the same Messages conversation that we'll do the earlier one. I", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: In my Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, suggest the dates and times\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding the Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, and finding my next two yoga classes.\nLet m\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2: score +5%", "response": "I'll start by gathering the information I need: finding the Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne, and finding my next two yoga classes.\nThe yoga classes found are all in August 2024 (past). I need to find my NEXT two yoga classes from the current date (2024-10-15). Let me query events from now forward.\nThe limit parameter is being passed as a string. Let me try without it.\nThe future events list doesn't show yoga classes yet (it was truncated). Let me search specifically for yoga and also get the full future events list.\nThe search returns all yoga classes but the display is truncated, and the future events list (default limit 10) didn't include yoga. Let me query narrower date ranges to find the next yoga classes after today.\nThe results are being truncated at 10 events. Let me narrow the date range to find yoga classes with fewer events per window.\nI found the first yoga class after today: **Monday, 2024-10-21 18:00:00**. Now I need the second one. Let me search the following weeks.\nThe results keep truncating at 10 events. Let me use a narrower window to find the second yoga class after Oct 21.\nThe window still has too many events. Let me narrow to a tighter range to find the second yoga class.\nStill truncating. Let me narrow further to find the second yoga class.\nI found both yoga classes:\n1. **Monday, 2024-10-21 18:00:00** (Yoga Class)\n2. **Sunday, 2024-10-27 18:00:00** (Yoga Class)\n\nTwo hours before each, for a 1-hour call:\n1. **Monday, 2024-10-21 16:00:00 – 17:00:00**\n2. **Sunday, 2024-10-27 16:00:00 – 17:00:00**\n\nNow let me find the Messages conversation with both Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne.\nI found the conversation. Let me read it to understand the context before sending.\nI now understand the conversation context. The current user is Astrid. Let me send the suggested dates/times to the group conversation.\nI've sent the suggested times. Now I need to let you know I've done this, then wait exactly 3 minutes for responses.\nI see new messages have arrived in the conversation. Per the task, I need to wait exactly 3 minutes from my message to you before checking responses. Let me wait.\nI've waited exactly 3 minutes. Now let me check the conversation for responses from both Joana and Vigdis.\nI've reviewed the responses that came in during the 3-minute window. Let me analyze them:\n\n- **Joana** (+351954123456): \"Both of those times are good for me!\" → confirms both proposed slots.\n- **Vigdis** (+4571345678): \"I'm up for 4-5PM on the 16th!\" → proposes a *different* time (Oct 16), not one of my suggested slots.\n- **Vigdis** (+4571345678): \"Give me one second while I check my schedule!\" → still checking, did **not** confirm either of the proposed times.\n\nThe task's scheduling condition requires **availability to be confirmed by both of them** for the proposed times. Vigdis did not confirm either of the suggested slots (she counter-proposed Oct 16 and is still checking), so the \"both confirm\" condition is not met. The call therefore cannot be scheduled, and we're done per the instructions.\n\nLet me inform you of the outcome.\nI've completed the task. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**1. Found your next two yoga classes:**\n- Monday, Oct 21, 18:00–19:00\n- Sunday, Oct 27, 18:00–19:00\n\n**2. Suggested two 1-hour call slots** (two hours before each class) in your Messages conversation with Joana Silva and Vigdis Rønne:\n- Option 1: Monday, Oct 21, 16:00–17:00\n- Option 2: Sunday, Oct 27, 16:00–17:00\n\n**3. Let you know immediately** that the suggestions were sent.\n\n**4. Waited exactly 3 minutes** for responses, then checked the conversation:\n- Joana confirmed both times work for her.\n- Vigdis did **not** confirm either proposed slot — she counter-proposed Oct 16 (4–5 PM) and said she was still checking her schedule.\n\n**5. Outcome:** Since availability was not confirmed by *both* of them for the suggested times, the call was not scheduled (per your instructions, scheduling only proceeds when both confirm). The task is complete — no calendar event was created, and no further confirmation message was sent to the group.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-395097df-23ff-4689-a281-4b85f574d78d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-1002ac8b-cff9-409e-9170-a615155a24bb"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message_to_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "conversation_id", "value": "ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Joana and Vigdis, I was thinking of scheduling a 1-hour call with both of you. Would both of you be available on Oct 16 at 4 PM or Oct 17 at 4 PM? ", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-e18425b4-df03-4b0a-8777-ce4f314d566e", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-395097df-23ff-4689-a281-4b85f574d78d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "Message sent to Joana and Vigdis suggesting a 1-hour call on October 16 at 4 PM and October 17 at 4 PM. Waiting for their response.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-81a7cc64-32f8-472d-a4cc-408a781c0d38", "dependencies": ["OracleEvent-AGENT-479d2a41-6896-4780-9f73-3dbc51784e01", "OracleEvent-AGENT-ded9b844-a686-4fe0-8313-baed17e87e8d"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "AgentUserInterface", "function": "send_message_to_user", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "content", "value": "October 16 at 4 PM was chosen as the date and time for the 1-hour call with Joana and Vigdis.", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-479d2a41-6896-4780-9f73-3dbc51784e01", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-e53b14eb-4f75-4fed-912f-29b6acb98f7b", "Event-ENV-c2a86c3c-e49e-4beb-8156-fae9d918c57f"], "event_relative_time": 30.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Phone Call with Joana and Vigdis", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 16:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 17:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[\"Joana Silva\",\"Vigdis Rønne\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-ded9b844-a686-4fe0-8313-baed17e87e8d", "dependencies": ["Event-ENV-c2a86c3c-e49e-4beb-8156-fae9d918c57f", "Event-ENV-e53b14eb-4f75-4fed-912f-29b6acb98f7b"], "event_relative_time": 30.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "send_message_to_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "conversation_id", "value": "ff602c484dad46ab94f51b9f02e365a9", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Hey Joana and Vigdis, just confirming our 1 hour call for October 16 at 4 PM. Looking forward to catching up then!", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "attachment_path", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.6, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "time", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 553, "wc_served": [1.05, 1.05], "wc_mean": 1.05, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.05, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 3761.39, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 3761.39, "prof_tok_in": 422068, "prof_tok_out": 12990, "prof_llm_calls": 20}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:53:22.933974", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_22_0byq1g", "task_desc": "Save all the properties that are priced at $3200 if they are not saved yet. Send an email to Luís Silva titled 'Request for Chess Coaching' asking him to be my chess coach. Create a calendar event for tomorrow 2024/10/16 at 12pm for one hour titled 'Tasting New Wines'. Delete the most recent email from Astrid Nakamura.", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Save all the properties that are priced at $3200 if they are not saved yet. Send an email \nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Save all properties priced at $3200 (if not already saved)\n2. Send email to Luís Silva about chess coaching\n3. Create\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll break this task into sub-requests:\n1. Save all properties priced at $3200 (if not already saved)\n2. Send email to Luís Silva about chess coaching\n3. Create calendar event for tomorrow at 12pm titled 'Tasting New Wines'\n4. Delete the most recent email from Astrid Nakamura\n\nLet me start by gathering the necessary information in parallel.\nThe apartment search failed due to type mismatch. Let me retry with proper numeric types and also get the full apartment list. I'll also verify the Astrid emails more thoroughly.\nThe `search_apartments` tool keeps rejecting string inputs for price. Let me try passing numeric values directly, and also re-fetch the full apartment list to filter manually.\nThe `search_apartments` tool has a type bug (it rejects string inputs for price). I'll filter manually from the full list, but the output was truncated. Let me try the search with numeric values and re-fetch the full list to see all apartments.\nThe `search_apartments` tool has a type bug rejecting string prices, and `list_all_apartments` output is truncated. Let me try passing numeric values without quotes to the search tool.\nThe `search_apartments` price filter is broken (type bug). Let me try `search_apartments` with no price filter to get the full list, which may render without truncation.\nThe `list_all_apartments` and `search_apartments` outputs are being truncated after ~5 entries, and the price filter is broken. I need to enumerate the full catalog via other filters. Let me try partitioning by property type to get complete subsets.\nThe results are being truncated at a fixed display length. I need smaller result sets to see all entries. Let me partition by bedroom count to get complete, displayable subsets.\nThe numeric filters all fail due to a type bug, and `list_all_apartments` truncates. I'll enumerate by combining `property_type` with `furnished_status` to get smaller, complete result sets. Let me start with the Apartment type split by furnishing.\nI found one $3200 property so far: \"The Lofts at Downtown\" (id `15103cfde2e3480daa03e6665611562e`, saved: false). Results are still truncated, so I'll narrow further by adding pet_policy filters to see all entries. Let me split the Apartment+Furnished set by pet policy.\nThe \"No pets\" Furnished Apartment set is still truncated. Let me split it further by floor_level to see all entries completely.\nThe \"No pets\" Furnished Apartment set is now complete — only \"The Lofts at Downtown\" ($3200) qualifies. Now let me fully enumerate the \"Pets allowed\" Furnished Apartment set (which was truncated) by floor level.\nThe \"Pets allowed\" Furnished Upper-floors set is still truncated (at least 5 entries, possibly more). Let me split it by lease_term to see all entries.\nThe \"1 year\" subset of Pets-allowed Furnished Upper-floor Apartments is still truncated. I'll partition it by amenity to get fully-visible subsets.\nThis brute-force enumeration is inefficient. The `search_apartments` tool has `min_price`/`max_price` filters — if they work (the int error was only for `number_of_bedrooms`), I can directly find all $3200 properties. Let me try that.\nThe numeric filters are unusable (string type error), so I must enumerate via categorical filters. The result cap is ~5 entries. I've been focused on Apartments, but there are other property types too. Let me discover all property types first.\nProperty types are: Apartment, Condo, Townhouse, Loft. Townhouse (2) and Loft (1) are fully enumerated (no $3200). The Condo set is truncated. Let me enumerate the remaining partitions: Apartment Unfurnished/Semi-furnished, and Condo by furnished status.\nThese are all truncated too. I need to systematically enumerate every partition with ≤5 entries. Let me continue with the remaining Apartment-Furnished pet-policy partitions and all Condo pet-policy partitions.\nI'm building a complete catalog. The result cap is 5 entries, and amenity filters overlap heavily. Let me enumerate by `floor_level` (mutually exclusive) across property types to find the rare buckets, then drill into the common ones.\nI now have a near-complete catalog. Let me consolidate what I've found and verify the remaining uncertain buckets (Apartment Ground floor, Apartment Upper floors, Condo Ground floor) for any $3200 entries.\nI found a $3200 property: **\"The Lofts at Downtown\"** (Apartment, Upper floors, Furnished, No pets, LA) — `15103cfde2e3480daa03e6665611562e`, currently `saved: false`. Let me verify there are no other $3200 properties in the remaining uncertain buckets (Apartment Ground floor, Condo Ground floor) by filtering on the rare \"No pets\" policy.\nI've confirmed the only $3200 property so far is **\"The Lofts at Downtown\"** (`15103cfde2e3480daa03e6665611562e`, saved:false). The premium buckets (Penthouse, Upper floors) were truncated, so let me close those gaps by pet-policy to ensure no other $3200 properties are hidden.\nI've now exhaustively enumerated the catalog. The only property priced at exactly **$3200** is **\"The Lofts at Downtown\"** (`15103cfde2e3480daa03e6665611562e`, currently `saved: false`). Let me save it, and in parallel start the other sub-tasks: find Luís Silva's email, get current user details, and locate Astrid Nakamura's most recent email.\nThe $3200 property is saved, and I found Luís Silva (a Chess Coach) and the current user. The Astrid search returned one email, but I should confirm it's the *most recent* by searching her email address directly. Let me do that, and in parallel send the chess-coaching email and create the calendar event.\nThe calendar event was created. The email failed because `recipients` must be a list. The Astrid search confirms only one email from her (`74699dcc20f64627bf9383eb0edab999`), which is therefore the most recent. Let me retry the email with a list and delete the Astrid email.\nAll four sub-tasks are done. Let me verify the saved apartment to confirm the save took effect.\nThe saved list is truncated and I don't see \"The Lofts at Downtown\" yet. Let me verify its saved status directly.\nAll four sub-tasks are complete and verified:\n\n1. **Saved the $3200 property** — \"The Lofts at Downtown\" (Los Angeles, $3200) was the only property priced at exactly $3200 in the catalog, and it is now saved (`saved: true`).\n2. **Sent the chess-coaching email** — Emailed Luís Silva (a chess coach in Lisbon) with subject \"Request for Chess Coaching\" asking him to be my coach.\n3. **Created the calendar event** — \"Tasting New Wines\" on 2024-10-16 from 12:00 to 13:00 (1 hour).\n4. **Deleted the most recent email from Astrid Nakamura** — She had only one email (\"Eco-Friendly Wine Packaging Ideas\"), which was the most recent, and it has been deleted.\nAll four sub-tasks have been completed and verified:\n\n1. **Saved the $3200 property** — \"The Lofts at Downtown\" (Los Angeles, $3,200) was the only property at that exact price and is now saved.\n2. **Sent the chess-coaching email** — Emailed Luís Silva with subject \"Request for Chess Coaching.\"\n3. **Created the calendar event** — \"Tasting New Wines\" on 2024-10-16, 12:00–13:00.\n4. **Deleted the most recent email from Astrid Nakamura** — Her single (and thus most recent) email was removed.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-2c19a9cb-cf63-491f-bf3d-4428160b60c3", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-0c85b077-7e12-46b9-a628-c947f222f556"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "efdc037efd7c4eed985de4a5fcc2063c", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-93bbecfb-4a41-4287-bf51-a2c71729a4d0", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-0c85b077-7e12-46b9-a628-c947f222f556"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "save_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "15103cfde2e3480daa03e6665611562e", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-d5ca4734-88b1-49a0-9e48-da3dc04c578b", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-0c85b077-7e12-46b9-a628-c947f222f556"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "delete_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "email_id", "value": "74699dcc20f64627bf9383eb0edab999", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "folder_name", "value": "INBOX", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-23fe73b2-4f37-4025-bc8a-6188bb5fb745", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-0c85b077-7e12-46b9-a628-c947f222f556"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Emails", "function": "send_email", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "recipients", "value": "[\"luis.silva.chess@gaia2mail.com\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "subject", "value": "Request for Chess Coaching", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "content", "value": "Dear Luis,\n\nWould you be my chess coach?\n\nBest,\nAurélien LaFleur", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "cc", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "attachment_paths", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-22e22a4a-b1c5-4de9-b8d6-9b6593da0ce2", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-0c85b077-7e12-46b9-a628-c947f222f556"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Calendar", "function": "add_calendar_event", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "title", "value": "Tasting New Wines", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "start_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 12:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "end_datetime", "value": "2024-10-16 13:00:00", "value_type": "str"}, {"name": "tag", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "description", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "location", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}, {"name": "attendees", "value": "[]", "value_type": "list[str]"}]}, "metadata": null}], "score": 0.8, "em": 0.0, "method": "gaia2_official_actions", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "execution", "level": "unknown", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 642, "wc_served": [1.05, 1.05], "wc_mean": 1.05, "wc_active": 2, "wc_n": 2, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "self", "code_rev": "3dad207e", "critic_model": "grok-4.5", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "meta", "score_provenance": "self_assessment", "judge_model": "hy3", "protocol_hash": "3aa73f4d0bd6", "prof_total_s": 4429.4, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 4429.4, "prof_tok_in": 736521, "prof_tok_out": 42631, "prof_llm_calls": 29}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:56:59.610836", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_xtv9xb", "task_desc": "I'm excited to say the sports coach in my contacts is now officially my girlfriend, so I need to message everyone else I was seeing. Create a group chat with all my Stockholm contacts 35 or younger (except my girlfriend) on Messages and tell them I'm in a committed relationship now so they shouldn't message anymore. Let me know once the message is sent. Watch for replies for 4 minutes after notifying me - if anyone responds, immediately send a private Messages message to this person saying this ", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: I'm excited to say the sports coach in my contacts is now officially my girlfriend, so I n\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by exploring the contacts to find the sports coach (girlfriend) and the Stockholm contacts 35 or younger.\nThe first contact is the user (Astrid). Let\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll start by exploring the contacts to find the sports coach (girlfriend) and the Stockholm contacts 35 or younger.\nThe offset needs to be an integer. Let me retry.\nLet me try calling without the offset parameter.\nThe contacts list has a view limit. Let me scroll through more contacts. The offset parameter needs to be an integer.\nThe offset parameter has a type issue. Let me use search instead to find the sports coach and Stockholm contacts.\nThe search only matches name/phone/email. I need to find the sports coach by examining contacts. Let me try the offset parameter as a number value.\nThe offset parameter keeps failing with a type error. Let me try passing it as a numeric value directly.\nThe offset parameter has a type mismatch issue. Let me try the InternalContacts tool which may behave differently, and also try a different offset value.\nThe offset parameter appears to be broken in both tools. Let me try the InternalContacts with offset to see if it behaves differently.\nThe offset parameter is broken (type mismatch bug). Let me try a workaround by searching for a common substring that appears in all emails to enumerate contacts.\nThe view limit appears to be 2 contacts per call, and the offset parameter is broken (type bug). Let me test whether the search returns more than 2 results for a common query, which would let me enumerate contacts.\nThe search returns up to 3 results, and the view limit is 2. The offset parameter has a type bug. Let me try passing offset as a numeric value (not a string) to work around the type error.\nThe offset parameter is broken (framework type bug). I'll enumerate contacts via search using phone country codes and other patterns. Let me search for Swedish contacts and the sports coach.\nThe search only matches name/phone/email (not job/description), and the offset parameter is broken. I need to enumerate all contacts to find the sports coach (described in the description field) and identify Stockholm contacts ≤35. Let me do a systematic letter sweep. First, let me verify search behavior with a few more letters.\nThe search returns a fixed small set regardless of query, which suggests it's not truly filtering. Let me test this hypothesis with letters unlikely to appear, and also try to find the sports coach via other means.\nThe search matches name/phone/email only (not description), and the offset parameter is broken. I need to enumerate contacts via search. Let me do a systematic letter sweep to discover all contacts, collecting unique IDs.\nThe search returns a fixed window of 3 results and doesn't reliably filter. Let me test the search with known full names to understand its behavior, and continue the letter sweep.\nThe search filters by name but caps at 3 results, and single-letter queries return a default set. The key issue is I can't enumerate all contacts. Let me try the `get_contacts` offset as a raw number (not string) to bypass the type bug.\nThe search caps at 3 results and the offset parameter has a type bug. Let me try calling `get_contacts` with a bare integer offset (no quotes) to bypass the string coercion, and also try with no offset.\n`get_contacts` with no offset works and returns a `contacts` array (display truncated). The offset must be an int. Let me try passing offset as a bare integer to paginate.\n`get_contacts` can't paginate (offset type bug). Let me test whether search matches description/city fields by querying distinctive terms like \"coach\", \"Stockholm\", and \"sports\".\nSearch only matches name/email/phone (not description or city), and caps at 3 results. I can't reliably enumerate all contacts this way. Let me pivot to the Messages app to understand the dating landscape — the user was \"seeing\" people, so conversations may reveal who they are, including the sports-coach girlfriend. Let me explore conversations and search message content.\nThe Messages search works well. The \"coach\" search returned 11 conversations (the girlfriend is the sports coach), and \"Stockholm\" returned 44 (likely most conversations, since the user lives there). The single-letter contact searches were returning a default fallback set, not real matches — so search caps at 3 real matches and I can't enumerate all contacts that way.\n\nThe dating context lives in Messages. Let me read the \"coach\" conversations to identify the sports-coach girlfriend and the other people the user was seeing. Let me read several in parallel.\nThe Messages search works well. The \"coach\" hits are group chats, not the girlfriend directly. Let me list all recent conversations (the offset type bug means I must omit it) to map out the user's messaging landscape and find 1-on-1 romantic conversations. Let me also try searching contacts by Swedish phone country code to find Stockholm contacts.\nSearch matches phone numbers (the \"+46\" query returned real Swedish contacts), but caps at 3 results, and single-letter queries return a fallback set. I can't fully enumerate contacts this way. The dating context is in Messages. Let me list recent conversations (no args, since numeric params get coerced to strings) and read the remaining \"coach\" conversations to find the romantic partners.\nThe Messages search is powerful (matches content). The \"coach\" hits are mostly group chats where \"coach\" appears in text (e.g., Åsa called \"a great coach\"). I need to identify the actual sports-coach girlfriend and enumerate Stockholm contacts ≤35. \n\nThe contact search appears capped at ~3-4 results. Let me test the cap with common single letters and enumerate Swedish contacts via phone-prefix and surname searches, plus search Messages for romantic context to identify who the user was dating.\nThe \"date\" search returned 7 targeted conversations (likely romantic). Let me read them to identify who the user was dating. I'll also continue mapping Stockholm contacts.\nThe \"date\" hits are mostly casual (\"coffee date\", \"dinner date\"), not romantic. I need the full contact list to reliably find the sports-coach girlfriend and all Stockholm contacts ≤35. Let me try `get_contacts` with no arguments (the offset error only occurred when I passed a string).\n`get_contacts()` with no args returned only 2 contacts (page size is small). The offset must be an int. Let me page through the contacts using numeric offsets.\n`get_contacts` is capped at 2 and offset requires an int (which the framework can't pass), so I can't paginate it. Let me check whether `InternalContacts` is a separate, fully-enumerable store, and try listing conversations with no args.\nBoth contact stores are capped at 2 and pagination is blocked (offset must be int). I'll rely on `search_contacts` (real matches, capped ~3-4) and `Messages__search` (returns conversation IDs). The girlfriend is a female sports coach. Let me search Messages for romantic/coach context (EN + SV) and probe the contact search cap.\nThe \"coach\" and \"ski\" searches return the **same 11 conversations** — strongly suggesting these involve the sports (ski) coach. The girlfriend is the sports coach. Let me read all 11 to find the romantic one and identify the coach.\nKey finding: The only **sports coach** in the messages is **Kasper (+4531723456)** — a ski coach (\"Coaching is going great... on the slopes\"; \"I wanted to give back to the sport and help the next generation of skiers\"). He's the girlfriend to exclude. (Åsa is called a \"great coach\" only in an academic/mentor sense, not sports.)\n\nNow I need all **Stockholm** contacts aged ≤35 (except Kasper, who's in Denmark). Let me search contacts for Stockholm/Sweden.\nThe search matches name/phone/email fields (not city). \"Lundqvist\" returned 3 Stockholm contacts (Astrid, Åke 45, Åsa 79). I need to find ALL Stockholm contacts ≤35. Let me probe the search cap and surface Swedish contacts via phone prefix and common letters.\nThe contact search is capped at ~3 results and unreliable for enumeration. Let me try `get_contacts` **without** an offset (the default may be applied as an int internally), and also try the InternalC", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 0.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-82242a99-c57d-4a86-877d-e6403032432d", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-ff25bf8c-4199-44d9-b834-418eb56fc9df"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "Messages", "function": "create_group_conversation", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "user_ids", "value": "[\"+46700234567\",\"+46701234537\",\"+46202123456\"]", "value_type": "list[str]"}, {"name": "title", "value": "", "value_type": "Optional[str]"}]