{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T14:57:48.494028", "benchmark": "gaia2", "group": "curated_patch", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia2_scenario_universe_21_1qgjj6", "task_desc": "Go ahead and remove all the properties with zip codes starting with 1, as I don't really like that part of Stockholm. Then, create a new group chat with Aurélie Dumont and Vasco Sousa via Messages and let them know that the properties have been removed. Let me know when the message has been sent. If either of them respond with more properties to remove or ask to add previously removed properties back to the saved list again, please do so. If you had to remove more properties, then, after removin", "augmented_prompt": "## Curated prior attempts (this task's chain)\n\n[Prior attempt — store version v2]\nTask: Go ahead and remove all the properties with zip codes starting with 1, as I don't really l\nAnswer given then (unverified): I'll start by examining the saved apartments to find ones with zip codes starting with \"1\".\nThe response appears truncated. Let me get the complete list of save\nActions used:  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  ->  -> \n\nVersion lineage (later supersedes earlier):\n  v1 -> v2", "response": "I'll start by examining the saved apartments to find ones with zip codes starting with \"1\".\nThe list appears truncated. Let me get the complete list of saved apartments.\nThe response is being truncated. Let me try searching with the saved_only filter to get a cleaner, complete list.\nThe `saved_only` parameter has a type issue. Let me try a different approach to get the complete saved list. I'll search by zip code to find properties with zip codes starting with \"1\".\nThe search by zip code \"1\" returned empty, which suggests it may be an exact match rather than prefix. Let me list all apartments to understand the full catalog and identify which saved ones have zip codes starting with \"1\".\nThe list is being truncated in display. Let me search for saved apartments in Stockholm specifically, since the user mentioned Stockholm and Stockholm zip codes start with \"1\".\nI can see Stockholm properties have zip codes starting with \"1\" (e.g., 114 41, 118 26, 111 23). The saved list display is being truncated, so let me enumerate all Stockholm apartments using price brackets to find which are saved. Let me run several searches in parallel.\nThe search tool has type quirks. Let me try passing numeric values directly (without quotes) for the price filters to split the Stockholm results.\nThe search tool has type issues with numeric filters. Let me split the Stockholm results by number of bedrooms to get smaller, complete result sets.\nThe search tool only reliably filters by `location` (other filters have type bugs). The Stockholm results are truncated at ~5 entries. Let me break Stockholm down by specific districts to get complete, non-truncated result sets.\nI'm building a complete picture. So far I've found 2 saved Stockholm apartments (zip starting with \"1\"): \"Stockholm Haven\" (118 26) and \"Stockholm Serenity\" (114 39). The saved list was truncated, so I need to find ALL saved apartments. Let me search each city to identify all saved properties and ensure I don't miss any Stockholm ones.\nI now have a clearer picture. Let me get the complete saved list directly (the earlier error was only on the `saved_only` param of search, not on `list_saved_apartments` itself) and also check Göteborg, which I searched under the wrong spelling.\nI now have a good picture. The saved list and searches are being truncated in display, so I need to be thorough. Key finding: only Stockholm has zip codes starting with \"1\" (Swedish postal codes: Stockholm = 10x–19x; Göteborg = 41x; Malmö = 21x; Uppsala = 75x; Lund = 22x; Helsingborg = 25x; Jönköping = 55x). So I only need to remove **saved Stockholm apartments**.\n\nI've found 2 saved Stockholm apartments so far: \"Stockholm Haven\" (118 26) and \"Stockholm Serenity\" (114 39). Let me search additional Stockholm districts to ensure I haven't missed any saved ones.\nI found another Stockholm apartment (\"Stockholm Archipelago\", zip 120 30) but it's not saved. So far the only **saved** Stockholm apartments (zip starting with \"1\") are:\n- \"Stockholm Haven\" (118 26)\n- \"Stockholm Serenity\" (114 39)\n\nLet me search a few more Stockholm districts to be certain I haven't missed any saved ones.\nI've now thoroughly searched Stockholm districts. The only **saved** Stockholm apartments (zip codes starting with \"1\") are:\n- **Stockholm Haven** (118 26) — `5a8070b881fb4a07bbeffc8b1e9b0109`\n- **Stockholm Serenity** (114 39) — `db61fa40d1714954a5b9aee3d20941ec`\n\nAll other saved apartments are in cities with zip codes NOT starting with \"1\" (Göteborg 41x, Malmö 21x, Uppsala 75x, Lund 22x, Helsingborg 25x, Jönköping 55x). Let me remove the two Stockholm saved apartments.\nBoth removals succeeded. Let me verify the saved list to confirm those two are gone and no other Stockholm saved apartments remain.\nThe two Stockholm saved apartments are now removed, and the remaining saved apartments are all in non-Stockholm cities (zip codes not starting with \"1\"). \n\nNow I need to create a group chat with Aurélie Dumont and Vasco Sousa via Messages. The Messages tool uses phone numbers as user IDs, so let me look up their IDs.\nI have both IDs. Now let me create the group chat with Aurélie Dumont and Vasco Sousa.\nThe group chat was created (ID: `94bd07b937ca384a4580585846018295`). Now let me send the message letting them know the properties have been removed.\nThe group message has been sent successfully. Now, per the task, I need to wait for any responses from Aurélie or Vasco (who may ask to remove more properties or add the removed ones back), and handle those. Let me wait for notifications.\nNo responses came in from Aurélie or Vasco during that wait. Let me wait a bit longer to give them time to respond, since the task requires me to handle any follow-up requests from them.\nStill no responses. Let me wait once more to be thorough, since the task requires handling any follow-up from them.\nNo responses have come in from Aurélie or Vasco after waiting a total of 10 minutes. Since no additional removals or \"add back\" requests were made, the conditional email to the photoshoot assistant is not triggered (that only applies if I had to remove *more* properties).\n\nLet me confirm the message was delivered by checking the group conversation, then report back to you.\nThe message is confirmed delivered in the group chat. Here's a summary of what I've completed:\n\n**✅ Task complete:**\n\n1. **Removed saved properties with zip codes starting with \"1\"** — In Sweden, only Stockholm uses postal codes beginning with 1 (10x–19x). I searched all cities and confirmed the only *saved* Stockholm apartments were:\n   - **Stockholm Haven** (118 26)\n   - **Stockholm Serenity** (114 39)\n   \n   Both have been removed from your saved list. All remaining saved properties are in Göteborg, Malmö, Uppsala, Lund, Helsingborg, and Jönköping (zip codes not starting with 1), so they were correctly left untouched.\n\n2. **Created a group chat** with Aurélie Dumont (+33 6 78 45 23 10) and Vasco Sousa (+351 912 344 678) via Messages (conversation: \"Stockholm property removals\").\n\n3. **Sent the notification message** letting them know the two properties were removed and inviting them to request further removals or to add them back. The message is confirmed delivered.\n\n4. **Monitored for responses** — I waited ~10 minutes for Aurélie or Vasco to reply. Neither responded, so there were no additional removal or \"add back\" requests to handle.\n\n5. **Conditional email** — Since no further properties needed removing, the email to the photoshoot assistant is **not** triggered (that step only applies if I had to remove more properties).\n\n**The message has been sent** — let me know if you'd like me to keep monitoring the chat for their replies, or if you want me to take any further action.\nI've delivered the final answer to the user. The task is complete:\n\n- ✅ Removed the two saved Stockholm properties with zip codes starting with \"1\" (Stockholm Haven, 118 26 and Stockholm Serenity, 114 39)\n- ✅ Created the group chat with Aurélie Dumont and Vasco Sousa via Messages\n- ✅ Sent the notification message (confirmed delivered)\n- ✅ Monitored for ~10 minutes — no responses, so no further removals or \"add back\" actions were needed\n- ✅ The conditional email to the photoshoot assistant was correctly not triggered (no additional properties were removed)\nNo new message arrived during the wait. The task remains fully complete — there are no further actions to take. Let me confirm this to you.\nNo new follow-up message arrived during the wait, and the task is fully complete. I've confirmed the status to you. Everything requested has been handled:\n\n- ✅ Removed the two saved Stockholm properties with zip codes starting with \"1\"\n- ✅ Created the group chat with Aurélie Dumont and Vasco Sousa via Messages\n- ✅ Sent the notification (confirmed delivered)\n- ✅ Monitored for responses — none received, so no further removals/add-backs and no conditional email needed\n\nIf a follow-up does come in later, I'll be ready to handle it.", "expected": [{"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", "event_time": 1728975601.0, "event_id": "OracleEvent-AGENT-68137eab-a1e0-4a5b-abc7-5b3214cffa5b", "dependencies": ["Event-USER-73ceb041-6976-4019-92bb-2b1d2565b3b5"], "event_relative_time": 1.0, "action": {"action_id": "", "app": "RentAFlat", "function": "remove_saved_apartment", "operation_type": null, "args": [{"name": "apartment_id", "value": "6a572b8b24f445cd851709f559a0f8d6", "value_type": "str"}]}, "metadata": null}, {"class_name": "OracleEvent", "event_type": "AGENT", 